window.DND = window.DND || {};
DND.featureText = {"artificer":{"Magical Tinkering":"Using thieves' tools or an artisan's tool, you spend an action touching a Tiny nonmagical object to give it one lasting effect: dim light, a short recorded message, a constant smell or sound, or a static image or text. You can maintain a number of enchanted objects equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum one), and creating one beyond that limit ends the oldest.","Spellcasting":"Your artificer spells channel through tools, so you need thieves' tools or an artisan's tool you're proficient with in hand for any spell with a material component. You know two cantrips at 1st level, rising to three at 10th and four at 14th, and can swap one when you gain a level. Spell slots follow the class table and return on a long rest. You prepare a number of spells equal to your Intelligence modifier plus half your level (minimum one), changeable after a long rest with at least a minute of tinkering per spell level. Your spell save DC is 8 plus proficiency plus Intelligence, and your spell attack bonus is proficiency plus Intelligence. You can also cast prepared ritual spells as rituals.","Infuse Item":"Starting at 2nd level, after each long rest you can touch nonmagical objects and imbue them with artificer infusions, turning them into magic items. You know four infusions at 2nd level, rising to twelve by 18th, and can swap one each time you gain a level. You can maintain infusions in two objects at first, growing to six at 18th level, with the oldest infusion ending if you exceed the limit. An infused item can be attuned immediately, and the infusion lasts until you die, after which it fades after days equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum one day). Infused items can also serve as your spellcasting focus.","The Right Tool for the Job":"At 3rd level, while holding thieves' tools or an artisan's tool, you can conjure one nonmagical set of artisan's tools in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you. Creating the set takes one hour of uninterrupted work, which can overlap with a short or long rest. The conjured tools vanish when you use this feature again.","Tool Expertise":"At 6th level, your proficiency bonus doubles for any ability check that uses a tool you're proficient with. This applies only to checks where your tool proficiency is already part of the roll.","Flash of Genius":"At 7th level, you can use your reaction when you or a creature you can see within 30 feet makes an ability check or saving throw to add your Intelligence modifier to the roll. You can use this a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum once) and regain all uses on a long rest.","Magic Item Adept":"At 10th level, you can attune to up to four magic items at once. When crafting a common or uncommon magic item, you need only a quarter of the usual time and half the usual gold. These benefits represent a deeper mastery of magic items that does not expand further at higher levels.","Spell-Storing Item":"At 11th level, after a long rest you can store a 1st- or 2nd-level artificer spell that takes one action to cast into a simple or martial weapon or a spellcasting focus item, without needing to prepare it. Any creature holding the item can use an action to cast the stored spell using your spellcasting ability. The stored spell remains until it has been used a number of times equal to twice your Intelligence modifier (minimum two) or you store a new spell.","Magic Item Savant":"At 14th level, you can attune to up to five magic items at once. You also ignore class, race, spell, and level requirements when attuning to or using magic items. Together these make you far more flexible with magical gear than other characters.","Magic Item Master":"Starting at 18th level, you can attune to up to six magic items at once. This is a further increase to your attunement capacity from earlier levels. No other changes come with it.","Soul of Artifice":"At 20th level, you gain a bonus to all saving throws equal to the number of magic items you're attuned to. If you're reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can use your reaction to end one of your infusions and drop to 1 hit point instead."},
"barbarian":{"Rage":"As a bonus action on your turn, you can enter a fury that lasts up to a minute. While raging and not in heavy armor, you gain advantage on Strength checks and saves, extra damage on Strength melee attacks, and resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage. You can rage 2 times per long rest at 1st level, rising to 6 at 17th and unlimited at 20th, while the bonus damage grows from +2 to +4. Spellcasting and concentration are blocked while raging.","Unarmored Defense":"When you wear no armor, your armor class equals 10 plus your Dexterity and Constitution modifiers. A shield still counts toward this formula.","Reckless Attack":"Starting at 2nd level, you can choose to attack recklessly with your first attack on a turn. This gives you advantage on Strength melee attacks that turn, but enemies get advantage on attacks against you until your next turn.","Danger Sense":"At 2nd level, you gain advantage on Dexterity saving throws against effects you can see, such as traps and visible spells. You lose this edge if you are blinded, deafened, or incapacitated.","Primal Knowledge (Optional)":"At 3rd level and again at 10th, you gain proficiency in one skill of your choice from the barbarian's starting skill list. This adds versatility outside of combat.","Extra Attack":"Beginning at 5th level, when you take the Attack action on your turn, you can make two attacks instead of one.","Fast Movement":"Starting at 5th level, your walking speed increases by 10 feet while you are not wearing heavy armor. It applies whenever you are not in heavy armor.","Feral Instinct":"By 7th level, you have advantage on initiative rolls. If you are surprised at the start of combat and not incapacitated, you can still act normally on your first turn, but only if you enter your rage before doing anything else. These are passive benefits with no per-rest limit.","Instinctive Pounce (Optional)":"At 7th level, when you use your bonus action to enter your rage, you can also move up to half your speed. This option pairs your movement with your rage activation.","Brutal Critical":"Beginning at 9th level, when you score a critical hit with a melee attack, you roll one additional weapon damage die for the extra damage. This increases to two extra dice at 13th level and three extra dice at 17th level.","Relentless Rage":"Starting at 11th level, if you drop to 0 hit points while raging and don't die outright, you can make a DC 10 Constitution saving throw to drop to 1 hit point instead. Each later use raises the DC by 5. A short or long rest resets the DC to 10.","Persistent Rage":"Beginning at 15th level, your rage ends early only if you fall unconscious or choose to end it. The usual conditions for an early end no longer apply.","Indomitable Might":"Beginning at 18th level, if your total on a Strength check is lower than your Strength score, you can use your Strength score in place of the total.","Primal Champion":"At 20th level, your Strength and Constitution scores each increase by 4. The maximum for both scores rises to 24. This capstone also comes with unlimited rages from the class table."},
"bard":{"Spellcasting":"Bards cast spells using Charisma, drawing from the bard spell list. You start with two cantrips and four 1st-level spells, plus spell slots that refresh after a long rest; your known cantrips, spells, and slot levels grow as you advance, reaching 9th-level slots at 17th level. Whenever you gain a level, you may swap one known spell for another you can cast. Your spell save DC is 8 plus proficiency bonus plus Charisma modifier, and a musical instrument serves as your spellcasting focus.","Bardic Inspiration":"As a bonus action, you give one creature within 60 feet that can hear you a d6 die it can add to an ability check, attack roll, or saving throw within 10 minutes. You can grant it a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum once), and uses return after a long rest. The die grows to a d8 at 5th level, a d10 at 10th level, and a d12 at 15th level.","Jack of All Trades":"Starting at 2nd level, you add half your proficiency bonus, rounded down, to any ability check that doesn't already include your proficiency bonus.","Song of Rest":"Starting at 2nd level, when you or allies who can hear your performance spend Hit Dice during a short rest to recover hit points, each of them regains an extra 1d6 hit points. This bonus die improves to a d8 at 9th level, a d10 at 13th level, and a d12 at 17th level.","Magical Inspiration (Optional)":"At 2nd level, if a creature holding your Bardic Inspiration die casts a spell that heals or deals damage, it can roll that die and add the result to the healing or damage for one affected target, which consumes the die.","Expertise":"At 3rd level, choose two of your skill proficiencies, and your proficiency bonus is doubled for ability checks using them. At 10th level, you choose two more skill proficiencies to receive this doubling.","Bardic Versatility (Optional)":"Whenever you gain an Ability Score Improvement feature, you may swap one skill from your Expertise for another proficient skill that isn't already doubled, or replace one known bard cantrip with another from the bard list.","Font of Inspiration":"Starting at 5th level, your expended Bardic Inspiration uses return when you finish either a short rest or a long rest, rather than only after a long rest.","Countercharm":"At 6th level, you can use an action to begin a performance that lasts until the end of your next turn. While it lasts, you and friendly creatures within 30 feet who can hear you have advantage on saving throws against being frightened or charmed. The performance ends early if you are incapacitated or silenced, or if you choose to end it.","Magical Secrets":"By 10th level, you choose two spells from any class, which must be cantrips or spells you can cast, and they count as bard spells for you. You learn two more spells from any class at 14th level and two more at 18th level.","Superior Inspiration":"At 20th level, if you roll initiative and have no Bardic Inspiration uses left, you regain one use."},
"blood-hunter":{"Hunter's Bane":"You gain advantage on Wisdom (Survival) checks to track fey, fiends, and undead, and on Intelligence checks to recall lore about them. Your hemocraft features that force saves use a DC of 8 + proficiency bonus + your chosen Intelligence or Wisdom modifier.","Blood Maledict":"You know one blood curse and learn more at 6th, 10th, 14th, and 18th level, with the option to swap one known curse whenever you gain a new one. When you invoke a curse, you can take necrotic damage equal to one hemocraft die to amplify it and add its extra effect, though this damage can't be reduced. You can use the feature once per rest, twice from 6th level, three times from 13th level, and four times from 17th level.","Fighting Style":"At 2nd level you choose a combat specialty: Archery gives +2 to ranged attack rolls, Dueling gives +2 to damage with a one-handed melee weapon when no other weapon is held, Great Weapon Fighting lets you reroll 1s and 2s on damage dice with two-handed or versatile melee weapons, and Two-Weapon Fighting adds your ability modifier to off-hand damage. You can only take each style once.","Crimson Rite":"As a bonus action you activate a known rite on a weapon you hold, and it lasts until you finish a short or long rest, costing necrotic damage equal to one hemocraft die. While active, your attacks with that weapon count as magical and add extra damage of a die matching the rite's type, and a weapon can carry only one rite at a time. You start with one rite (Flame, Frozen, Storm, Dead, Oracle, or Roar), learn another at 7th level, and a third at 14th level, with the last three rites requiring 14th level.","Extra Attack":"Starting at 5th level, when you take the Attack action on your turn you can make two attacks instead of one.","Brand of Castigation":"At 6th level, when you damage a creature with a weapon that has an active crimson rite, you can brand it at no action cost. You always know the branded creature's direction while on the same plane, and whenever it damages you or a creature within 5 feet of you, it takes psychic damage equal to your Hemocraft modifier (minimum 1). The brand lasts until you dismiss it or apply a new one, and you can use this feature once per rest.","Grim Psychometry":"At 9th level you gain advantage on Intelligence (History) checks about the dark or tragic past of an object you touch or your current location. At the DM's discretion, a high enough roll may show you brief visions of that past.","Dark Augmentation":"Starting at 10th level, your speed increases by 5 feet, and you gain a bonus to Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution saving throws equal to your Hemocraft modifier (minimum +1). These benefits are permanent.","Brand of Tethering":"Starting at 13th level, the psychic damage from your Brand of Castigation rises to twice your Hemocraft modifier (minimum 2). A branded creature cannot take the Dash action, and if it tries to teleport or leave its plane, it takes 4d6 psychic damage and must succeed on a Wisdom save or the attempt fails.","Hardened Soul":"At 14th level you gain advantage on saving throws against being charmed and frightened.","Sanguine Mastery":"At 20th level, once per turn you can reroll a hemocraft die when a blood hunter feature calls for one and use either result. Additionally, when you score a critical hit with a weapon that has an active crimson rite, you regain one expended use of Blood Maledict."},
"cleric":{"Spellcasting":"Clerics cast spells from the cleric list using Wisdom. Each long rest you prepare a number of spells equal to your Wisdom modifier plus cleric level (minimum one), limited to spell levels you have slots for. Slots grow from two 1st-level slots to nine-level slots at 17th, and cantrips known rise from three to five. You can also cast prepared ritual spells and use a holy symbol as your focus.","Channel Divinity":"Starting at 2nd level, you draw divine energy to fuel magical effects, beginning with Turn Undead and one domain option. Each use spends your one charge until you finish a short or long rest. Effects requiring saves use your cleric spell save DC. At 6th level you get two charges between rests, and at 18th level three.","Channel Divinity: Turn Undead":"As an action, you show your holy symbol and pray against the undead. Each undead within 30 feet that can see or hear you must make a Wisdom save or be turned for one minute or until it takes damage. Turned undead must flee from you, can't take reactions, and may only Dash or escape effects; if cornered, they Dodge.","Harness Divine Power (Optional)":"At 2nd level, you can spend a Channel Divinity use as a bonus action to regain one expended spell slot, up to a level equal to half your proficiency bonus, rounded up. You can use this once at 2nd level, twice at 6th, and three times at 18th. All uses return after a long rest.","Cantrip Versatility (Optional)":"Whenever you gain an Ability Score Improvement, you may swap one cleric cantrip you know for a different cleric cantrip. This lets you adjust your cantrip selection as your character develops. It becomes available at the same levels that grant Ability Score Improvements.","Destroy Undead":"Starting at 5th level, when an undead fails its save against Turn Undead, it is destroyed instantly if its challenge rating is at or below a threshold. That threshold rises from 1/2 at 5th level to 1 at 8th, 2 at 11th, 3 at 14th, and 4 at 17th.","Blessed Strikes (Optional)":"At 8th level, when you damage a creature with a cantrip or weapon attack, you can also deal 1d8 radiant damage to that creature. You can use this once per turn, and must wait until the start of your next turn to use it again. This option replaces the Divine Strike or Potent Spellcasting feature.","Divine Intervention":"From 10th level, you can use your action to ask your deity for help and roll percentile dice. If the roll is equal to or lower than your cleric level, the DM decides how your deity intervenes. A successful intervention locks the feature for 7 days, while a failure lets you try again after a long rest. At 20th level, your request always succeeds."},
"druid":{"Druidic":"You know the secret druidic language and can use it to hide messages that other druids spot automatically. Anyone else needs a DC 15 Wisdom (Perception) check to notice a hidden message, but they cannot decipher it without magic.","Spellcasting":"Your druid spells use Wisdom, and you start with two cantrips and two 1st-level slots, gaining more cantrips and slots as you level up. Each day you prepare a list of spells equal to your Wisdom modifier plus your druid level, and you can change that list after a long rest. You regain spell slots on a long rest, and you can cast prepared ritual spells without using a slot. A druidic focus works as your spellcasting focus.","Wild Shape":"Starting at 2nd level, you can use an action to transform into a beast you have seen before, with the maximum challenge rating rising from 1/4 to 1/2 at 4th level and to 1 at 8th level. You can use this twice and regain uses on a short or long rest. You can stay transformed for half your druid level in hours, and you can't cast spells while in beast form. When the beast form drops to 0 hit points, excess damage carries over to your normal form.","Wild Companion (Optional)":"At 2nd level, you can spend a Wild Shape use as an action to cast Find Familiar without needing material components. The summoned creature is a fey rather than a beast, and it disappears after half your druid level in hours. This option lets you call a spirit companion in place of a standard familiar.","Cantrip Versatility (Optional)":"Whenever you gain an Ability Score Improvement from this class, you can swap one druid cantrip you know for a different cantrip from the druid spell list. This lets you adjust your known cantrips as your magic develops. You can use it at 4th, 8th, 12th, 16th, and 19th level.","Timeless Body":"Starting at 18th level, your body ages much more slowly due to primal magic. For every 10 years that pass, you only age 1 year. This allows you to remain vigorous for far longer than normal.","Beast Spells":"Beginning at 18th level, you can cast many druid spells while in a beast shape from Wild Shape. You can perform the somatic and verbal parts of a spell in beast form, but you still cannot supply material components. This expands your options when transformed.","Archdruid":"At 20th level, you can use Wild Shape an unlimited number of times. You can also ignore the verbal and somatic components of your druid spells, along with material components that have no cost and aren't consumed. This applies in both your normal form and your beast form."},
"fighter":{"Fighting Style":"You pick a specialty combat technique from a list, such as a bonus to ranged attacks, extra AC while wearing armor, or added damage when wielding one melee weapon. You can't take the same style twice. Martial Versatility lets you swap it at later ability score levels.","Second Wind":"As a bonus action on your turn, you can heal yourself for 1d10 plus your fighter level. You can use it once, and you must finish a short or long rest before using it again.","Action Surge":"Starting at 2nd level, you can take one additional action on your turn. You can use it once between rests, and at 17th level you can use it twice between rests, though not both times on the same turn.","Martial Versatility (Optional)":"Whenever you gain an ability score improvement level, you can change your martial focus. You can replace one fighting style you know with another fighter style. If you know Battle Master maneuvers, you can also swap one maneuver for a different one.","Extra Attack":"Starting at 5th level, when you take the Attack action on your turn, you can make two attacks instead of one. This rises to three attacks at 11th level and four attacks at 20th level.","Indomitable":"Starting at 9th level, when you fail a saving throw you can reroll it and must keep the new result. You can use this once per long rest, which rises to twice at 13th level and three times at 17th level."},
"monk":{"Unarmored Defense":"While you wear no armor and hold no shield, your Armor Class becomes 10 plus your Dexterity and Wisdom modifiers. This works as a constant defense that needs no ki or rest to use.","Martial Arts":"Your unarmed strikes and monk weapons can use Dexterity for attack and damage rolls, and they deal a Martial Arts die instead of their normal damage, starting at d4. That die grows to d6 at 5th level, d8 at 11th, and d10 at 17th. When you take the Attack action with one of these, you can also make one unarmed strike as a bonus action once per turn.","Ki":"Starting at 2nd level, you have a pool of ki points equal to your monk level's table value, spent on Flurry of Blows, Patient Defense, and Step of the Wind. Spent points come back only after a short or long rest, and you must meditate for at least 30 minutes during that rest. Ki save DCs equal 8 plus your proficiency bonus and Wisdom modifier, and your pool grows with each level.","Unarmored Movement":"From 2nd level, your walking speed rises while you wear no armor and hold no shield. The bonus grows to +15, +20, +25, and +30 feet at 6th, 10th, 14th, and 18th level. At 9th level, you can move up vertical surfaces and across liquids during your turn without falling.","Dedicated Weapon (Optional)":"At 2nd level, you can focus ki into one simple or martial weapon you are proficient with, after finishing a short or long rest. That weapon then counts as a monk weapon until you use this feature again. The weapon cannot have the heavy or special property.","Deflect Missiles":"Starting at 3rd level, you can use your reaction when a ranged weapon attack hits you to reduce the damage by 1d10 plus your Dexterity modifier and monk level. If that brings the damage to zero, you can catch a small missile with a free hand. You can then spend 1 ki point to throw it back as a proficient monk weapon attack with a 20/60 range, using the same reaction.","Ki-Fueled Attack (Optional)":"From 3rd level, whenever you spend at least 1 ki point as part of your action on your turn, you can make one unarmed strike or monk weapon attack as a bonus action before that turn ends. This lets you add an extra attack once per turn while using ki for other features.","Slow Fall":"Starting at 4th level, you can use your reaction when you fall to reduce the falling damage you take by five times your monk level. At higher monk levels, this reduction grows, making long drops much less dangerous.","Quickened Healing (Optional)":"At 4th level, you can take an action and spend 2 ki points to roll a Martial Arts die and regain hit points equal to the roll plus your proficiency bonus. Because the die improves with your monk level, this healing scales as you advance.","Extra Attack":"Beginning at 5th level, you can make two attacks instead of one whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. This substantially boosts your damage output each turn without spending any ki.","Stunning Strike":"Starting at 5th level, after you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can spend 1 ki point to attempt to stun it. The target must make a Constitution saving throw, and on a failure it is stunned until the end of your next turn. You can use it as often as your ki allows.","Focused Aim (Optional)":"At 5th level, when you miss with an attack roll, you can spend 1 to 3 ki points to add 2 to your roll for each point spent. This can convert a near miss into a hit. The number of points spent is your choice each time.","Ki-Empowered Strikes":"Starting at 6th level, your unarmed strikes count as magical attacks. This lets them overcome resistances and immunities that normally block nonmagical physical damage.","Evasion":"At 7th level, you can avoid much of the damage from area effects that normally allow a Dexterity saving throw for half damage. A successful save means you take no damage, and a failed save means you take only half damage.","Stillness of Mind":"Starting at 7th level, you can use your action to end one effect on yourself that has charmed or frightened you. This is a reliable way to recover from control effects in combat.","Purity of Body":"At 10th level, your control of ki makes you immune to disease and poison. This protects you from many dangerous hazards and afflictions throughout your adventures.","Tongue of the Sun and Moon":"Starting at 13th level, you understand all spoken languages. Any creature that can understand a language can also understand what you say, regardless of the language you use.","Diamond Soul":"Beginning at 14th level, you gain proficiency in all saving throws. Additionally, when you fail a saving throw, you can spend 1 ki point to reroll it and must use the new result.","Timeless Body":"At 15th level, ki sustains your body so that you no longer suffer the frailty of old age, and you cannot be magically aged. You can still die of old age, and you no longer need food or water to survive.","Empty Body":"Beginning at 18th level, you can spend 4 ki points as an action to become invisible for 1 minute and gain resistance to all damage except force damage. You can also spend 8 ki points to cast astral projection without material components, though you cannot bring other creatures along.","Perfect Self":"At 20th level, if you roll initiative and have no ki points remaining, you regain 4 ki points. This gives you a burst of energy to start a fight when you have run dry."},
"paladin":{"Divine Sense":"As an action you can sense celestials, fiends, and undead within 60 feet that lack total cover, learning their type but not identity, and also detect consecrated or desecrated places and objects in that radius. The sense lasts until the end of your next turn. You can use it 1 plus your Charisma modifier times per long rest.","Lay on Hands":"You have a healing pool equal to five times your paladin level that refills on a long rest. As an action you can touch a creature and draw from the pool to restore hit points, up to what remains. Alternatively, spending 5 pool points cures one disease or neutralizes one poison, and this works on undead and constructs no differently than other creatures, meaning it has no effect on them.","Fighting Style":"At 2nd level you choose a combat specialty you can never take again. Options include learning two cleric cantrips with Charisma as the casting ability, blindsight out to 10 feet, bonus AC while in armor, extra damage with a one-handed melee weapon, rerolling low damage dice with two-handed weapons, and several Unearthed Arcana styles such as interception, protection, and unarmed fighting. You can swap one known style when you gain an Ability Score Improvement.","Spellcasting":"Starting at 2nd level you cast paladin spells using Charisma, with slots set by the paladin table and recovered on a long rest. Each day you prepare a number of paladin spells equal to your Charisma modifier plus half your paladin level, rounded down, with a minimum of one. Your spell save DC and attack bonus are derived from Charisma and proficiency, and a holy symbol serves as your focus.","Divine Smite":"Beginning at 2nd level, when a melee weapon attack hits, you can spend a spell slot to add radiant damage on top of the weapon damage. A 1st-level slot deals 2d8, and each higher slot adds 1d8, capping at 5d8. Against undead or fiends the extra damage rises by 1d8, up to a maximum of 6d8.","Divine Health":"Starting at 3rd level, the divine power within you grants immunity to disease.","Harness Divine Power (Optional)":"Starting at 3rd level, you can spend a Channel Divinity use as a bonus action to touch your holy symbol and recover one expended spell slot. The recovered slot can be no higher than half your proficiency bonus, rounded up. You can use this once per long rest at 3rd level, twice at 7th, and three times at 15th.","Martial Versatility (Optional)":"Whenever you gain an Ability Score Improvement, you may replace one fighting style you already know with another paladin fighting style. It reflects a change in your combat focus over time. This is an optional rule that lets you adapt your martial training as you advance.","Extra Attack":"Starting at 5th level, when you take the Attack action on your turn you can make two attacks instead of one.","Aura of Protection":"From 6th level, you and friendly creatures within 10 feet add your Charisma modifier (minimum +1) to saving throws while you are conscious. The range expands to 30 feet at 18th level.","Aura of Courage":"Starting at 10th level, you and allies within 10 feet cannot be frightened while you remain conscious. At 18th level the aura's range grows to 30 feet.","Improved Divine Smite":"By 11th level, every melee weapon hit you land carries divine power, dealing an extra 1d8 radiant damage to the target. This effect is always on and does not use a spell slot.","Cleansing Touch":"Starting at 14th level, you can use your action to end one spell affecting yourself or a willing creature you touch. You can do this a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier, with a minimum of once. Uses return on a long rest."},
"ranger":{"Favored Enemy":"At 1st level, you pick a creature type, or two humanoid races, as your favored enemies. You get advantage on Wisdom (Survival) checks to track them and Intelligence checks to recall lore about them. You also learn a language they speak, and you choose another favored enemy at 6th and 14th level.","Natural Explorer":"At 1st level, you choose one favored terrain type, which doubles your proficiency bonus on Intelligence or Wisdom checks there for skills you already know. After an hour or more of travel in that terrain, difficult ground doesn't slow your group, you can't get lost without magic, and you stay alert to danger. You also move stealthily alone, find twice the food when foraging, and learn the number, size, and age of creatures you track. You gain more terrain types at 6th and 10th level.","Deft Explorer (Optional)":"This replaces Natural Explorer. At 1st level, you gain Canny, which doubles your proficiency bonus for one chosen skill, and you learn two extra languages. At 6th level, your walking speed rises by 5 and you gain climbing and swimming speeds equal to it. At 10th level, you can use an action to gain temporary hit points a number of times per long rest equal to your proficiency bonus, and finishing a short rest reduces exhaustion by one.","Favored Foe (Optional)":"This replaces Favored Enemy and works with Foe Slayer. When you hit a creature, you can mark it for up to 1 minute, requiring concentration, and the first time each turn you damage it you add 1d4 extra damage, including when you mark it. You can mark a number of targets equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest, and the bonus die grows to 1d6 at 6th level and 1d8 at 14th.","Fighting Style":"At 2nd level, you choose a combat specialty that you can't pick again later. Options include archery, blind fighting, defense, dueling, two-weapon fighting, and thrown weapon fighting, plus druidic warrior, which grants two druid cantrips using Wisdom. Several additional options come from Unearthed Arcana. Martial Versatility lets you swap this choice later.","Spellcasting":"From 2nd level, you cast ranger spells using Wisdom, drawing on nature magic much like a druid. Your spell slots and number of known spells rise with level, and you regain expended slots on a long rest. Your spell save DC is 8 plus proficiency bonus plus Wisdom modifier, and your spell attack bonus is proficiency bonus plus Wisdom modifier. You can also use a druidic focus, such as a sprig of holly or a carved staff, as your spellcasting focus.","Spellcasting Focus (Optional)":"From 2nd level, you cast ranger spells using Wisdom, drawing on nature magic much like a druid. Your spell slots and number of known spells rise with level, and you regain expended slots on a long rest. Your spell save DC is 8 plus proficiency bonus plus Wisdom modifier, and your spell attack bonus is proficiency bonus plus Wisdom modifier. You can also use a druidic focus, such as a sprig of holly or a carved staff, as your spellcasting focus.","Primeval Awareness":"Starting at 3rd level, you can use your action and expend a ranger spell slot to sense certain creatures nearby, lasting 1 minute per slot level. The creatures include aberrations, celestials, dragons, elementals, fey, fiends, and undead, detected within 1 mile, or 6 miles in your favored terrain. You learn only whether they are present, not where they are or how many.","Primal Awareness (Optional)":"This replaces Primeval Awareness. At 3rd, 5th, 9th, 13th, and 17th level you learn a specific nature spell, such as Speak with Animals or Commune with Nature, which doesn't count against your known spells. You can cast each of these once without a spell slot, and you regain that use on a long rest.","Martial Versatility (Optional)":"Whenever you gain a level that grants an Ability Score Improvement, you can replace one fighting style you know with a different ranger fighting style. This lets you refocus your combat training as your character develops. It doesn't add extra uses, just flexibility at those levels.","Extra Attack":"Starting at 5th level, when you take the Attack action on your turn, you can attack twice instead of once.","Land's Stride":"From 8th level, moving through nonmagical difficult terrain costs no extra movement. You can also pass through nonmagical thorny or spiny plants without being slowed or hurt by them. You have advantage on saves against magical plants that are created or shaped to impede movement, such as those from Entangle.","Hide in Plain Sight":"Starting at 10th level, you can spend 1 minute camouflaging yourself with natural materials like mud, dirt, or plants. While you stay still and take no actions, pressing against a large solid surface gives you a +10 bonus to Dexterity (Stealth) checks. Moving or acting ends the bonus, and you must camouflage yourself again to regain it.","Nature's Veil (Optional)":"This replaces Hide in Plain Sight. As a bonus action, you can turn invisible, along with your worn and carried equipment, until the start of your next turn. You can use this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all uses on a long rest.","Vanish":"Starting at 14th level, you can take the Hide action as a bonus action on your turn. You also can't be tracked by nonmagical means unless you choose to leave a trail behind.","Feral Senses":"At 18th level, you gain heightened senses for fighting unseen foes. Attacking a creature you can't see doesn't give you disadvantage on the attack roll. You also sense invisible creatures within 30 feet that aren't hiding from you, as long as you aren't blinded or deafened.","Foe Slayer":"At 20th level, you can add your Wisdom modifier to the attack roll or damage roll of one attack per turn against a favored enemy. You decide whether to add it before or after the roll, but always before the roll's effects are applied."},
"rogue":{"Expertise":"At 1st level you pick two skills you're proficient in, or one skill plus thieves' tools, and double your proficiency bonus on checks using them. At 6th level you choose two more proficiencies to get the same doubling.","Sneak Attack":"Once per turn, a finesse or ranged weapon hit deals extra damage if you have advantage on the attack, or if an ally-free foe of the target stands within 5 feet of it and you lack disadvantage. The bonus starts at 1d6 and grows with rogue level, reaching 10d6 at 19th level.","Thieves' Cant":"You know a coded language of slang and gestures that lets you hide messages inside normal conversation, though only other cant speakers can read them. Conveying a message takes four times as long as saying it plainly. You also know a set of symbols that signal simple warnings, such as danger, loot, or a safe house.","Cunning Action":"From 2nd level, you can take a bonus action on each of your turns in combat to Dash, Disengage, or Hide. This keeps you mobile and evasive without using your main action.","Steady Aim (Optional)":"Starting at 3rd level, you can spend a bonus action to gain advantage on your next attack roll this turn, but only if you haven't moved yet this turn. Afterward your speed drops to 0 until the turn ends.","Uncanny Dodge":"Beginning at 5th level, when a visible attacker hits you, you can use your reaction to halve that attack's damage. You can use it as often as you can spend reactions, so it's usable once per round.","Evasion":"From 7th level, you avoid much of the damage from area effects that allow a Dexterity saving throw for half damage. A successful save means no damage, and a failed save means only half damage.","Reliable Talent":"At 11th level, your skill checks become much more consistent. When you make an ability check that adds your proficiency bonus, any d20 roll of 9 or lower counts as a 10.","Blindsense":"Starting at 14th level, as long as you can hear, you sense hidden or invisible creatures within 10 feet of you. You know where they are, though this doesn't let you see them clearly.","Slippery Mind":"At 15th level, your mental resilience grows, and you gain proficiency in Wisdom saving throws. This makes it harder for enemies to control or confuse you.","Elusive":"From 18th level, attackers rarely get an edge on you. While you aren't incapacitated, no attack roll against you can have advantage.","Stroke of Luck":"At 20th level, you can turn a missed attack against a target within range into a hit, or treat a failed ability check's d20 roll as a 20. Once you use it, you must finish a short or long rest before using it again."},
"sorcerer":{"Spellcasting":"You cast sorcerer spells using Charisma, drawing on an innate magical source. At 1st level you know four cantrips and two 1st-level spells, and you regain expended spell slots on a long rest. Your cantrips, spells known, and slots grow with level, reaching 9th-level slots at 17th level.","Font of Magic":"At 2nd level you gain sorcery points, a pool of magical energy equal to your level that refills on a long rest. You can spend them to create spell slots of up to 5th level, or convert unspent spell slots back into points as a bonus action. Created slots vanish after a long rest, and your point maximum rises with level.","Metamagic":"At 3rd level you learn two metamagic options that twist how your spells work, spending sorcery points to alter each casting. You can apply only one option per spell unless an option says otherwise. You gain a third option at 10th level and a fourth at 17th level.","Sorcerous Versatility (Optional)":"At each level that grants an Ability Score Improvement, you can swap out one chosen metamagic option for another you qualify for, or replace a sorcerer cantrip with a different one from the sorcerer list. This lets you adapt your build as your magic develops. It is an optional rule your group may choose to use.","Magical Guidance (Optional)":"Starting at 5th level, when you fail an ability check, you can spend 1 sorcery point to reroll the d20 and must use the new result. This can turn a failure into a success. It is an optional rule your group may choose to use.","Sorcerous Restoration":"At 20th level, you recover 4 expended sorcery points whenever you finish a short rest. This lets you refuel your magic far more often than only on a long rest. It makes your sorcery point pool much more sustainable during the day."},
"warlock":{"Pact Magic":"Your arcane study and your patron's gifts let you cast warlock spells. You know a set number of cantrips and spells, and those counts rise with your level. All your spell slots share one level, which increases over time, and you regain them on any short or long rest. Charisma is your spellcasting ability for DCs and attack bonuses.","Eldritch Invocations":"At 2nd level you gain two invocations, minor magical abilities drawn from forbidden lore. The number you know grows at certain levels, reaching eight by 18th level. Whenever you gain a warlock level, you may swap one known invocation for another you qualify for.","Pact Boon":"At 3rd level your patron grants one of four gifts: a pact weapon, a familiar, a grimoire of at-will cantrips, or an amulet that adds a d4 to failed ability checks a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest. The Pact of the Star Chain, an Unearthed Arcana option, requires the Seeker patron and grants augury as a ritual plus one advantage on an Intelligence check per rest. Lost items can be replaced through a one-hour ceremony.","Eldritch Versatility (Optional)":"Each time you gain an Ability Score Improvement level, you may revise an earlier choice in place of taking the score increase. You can swap one warlock cantrip, change your Pact Boon option, or, at 12th level or higher, exchange a Mystic Arcanum spell for another warlock spell of the same level. If a swap makes an invocation ineligible, you must replace that invocation as well.","Mystic Arcanum":"At 11th level your patron grants a 6th-level warlock spell you can cast once without expending a slot. You gain another arcanum at 13th level (7th-level spell), 15th level (8th-level spell), and 17th level (9th-level spell). Each arcanum refreshes after a long rest.","Eldritch Master":"At 20th level you can spend one minute pleading with your patron to restore all expended Pact Magic spell slots. Once you use this, you must finish a long rest before doing so again."},
"wizard":{"Spellcasting":"Wizards cast spells from a spellbook, starting with three cantrips and six 1st-level spells, and gain two new spells each time they level up. Intelligence sets your spell save DC and attack bonus, and each long rest you prepare a number of spells equal to your Intelligence modifier plus your wizard level. Spells in your book with the ritual tag can be cast as rituals without being prepared, and your known cantrips grow from three to five as you advance.","Arcane Recovery":"Once per day, after finishing a short rest, you can regain expended spell slots with a combined level up to half your wizard level, rounded up. None of the recovered slots can be 6th level or higher. The recovery limit increases as your wizard level rises.","Cantrip Formulas (Optional)":"Starting at 3rd level, you can record formulas in your spellbook that help you reshape your cantrips. After each long rest, you can consult them to replace one wizard cantrip you know with another from the wizard spell list. The number of swaps stays at one per long rest.","Spell Mastery":"At 18th level, you choose one 1st-level and one 2nd-level wizard spell from your spellbook and can cast each at its lowest level without using a slot, as long as it is prepared. Casting either at a higher level still requires a spell slot. Spending 8 hours of study lets you exchange one or both chosen spells for different spells of the same levels.","Signature Spells":"At 20th level, you select two 3rd-level wizard spells from your spellbook as signature spells. They are always prepared and do not count against your prepared-spell limit. You can cast each one once at 3rd level without a spell slot, and that use recovers on a short or long rest. Casting either at a higher level still requires a spell slot."},
"artificer:alchemist":{"Tool Proficiency":"At 3rd level you become proficient with alchemist's supplies. If you already have that proficiency, you instead gain proficiency with one artisan's tool of your choice.","Experimental Elixir":"Each time you finish a long rest, you brew one elixir in an empty flask you touch, and its random effect (rolled on a d6 table) triggers when a creature drinks it or someone administers it to an incapacitated creature. You can make extra elixirs by spending a spell slot of 1st level or higher for each, using your action and choosing the effect. Carrying alchemist's supplies is required, and an elixir lasts until consumed or until your next long rest. At 6th level you make two elixirs at the end of a long rest, and at 15th level three, each needing its own flask and rolled separately.","Alchemical Savant":"At 5th level, when you cast a spell using alchemist's supplies as your spellcasting focus, you can add a bonus equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1) to one roll of that spell. The roll must either restore hit points or be a damage roll dealing acid, fire, necrotic, or poison damage.","Restorative Reagents":"At 9th level, a creature that drinks one of your experimental elixirs gains temporary hit points equal to 2d6 plus your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1). You can also cast Lesser Restoration without a spell slot or preparing it, using alchemist's supplies as your focus, a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum once) that refresh on a long rest.","Chemical Mastery":"At 15th level you gain resistance to acid and poison damage and become immune to the poisoned condition. Using alchemist's supplies as your focus, you can cast Greater Restoration and Heal without a spell slot, preparation, or material components. Each of those two spells can be cast this way only once until you finish a long rest."},
"artificer:armorer":{"Tools of the Trade":"Choosing this specialization at 3rd level gives you heavy armor training and smith's tools proficiency. If you already know smith's tools, you pick another artisan's tool set to learn instead.","Arcane Armor":"Starting at 3rd level, you can spend an action to turn worn armor into a magical conduit for your artificer spells, provided you hold smith's tools. The armor fuses to your body, cannot be removed against your will, and expands to cover you fully, with the helmet retractable as a bonus action and any lost limbs replaced by working ones. You can still don or doff it as an action, its Strength requirement no longer applies to you, and it stays in effect until you wear different armor or die.","Armor Model":"At 3rd level you configure your Arcane Armor as either a Guardian or an Infiltrator, and the chosen model grants its own features. Its special weapon uses your Intelligence modifier for attack and damage rolls instead of Strength or Dexterity. You may switch models after any short or long rest while holding smith's tools. Guardian gives gauntlets that deal 1d8 thunder damage and impose disadvantage on a struck creature's attacks against anyone but you, plus a bonus action that grants temporary hit points equal to your class level, usable a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest. Infiltrator gives a lightning launcher with 90/300 foot range that deals 1d6 lightning damage, adds one extra 1d6 once per turn on a hit, plus a 5-foot speed boost and advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks.","Extra Attack":"Beginning at 5th level, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn, you can make two attacks instead of one.","Armor Modifications":"At 9th level, your infusions can modify Arcane Armor, which now counts as separate infusable items: the chest piece, boots, helmet, and special weapon. Infusions carry over when you change models, and your maximum number of infused items rises by 2, though those extra items must be part of your Arcane Armor.","Perfected Armor":"At 15th level, each model gains a new benefit. Guardian lets you use a reaction when a visible creature of Huge size or smaller ends its turn within 30 feet, forcing a Strength save against your spell save DC; on a failure you pull it up to 25 feet into an open space, and if it lands within 5 feet you may make a melee weapon attack against it. You can use this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest. Infiltrator makes any creature damaged by your Lightning Launcher glow until the start of your next turn, shedding dim light and giving it disadvantage on attacks against you, while your next attack against it has advantage and deals an extra 1d6 lightning damage on a hit."},
"artificer:artillerist":{"Tool Proficiency":"At 3rd level you become proficient with woodcarver's tools. If you already have that proficiency, you instead gain proficiency with one artisan's tool of your choice.","Eldritch Cannon":"As an action you conjure a Small or Tiny magical cannon on a nearby flat surface, and you can recreate it after a long rest or by spending a spell slot. It has AC 18 and hit points equal to five times your artificer level, dies at 0 HP or after an hour, and can be dismissed early. As a bonus action within 60 feet you activate it: Flamethrower breathes a 15-foot cone for 2d8 fire damage (Dex save, half on success), Force Ballista makes a spell attack for 2d8 force damage at 120 feet and pushes the target 5 feet, and Protector grants temporary HP equal to 1d8 plus your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1) to nearby allies. Legged cannons can also move up to 15 feet as part of that bonus action.","Arcane Firearm":"At 5th level, after a long rest, you can carve sigils with woodcarver's tools into a wand, staff, or rod to make it your arcane firearm, moving the sigils if you later carve a different item. You can use it as a spellcasting focus for artificer spells. When you cast a spell through it, you roll a d8 and add that number to one of the spell's damage rolls.","Explosive Cannon":"Starting at 9th level, your cannons hit harder, adding 1d8 to their damage rolls. As an action within 60 feet, you can detonate a cannon, destroying it and forcing creatures within 20 feet to make a Dexterity save against your spell save DC, taking 3d8 force damage on a failed save or half as much on a success.","Fortified Position":"At 15th level, you and allies gain half cover while within 10 feet of your eldritch cannons. You can maintain two cannons at once, create both with a single action (each still requiring its own spell slot), and activate both with one bonus action. The two cannons can be identical or different, but you cannot have a third while two are active."},
"artificer:battle-smith":{"Battle Ready":"At 3rd level you gain martial weapon proficiency. When you attack with a magic weapon, you can use your Intelligence modifier instead of Strength or Dexterity for both attack and damage rolls.","Steel Defender":"At 3rd level you create a loyal construct companion with AC 15, 40 ft. speed, and HP equal to 2 plus your Intelligence modifier plus 5 per artificer level. It acts right after you on initiative, usually only dodging unless you spend a bonus action to command it, and its Force-Empowered Rend deals 1d8 plus your proficiency bonus in force damage. Its Repair ability works three times per day, restoring 2d8 plus your proficiency bonus HP, and you can revive it within an hour of its death using smith's tools and a 1st-level or higher spell slot. You can replace it with a new one at the end of a long rest.","Extra Attack":"Starting at 5th level, you can make two attacks whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.","Arcane Jolt":"At 9th level, your magic weapon hits and your steel defender's hits can channel arcane energy to either deal an extra 2d6 force damage to the target or restore 2d6 HP to a creature you can see within 30 feet of the target. You can use this a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum once), but only once per turn, and uses refresh on a long rest.","Improved Defender":"At 15th level, the Arcane Jolt bonus damage and healing both increase to 4d6, and your steel defender gains a +2 bonus to AC. Whenever the defender uses Deflect Attack, the attacker also takes force damage equal to 1d4 plus your Intelligence modifier."},
"barbarian:ancestral-guardian":{"Ancestral Protectors":"At 3rd level, spectral warriors manifest whenever you enter a rage. The first creature you hit on your turn while raging is marked by them until the start of your next turn: it has disadvantage on attacks aimed at anyone other than you, and any creature it hits (except you) takes reduced damage from that attack. The mark ends early if your rage does.","Spirit Shield":"Starting at 6th level, while raging, you can spend your reaction to reduce damage taken by another creature you can see within 30 feet of you by 2d6. The reduction increases to 3d6 at 10th level and 4d6 at 14th level.","Consult the Spirits":"At 10th level, you can cast Augury or Clairvoyance using Wisdom without a spell slot or material components. A Clairvoyance cast this way invisibly summons one of your ancestral spirits to the target location instead of creating a sensor. After using either spell this way, you must finish a short or long rest before using it again.","Vengeful Ancestors":"At 14th level, when you use Spirit Shield to reduce an attack's damage, the attacker takes force damage equal to the amount your shield prevented. This retaliation happens each time you use Spirit Shield against an attack."},
"barbarian:battlerager":{"Battlerager Armor":"Starting at 3rd level, your spiked armor becomes a weapon. While raging, you can use a bonus action to strike with the spikes at a foe within 5 feet, using Strength for the attack and damage, for 1d4 piercing on a hit. Grappling with the Attack action also deals 3 piercing damage on a successful grapple.","Reckless Abandon":"From 6th level, each time you use Reckless Attack while raging, you gain temporary hit points equal to your Constitution modifier, with a minimum of 1. Any of those temporary hit points still remaining when the rage ends disappear.","Battlerager Charge":"At 10th level, you can take the Dash action as a bonus action while raging. This lets you move quickly without spending your action on the turn.","Spiked Retribution":"At 14th level, any creature within 5 feet that hits you with a melee attack takes 3 piercing damage in return. This only works while you are raging, are not incapacitated, and are wearing spiked armor."},
"barbarian:beast":{"Form of the Beast":"When you rage from 3rd level on, you sprout a natural weapon of your choice: a bite (1d8 piercing, with a healing trigger once per turn if you're below half HP), claws (1d6 slashing, with an extra claw attack once per turn when using the Attack action), or a reach tail (1d8 piercing that can be used in a reaction to add a d8 to your AC against a nearby attacker). The weapon counts as a simple melee weapon, and you add your Strength modifier to its attack and damage rolls.","Bestial Soul":"Starting at 6th level, your natural weapons count as magical for overcoming resistance and immunity to nonmagical attacks. After each short or long rest, you pick one adaptation that lasts until your next rest: a swimming speed equal to your walking speed with underwater breathing, a climbing speed equal to your walking speed that lets you scale difficult surfaces such as ceilings, or a jump extension based on a Strength (Athletics) check, usable once per turn.","Infectious Fury":"At 10th level, hitting a creature with a natural weapon while raging can force it to make a Wisdom saving throw with a DC of 8 plus your Constitution modifier and proficiency bonus. On a failed save, you choose either to compel the target to spend its reaction attacking another creature you can see, or to deal 2d12 psychic damage. You can use this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all uses on a long rest.","Call the Hunt":"At 14th level, when you start a rage you can invite a number of willing creatures within 30 feet equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum one), and each accepting creature gains you grant 5 temporary hit points. While the rage lasts, those allies can once per turn roll a d6 and add the result to the damage of a hit. You can use this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all uses on a long rest."},
"barbarian:berserker":{"Frenzy":"At 3rd level, you can add a frenzy to your rage, which lets you make one melee weapon attack as a bonus action on each later turn while the rage lasts. The cost is one level of exhaustion when the rage ends.","Mindless Rage":"Starting at 6th level, your rage protects you from being charmed or frightened. If either effect is already on you when you begin raging, it is paused rather than removed until the rage ends. No separate uses are needed since it works for as long as you rage.","Intimidating Presence":"At 10th level, you can use your action to terrify one creature you can see within 30 feet, which must make a Wisdom save (DC 8 + proficiency bonus + Charisma modifier) or be frightened until the end of your next turn. You can spend later actions to extend the fear, but it ends if the target is out of sight or more than 60 feet away. A creature that passes its save can't be targeted by this feature again for 24 hours.","Retaliation":"Starting at 14th level, when a creature within 5 feet of you damages you, you can use your reaction to make a melee weapon attack against it."},
"barbarian:giant":{"Giant's Power":"At 3rd level, you learn to speak, read, and write Giant, or another language if you already know Giant. You also gain one cantrip of your choice, either druidcraft or thaumaturgy, and Wisdom is the ability you use to cast it.","Giant's Havoc":"While raging at 3rd level, you can add your Rage Damage bonus to the damage of successful Strength-based thrown weapon attacks. Your reach also grows by 5 feet, and if you are smaller than Large you become Large along with your gear, unless there isn't room for the change.","Elemental Cleaver":"When you start a rage at 6th level, you can imbue one weapon you hold with acid, cold, fire, thunder, or lightning. While raging with it, the weapon's damage changes to that type, adds 1d6 of that damage on a hit, and gains the thrown property (20/60 feet), returning to your hand after each throw. As a bonus action while raging, you can switch the imbued type, and the benefits don't work for anyone else wielding it. At 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d6.","Mighty Impel":"At 10th level, as a bonus action while raging, you can move a Medium or smaller creature within your reach to an empty space you can see within 30 feet. An unwilling target gets a Strength saving throw against DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier to resist. If the destination can't physically support the creature, it falls, takes normal fall damage, and lands prone. At 14th level, this extends to Large or smaller creatures.","Demiurgic Colossus":"At 14th level, your rage boosts your reach by an extra 10 feet and lets you grow to Large or Huge, your choice. It also lets Mighty Impel affect Large or smaller creatures and raises Elemental Cleaver's extra damage to 2d6."},
"barbarian:storm-herald":{"Storm Aura":"While raging, you project a 10-foot magical aura that stops at total cover. Entering a rage triggers its effect, and you can retrigger it as a bonus action on each turn. You pick desert, sea, or tundra, with save DCs of 8 + proficiency + Constitution modifier: desert deals fire damage to others (2, rising to 3, 4, 5, then 6 at levels 5, 10, 15, and 20), sea forces a Dexterity save for lightning damage (1d6, scaling to 2d6, 3d6, then 4d6), and tundra grants temporary hit points to chosen allies (2, rising like desert). You can switch environments whenever you gain a barbarian level.","Storm Soul":"At 6th level, your chosen environment keeps helping you even when the aura is off. Desert gives fire resistance, immunity to extreme heat, and an action to set an unattended flammable object alight by touch. Sea gives lightning resistance, underwater breathing, and a 30-foot swim speed. Tundra gives cold resistance, immunity to extreme cold, and an action to freeze a 5-foot cube of water into ice that melts after 1 minute, unless a creature is inside it.","Shielding Storm":"At 10th level, you extend your storm's protection to allies. While a creature you choose is inside your Storm Aura, it gains the damage resistance from your Storm Soul for your chosen environment. This makes the aura a defensive tool for your party as well as a damaging one.","Raging Storm":"At 14th level, your storm strikes back harder. Desert lets you use your reaction after a creature in your aura hits you to force a Dexterity save, dealing fire damage equal to half your barbarian level on a failure. Sea lets you use your reaction after hitting a creature in your aura to force a Strength save, knocking it prone on a failure. Tundra lets you pick a creature in your aura when the aura activates and force a Strength save, reducing its speed to 0 until the start of your next turn on a failure."},
"barbarian:totem-warrior":{"Spirit Seeker":"At 3rd level you learn Beast Sense and Speak with Animals, but you can only cast them as rituals, so no spell slots are spent. This gives you a way to communicate with and sense beasts without using up your magic.","Totem Spirit":"At 3rd level you pick one totem animal, which grants a benefit while you rage, and you need a physical charm made from that animal's fur, feathers, claws, teeth, or bones. Bear gives resistance to all damage except psychic. Eagle lets enemies attack you with disadvantage on opportunity attacks and lets you Dash as a bonus action, both only without heavy armor. Elk adds 15 feet to your walking speed without heavy armor. Tiger adds 10 feet to long jumps and 3 feet to high jumps. Wolf lets allies have advantage on melee attacks against hostile creatures within 5 feet of you.","Aspect of the Beast":"At 6th level you gain a permanent passive benefit from a totem animal, which can be the one you chose earlier or a new one. Bear doubles your carrying capacity and gives advantage on Strength checks to push, pull, lift, or break things. Eagle lets you see up to a mile with clarity and ignores dim light penalties on Wisdom (Perception). Elk doubles your travel pace and that of up to ten companions within 60 feet, while you are not incapacitated. Tiger grants proficiency in two of Athletics, Acrobatics, Stealth, and Survival. Wolf lets you track creatures at a fast pace and move stealthily at a normal pace.","Spirit Walker":"At 10th level you can cast Commune with Nature, but only as a ritual. When you do, a spectral version of one of your chosen totem animals appears and delivers the information you seek.","Totemic Attunement":"At 14th level you gain a stronger raging benefit from a totem animal, which can match your earlier choice or be a different one. Bear makes hostile creatures within 5 feet of you attack with disadvantage against anyone other than you or another creature with this feature, unless they cannot see or hear you or cannot be frightened. Eagle gives you a flying speed equal to your walking speed while raging, but only in short bursts, and you fall if you end your turn in the air. Elk lets you use a bonus action to move through the space of a Large or smaller creature, which forces a Strength save (DC 8 plus Strength modifier plus proficiency bonus) or knocks it prone and deals 1d12 plus Strength modifier bludgeoning damage. Tiger grants a bonus-action extra melee attack after moving at least 20 feet straight toward a Large or smaller target. Wolf lets you use a bonus action to knock a Large or smaller creature prone after hitting it with a melee weapon attack."},
"barbarian:wild-magic":{"Magic Awareness":"As an action, you can briefly sense concentrated magic. Until the end of your next turn, you detect any spell or magic item within 60 feet that isn't hidden behind total cover, and each sensed spell reveals its school. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all uses after a long rest.","Wild Surge":"When you enter a rage, you roll on the Wild Magic table to get a random magical effect. Any saving throw it requires has a DC of 8 plus your proficiency bonus plus your Constitution modifier. Some results can be repeated as bonus actions for the rest of the rage, and they range from necrotic bursts and short teleports to summoned spirits, weapon enchantment, retaliatory force damage, a temporary AC boost, difficult terrain, and radiant blinding bolts.","Bolstering Magic":"Starting at 6th level, you can use an action to touch a creature, including yourself, and grant it one benefit of your choice. The first option gives it a d3 to add to attack rolls and ability checks for 10 minutes, while the second lets it regain one expended spell slot of level 3 or lower, though a creature can receive that slot benefit only once per long rest. You can use this action a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all uses after a long rest.","Unstable Backlash":"At 10th level, while you are raging and have just taken damage or failed a saving throw, you can use your reaction to roll on the Wild Magic table and immediately produce the result. The new effect replaces whatever Wild Surge effect you currently have active.","Controlled Surge":"At 14th level, whenever you roll on the Wild Magic table, you roll twice and choose which of the two outcomes to apply. If both dice show the same number, you may disregard it and pick any effect on the table."},
"barbarian:zealot":{"Divine Fury":"You pick necrotic or radiant when you take the path at 3rd level. The bonus is tied to your rage, so it ends when the rage does.","Warrior of the Gods":"Starting at 3rd level, a spell whose only effect is returning you to life, without making you undead, can be cast on you without material components. This applies to spells like Raise Dead.","Fanatical Focus":"From 6th level, if you fail a saving throw while raging, you can reroll it and must take the new result. You can use this once per rage.","Zealous Presence":"At 10th level, you can use a bonus action to give a divine battle cry. Up to ten allies of your choice within 60 feet who can hear you gain advantage on attack rolls and saving throws until the start of your next turn. You can use it once per long rest.","Rage Beyond Death":"From 14th level, while raging, dropping to 0 hit points does not knock you unconscious, but you still make death saving throws and take damage normally at 0 HP. If failed death saves would kill you, you instead survive until your rage ends, and you die then only if you are still at 0 HP. There are no uses limit or later upgrades."},
"bard:creation":{"Mote of Potential":"When you give a creature a Bardic Inspiration die, you can attach a Tiny, intangible, invulnerable mote that orbits within 5 feet of it until that die is spent. When the die is used, the mote adds an effect: an ability check lets the creature reroll and keep the better result, an attack roll triggers thunder damage equal to the die result against creatures near the target unless they pass a Constitution save against your spell save DC, and a saving throw grants temporary hit points equal to the die result plus your Charisma modifier (minimum 1).","Performance of Creation":"As an action, you can conjure one nonmagical item of Medium or smaller size within 10 feet, worth up to 20 gp per bard level, which fades after hours equal to your proficiency bonus. You can make one free use per long rest, or spend a 2nd-level or higher spell slot for another, and only one conjured item can exist at a time. The maximum size grows to Large at 6th level and Huge at 14th level.","Animating Performance":"As an action at 6th level, you animate one Large or smaller nonmagical item within 30 feet that no one is wearing or carrying, using the Dancing Item stat block scaled by your proficiency bonus. The item lasts up to 1 hour, until it drops to 0 hit points, or until you die, and it acts right after your turn, defaulting to Dodge unless you spend a bonus action to direct it. You can give it orders as part of the bonus action used for Bardic Inspiration. Once per long rest, or by spending a 3rd-level or higher spell slot, you can animate another, and only one animated item can exist at a time.","Creative Crescendo":"At 14th level, when you use Performance of Creation, you can create several items at once, up to your Charisma modifier (minimum two). Only one of them may be the maximum size, and the rest must be Small or Tiny. The gold piece limit on created items no longer applies."},
"bard:eloquence":{"Silver Tongue":"Beginning at 3rd level, any Charisma (Persuasion) or Charisma (Deception) check lets you treat a d20 roll of 9 or less as a 10.","Unsettling Words":"Starting at 3rd level, you can spend one Bardic Inspiration use as a bonus action to target a creature you can see within 60 feet. Roll the die, and the target subtracts that number from its next saving throw before your next turn. Its uses are limited by your Bardic Inspiration uses.","Unfailing Inspiration":"At 6th level, if a creature adds your Bardic Inspiration die to a check, attack, or save and still fails, it keeps the die. This lets the die carry over to another roll instead of being lost.","Universal Speech":"At 6th level, you can use an action to let up to your Charisma modifier creatures within 60 feet (minimum one) understand you in any language for 1 hour. You can use it once per long rest, or spend a spell slot to use it again sooner.","Infectious Inspiration":"At 14th level, when a creature within 60 feet succeeds on a roll using your Bardic Inspiration die, you can use your reaction to give a different creature that can hear you within 60 feet a Bardic Inspiration die without spending one of your uses. You can do this a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum once), and you regain all uses on a long rest."},
"bard:glamour":{"Mantle of Inspiration":"At 3rd level, you can spend one Bardic Inspiration as a bonus action to gain a striking fey look. Up to your Charisma modifier (minimum one) willing allies within 60 feet who can see you each gain 5 temporary hit points and can use their reaction to move their full speed without provoking opportunity attacks. The temporary hit points rise to 8 at 5th level, 11 at 10th, and 14 at 15th.","Enthralling Performance":"At 3rd level, you can perform for at least 1 minute by singing, reciting, or dancing. Afterward, up to your Charisma modifier (minimum one) humanoids within 60 feet who watched and listened to the whole show must each pass a Wisdom save against your spell save DC or become charmed. Charmed targets praise you, hinder your opponents, and avoid violence unless already inclined to help, and the effect ends after 1 hour, on damage, if you attack them, or if they see you harm an ally. Targets who succeed don't realize you tried, and you can use this once per short or long rest.","Mantle of Majesty":"At 6th level, as a bonus action, you cast Command without using a spell slot and take on an unearthly beauty for 1 minute or until your concentration ends. While it lasts, you can cast Command as a bonus action on each of your turns without a spell slot. Creatures already charmed by you automatically fail their saves against these Commands, and you can use this feature again only after a long rest.","Unbreakable Majesty":"At 14th level, your appearance permanently becomes more lovely and fierce. As a bonus action, you can project a majestic presence for 1 minute or until you are incapacitated. While active, the first attack each turn against you requires the attacker to make a Charisma save against your spell save DC; on a failure, it cannot attack you that turn and must retarget or waste the attack, and on a success it has disadvantage on saves against your spells during its next turn. You can use this again after a short or long rest."},
"bard:lore":{"Bonus Proficiencies":"Joining the College at 3rd level grants you proficiency in three skills of your choice. This broadens your capability for ability checks from the start.","Cutting Words":"At 3rd level, you can spend a Bardic Inspiration die as a reaction to subtract its result from a visible creature's attack roll, ability check, or damage roll within 60 feet. You can wait until after the creature rolls, but before the outcome or damage is resolved. Each use draws from your limited Bardic Inspiration pool, and creatures that cannot hear you or are immune to being charmed are unaffected.","Additional Magical Secrets":"At 6th level, you learn two spells from any class's list, as long as each is a cantrip or a spell level you can already cast. They count as bard spells for you without taking up spots in your known spells total.","Peerless Skill":"Starting at 14th level, you can spend a Bardic Inspiration use on an ability check to add the rolled die to the total. You can decide after seeing the d20 result but before the DM rules on success or failure. It draws from the same limited Bardic Inspiration pool."},
"bard:spirits":{"Guiding Whispers":"At 3rd level, you learn the Guidance cantrip, which doesn't use up one of your bard cantrips known. When you cast it, its range extends to 60 feet.","Spiritual Focus":"From 3rd level, a candle, crystal ball, skull, spirit board, or tarokka deck can serve as your spellcasting focus for bard spells. At 6th level, when a damaging or healing bard spell cast through this focus takes effect, you roll a d6 and add that result to one of the spell's damage or healing rolls.","Tales from Beyond":"From 3rd level, while holding your focus, you can spend a Bardic Inspiration use as a bonus action and roll on the Spirit Tales table with that die to pick a tale, which lasts until you grant it or finish a short or long rest. Using an action, you choose a creature you can see within 30 feet (possibly yourself) to receive the effect, which you can't grant again until you roll a new tale. Only one tale can be held at a time, and a new roll replaces the old one. Any saving throw uses your spell save DC.","Spirit Session":"At 6th level, you can perform an hour-long ritual with your focus during a short or long rest, joined by willing creatures up to your proficiency bonus, including yourself. When it ends, you temporarily learn one spell of a level no higher than the number of participants, from any class, that you can cast and that belongs to the Divination or Necromancy school. The spell counts as a bard spell without using up a spell known slot, and you can perform the ritual once per long rest, keeping the spell until you start a long rest.","Mystical Connection":"At 14th level, when you roll on the Spirit Tales table, you roll the die twice and choose which of the two resulting tales to bestow. If both dice show the same number, you may instead select any tale on the table."},
"bard:swords":{"Bonus Proficiencies":"At 3rd level, joining this college grants proficiency with medium armor and the scimitar. If you already know a simple or martial melee weapon, you can also use it as a spellcasting focus for your bard spells.","Fighting Style":"At 3rd level, you pick one fighting specialty, and you can't select the same option twice. Dueling gives +2 to damage with a one-handed melee weapon when no other weapon is in use, while Two-Weapon Fighting lets you add your ability modifier to the damage of your off-hand attack.","Blade Flourish":"Starting at 3rd level, whenever you take the Attack action, your walking speed rises by 10 feet until the end of that turn. If a weapon attack from that action hits, you can apply one flourish, though only one per turn, and each costs a Bardic Inspiration use. Defensive Flourish adds the die roll as extra damage and to your AC until your next turn, Slashing Flourish splits the extra damage with creatures within 5 feet, and Mobile Flourish adds damage, pushes the target away by 5 feet plus the die roll in feet, and lets you use your reaction to reposition near it.","Extra Attack":"Beginning at 6th level, when you take the Attack action on your turn, you can make two attacks instead of one.","Master's Flourish":"Starting at 14th level, when you use a Blade Flourish, you can roll a d6 in place of spending a Bardic Inspiration die. This makes the flourishes usable without consuming your inspiration uses."},
"bard:valor":{"Bonus Proficiencies":"At 3rd level, joining this college grants training with medium armor, shields, and martial weapons.","Combat Inspiration":"From 3rd level, an ally holding one of your Bardic Inspiration dice can either add the rolled number to damage on a weapon attack it just made, or spend its reaction to add the roll to its AC against an incoming attack after seeing the roll but before the hit is decided.","Extra Attack":"At 6th level, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn, you can make two attacks instead of one.","Battle Magic":"At 14th level, when you cast a bard spell using your action, you can also make one weapon attack as a bonus action. This lets you combine spellcasting and melee strikes in the same turn."},
"bard:whispers":{"Psychic Blades":"Once per turn, when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can spend a Bardic Inspiration use to add extra psychic damage to that target. The damage starts at 2d6 and rises to 3d6 at 5th level, 5d6 at 10th level, and 8d6 at 15th level.","Words of Terror":"After talking with a humanoid alone for a full minute, you can plant paranoia in its mind. At the end of the talk, it makes a Wisdom save against your spell save DC or becomes frightened of you or a creature you choose for 1 hour, ending early if it or its allies are harmed. If it succeeds, it never realizes you tried. You can use this once per short or long rest.","Mantle of Whispers":"At 6th level, when a humanoid dies within 30 feet, you can use your reaction to capture its shadow, which you keep until you use it or finish a long rest. Using the shadow as an action turns it into a disguise that makes you look like the dead person, alive and healthy, for 1 hour or until you end it as a bonus action. You gain the casual personal details the person would share with an acquaintance, but not secrets. Observers can see through the disguise with a Wisdom (Insight) check contested by your Charisma (Deception) check, and you add +5 to yours. You can capture only one shadow per short or long rest.","Shadow Lore":"At 14th level, as an action, you whisper a phrase that only one creature within 30 feet can hear, provided it shares your language and can hear you. The target makes a Wisdom save against your spell save DC, and on a failure it is charmed by you for 8 hours or until you or your allies harm it. It believes you know its most shameful secret, so it obeys your commands out of fear, though it won't risk its life for you and offers favors like a close friend would. When the charm ends, it doesn't remember why it feared you. You can use this once per long rest."},
"cleric:arcana":{"Arcane Initiate":"You become proficient in Arcana and learn two wizard cantrips of your choice, which are treated as cleric cantrips for you. There are no later-level upgrades to this feature.","Channel Divinity: Arcane Abjuration":"Starting at 2nd level, you spend a Channel Divinity use as an action to show your holy symbol to one celestial, elemental, fey, or fiend within 30 feet that can see or hear you. If it fails a Wisdom save, it is turned for 1 minute or until it takes damage, and it must flee from you, cannot end its move near you, takes no reactions, and can only Dash or escape, or Dodge if cornered. At 5th level, a failed save also banishes it for 1 minute if it is off its home plane and its challenge rating is within a threshold that rises from 1/2 at 5th level to 1 at 8th, 2 at 11th, 3 at 14th, and 4 at 17th. The banishment needs no concentration.","Spell Breaker":"Starting at 6th level, whenever you heal an ally with a spell of 1st level or higher, you can also end one spell on that ally. The ended spell's level cannot exceed the level of the spell slot you used for the healing.","Potent Spellcasting":"Starting at 8th level, you add your Wisdom modifier to the damage dealt by any cleric cantrip you cast.","Arcane Mastery":"At 17th level, you pick four wizard spells, one each of 6th, 7th, 8th, and 9th level, and add them to your domain spells. They are always prepared and count as cleric spells for you."},
"cleric:death":{"Bonus Proficiency":"Choosing this domain at 1st level gives you proficiency with all martial weapons.","Reaper":"At 1st level you learn one necromancy cantrip of your choice from any class's spell list. When you cast a necromancy cantrip that normally affects only one creature, you can aim it at two creatures that are within range and no more than 5 feet apart from each other.","Channel Divinity: Touch of Death":"Starting at 2nd level, after a melee weapon attack hits a creature, you can spend a Channel Divinity use to add extra necrotic damage to that target. The bonus equals 5 plus twice your cleric level.","Inescapable Destruction":"Starting at 6th level, the necrotic damage from your cleric spells and Channel Divinity options bypasses resistance to necrotic damage.","Divine Strike":"At 8th level, once on each of your turns when a weapon attack hits a creature, you can infuse the strike with necrotic energy for an extra 1d8 necrotic damage. At 14th level, this bonus damage increases to 2d8.","Improved Reaper":"Starting at 17th level, when you cast a necromancy spell of 1st through 5th level that targets only one creature, you can target two creatures instead, as long as they are within range and within 5 feet of each other. If the spell consumes its material components, you must supply them for each target."},
"cleric:forge":{"Bonus Proficiencies":"Taking this domain at 1st level grants training with heavy armor and smith's tools.","Blessing of the Forge":"At 1st level, you can spend a long rest's end touching a nonmagical suit of armor or simple or martial weapon to make it magical for a while. The item gives +1 AC if it's armor, or +1 to attack and damage rolls if it's a weapon, and the effect lasts until your next long rest ends or you die. You can use it once per long rest.","Channel Divinity: Artisan's Blessing":"Starting at 2nd level, you can spend a Channel Divinity use on an hour-long ritual that crafts a nonmagical item containing metal, worth up to 100 gp, such as a weapon, armor, ammunition, tools, or a copy of a key you possess. You lay out metal, including coins, equal in value to the finished item, and it fuses into the creation at the ritual's end within 5 feet of you.","Soul of the Forge":"At 6th level, you gain resistance to fire damage. While wearing heavy armor, you also get a +1 bonus to AC.","Divine Strike":"At 8th level, once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can add extra fire damage. The bonus is 1d8 at 8th level and rises to 2d8 at 14th level.","Saint of Forge and Fire":"At 17th level, you become immune to fire damage. While wearing heavy armor, you also resist bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage from nonmagical attacks."},
"cleric:grave":{"Circle of Mortality":"When a spell you cast would roll dice to restore hit points to a creature at 0 hit points, you use the maximum value on each die instead. You also gain the Spare the Dying cantrip, which doesn't count against your known cantrips. It has a 30-foot range for you and can be cast as a bonus action.","Eyes of the Grave":"As an action, you sense undead within 60 feet until the end of your next turn, excluding any behind total cover or shielded from divination. The sense reveals only their locations, not their nature or identity. You can use it a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum once), regaining all uses on a long rest.","Channel Divinity: Path to the Grave":"Starting at 2nd level, you spend Channel Divinity as an action to curse a creature you can see within 30 feet, lasting until the end of your next turn. The next attack by you or an ally that hits the cursed creature makes it vulnerable to that attack's damage, and the curse then ends.","Sentinel at Death's Door":"At 6th level, when you or a visible ally within 30 feet is critically hit, you can use your reaction to turn that critical hit into a normal hit, canceling any effects the critical would trigger. You can use this a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum once), regaining uses on a long rest.","Potent Spellcasting":"Starting at 8th level, you add your Wisdom modifier to the damage dealt by any cleric cantrip you cast.","Keeper of Souls":"At 17th level, when an enemy you can see dies within 30 feet, you or one chosen ally within 30 feet regains hit points equal to that enemy's Hit Dice. You must not be incapacitated, and you can use this only once until the start of your next turn."},
"cleric:knowledge":{"Blessings of Knowledge":"At 1st level you pick up two languages of your choice and gain proficiency in two of Arcana, History, Nature, or Religion. Your proficiency bonus doubles on ability checks using those two skills.","Channel Divinity: Knowledge of the Ages":"Starting at 2nd level, spending one Channel Divinity use as an action grants proficiency in one skill or tool you choose. The proficiency lasts 10 minutes. It is a temporary boost that refreshes with each use of Channel Divinity.","Channel Divinity: Read Thoughts":"At 6th level, use an action and a Channel Divinity use to target a creature you can see within 60 feet, which must make a Wisdom save. On a failure, you read its surface thoughts for 1 minute while it stays within 60 feet, and you can spend your action to end the effect and cast Suggestion on it for free, with the target auto-failing that save. A creature that succeeds can't be targeted this way again until you finish a long rest.","Potent Spellcasting":"Starting at 8th level, you add your Wisdom modifier to the damage dealt by any cleric cantrip. It applies every time you cast one of those cantrips.","Visions of the Past":"At 17th level, meditate for at least 1 minute, concentrating for up to your Wisdom score in minutes, to see shadowy glimpses of recent events tied to a held object or your surroundings. Object reading reveals an item's past owners and their most significant event with it, and extra minutes reveal earlier owners within your Wisdom score in days. Area reading shows significant events in a 50-foot cube going back Wisdom-score days, one per minute, starting with the newest. You can use this once per short or long rest."},
"cleric:life":{"Bonus Proficiency":"It lets you wear heavy armor without the usual penalties for lacking that proficiency.","Disciple of Life":"Starting at 1st level, every time you cast a healing spell of 1st level or higher that restores hit points to a creature, that creature gains extra hit points equal to 2 plus the spell's level.","Channel Divinity: Preserve Life":"From 2nd level, you can use an action to show your holy symbol and release healing energy totaling five times your cleric level, divided among creatures you choose within 30 feet. No recipient can be healed above half its maximum hit points, and undead and constructs can't be targeted. Uses are limited by your Channel Divinity allotment, which refreshes on a rest.","Blessed Healer":"Beginning at 6th level, whenever you cast a healing spell of 1st level or higher on another creature, you also regain hit points equal to 2 plus the spell's level.","Divine Strike":"At 8th level, once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can add extra radiant damage of 1d8. At 14th level, this bonus damage increases to 2d8.","Supreme Healing":"Starting at 17th level, whenever a spell calls for rolling dice to restore hit points, you use the maximum value of each die instead of rolling. For example, a spell that would restore 2d6 hit points instead restores 12."},
"cleric:light":{"Bonus Cantrip":"Taking this domain at 1st level grants you the Light cantrip if you don't already know it. It doesn't use up one of your cleric cantrip slots.","Warding Flare":"From 1st level, when a creature you can see within 30 feet attacks you, you can use your reaction to give that attack disadvantage. Creatures that can't be blinded are immune. You can use this a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum once), and all uses return after a long rest.","Channel Divinity: Radiance of the Dawn":"Starting at 2nd level, you spend Channel Divinity as an action to show your holy symbol, which dispels magical darkness within 30 feet. Each hostile creature within 30 feet makes a Constitution save, taking 2d10 plus your cleric level in radiant damage on a failure or half on a success. Creatures with total cover from you are unaffected.","Improved Flare":"Starting at 6th level, you can use Warding Flare against a creature you can see within 30 feet that attacks someone other than you. This widens the feature's reach beyond attacks against yourself.","Potent Spellcasting":"Starting at 8th level, your Wisdom modifier is added to the damage of any cleric cantrip you cast. This boosts your cantrip damage output as you advance.","Corona of Light":"Starting at 17th level, you use your action to create a sunlight aura lasting 1 minute, which you can end early with another action. It sheds bright light in a 60-foot radius and dim light for 30 feet beyond that. Enemies in the bright light have disadvantage on saving throws against spells that deal fire or radiant damage."},
"cleric:nature":{"Acolyte of Nature":"At 1st level you learn one druid cantrip, which counts as a cleric cantrip for you without using up your cleric cantrip slots. You also become proficient in Animal Handling, Nature, or Survival, your choice.","Bonus Proficiency":"At 1st level you gain proficiency with heavy armor. This is a permanent benefit with no uses or limits.","Channel Divinity: Charm Animals and Plants":"Starting at 2nd level, you spend a Channel Divinity use as an action, showing your holy symbol and invoking your deity's name. Each beast or plant creature within 30 feet that can see you must make a Wisdom saving throw, and those that fail are charmed for 1 minute or until damaged, becoming friendly to you and anyone you designate.","Dampen Elements":"Starting at 6th level, you can use your reaction when you or a creature within 30 feet takes acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage. You grant that creature resistance against that instance of the damage.","Divine Strike":"At 8th level, once on each of your turns when you hit with a weapon attack, you can add extra cold, fire, or lightning damage of your choice. The extra damage is 1d8 at 8th level and rises to 2d8 at 14th level.","Master of Nature":"At 17th level, you can take a bonus action on your turn to verbally command each creature currently charmed by your Charm Animals and Plants feature. You dictate what each one does on its next turn. This works on any creatures still under that charm."},
"cleric:order":{"Bonus Proficiencies":"Choosing this domain at 1st level gives you training with heavy armor and one skill of your choice, either Intimidation or Persuasion.","Voice of Authority":"Starting at 1st level, when you cast a spell using a slot of 1st level or higher that targets an ally, that ally can immediately use its reaction to make one weapon attack on a creature you can see. If the spell targets several allies, you decide which one gets the attack.","Channel Divinity: Order's Demand":"At 2nd level, you spend a Channel Divinity use as an action to hold up your holy symbol and unsettle nearby creatures within 30 feet that can see or hear you. Each creature you pick makes a Wisdom saving throw, and on a failure it is charmed until the end of your next turn or until it takes damage. You can also make charmed creatures drop whatever they're holding.","Embodiment of the Law":"At 6th level, when you cast an enchantment spell using a slot of 1st level or higher whose normal casting time is one action, you can cast it as a bonus action instead. You can do this a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum once), and all uses return after a long rest.","Divine Strike":"At 8th level, once per turn when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can add 1d8 psychic damage to that hit. The bonus damage rises to 2d8 at 14th level.","Order's Wrath":"At 17th level, if you deal Divine Strike damage to a creature on your turn, you can place a curse on it that lasts until the start of your next turn. The next time one of your allies hits that cursed creature, it takes 2d8 psychic damage and the curse ends. You can apply this curse only once per turn."},
"cleric:peace":{"Implement of Peace":"At 1st level, you become proficient in one skill of your choice: Insight, Performance, or Persuasion.","Emboldening Bond":"As an action, you bond a number of willing creatures within 30 feet, including yourself, equal to your proficiency bonus, lasting 10 minutes or until you use it again. While bonded creatures are within 30 feet of one another, each can add a d4 to one attack roll, ability check, or saving throw, but only once per turn. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all uses on a long rest.","Channel Divinity: Balm of Peace":"Starting at 2nd level, as an action you move up to your speed without provoking opportunity attacks. Each creature you come within 5 feet of during that move regains 2d6 plus your Wisdom modifier in hit points (minimum 1), though each creature can benefit only once per use. This uses one of your Channel Divinity uses.","Protective Bond":"Starting at 6th level, when a creature affected by Emboldening Bond is about to take damage, another bonded creature within 30 feet can use its reaction to teleport to an open space within 5 feet of the first. That second creature takes the damage in its place.","Potent Spellcasting":"At 8th level, you add your Wisdom modifier to the damage of any cleric cantrip you cast.","Expansive Bond":"At 17th level, the ranges of Emboldening Bond and Protective Bond increase from 30 feet to 60 feet. In addition, a creature that takes another's damage through Protective Bond gains resistance to that damage."},
"cleric:tempest":{"Bonus Proficiencies":"At 1st level you become proficient with martial weapons and heavy armor. It's a passive gain with no uses or scaling, giving you access to stronger weapons and armor from the start.","Wrath of the Storm":"From 1st level, when a creature you can see within 5 feet hits you, you can use your reaction to force it to make a Dexterity save. It takes 2d8 lightning or thunder damage (your choice) on a failed save, or half as much on a success. You can use it a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum once), regaining all uses on a long rest.","Channel Divinity: Destructive Wrath":"Starting at 2nd level, you can spend a Channel Divinity use to make lightning or thunder damage you roll deal its maximum value instead of being rolled. It works on any lightning or thunder damage you roll, so it's useful for boosting big damage spells or attacks.","Thunderous Strike":"At 6th level, when you deal lightning damage to a Large or smaller creature, you can also shove it up to 10 feet away from you. It's a passive add-on to your lightning hits that costs no uses and has no scaling. It's mainly used for creating distance or repositioning enemies.","Divine Strike":"At 8th level, once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can add an extra 1d8 thunder damage to that target. The bonus scales up to 2d8 at 14th level. It's limited to once per turn, not per attack.","Stormborn":"At 17th level, you gain a flying speed equal to your current walking speed whenever you are outdoors and not underground. Flight is unavailable while you're indoors or underground."},
"cleric:trickery":{"Blessing of the Trickster":"Starting at 1st level, you use an action to touch a willing ally other than yourself and grant it advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. The boost lasts one hour, and using the feature again replaces the earlier blessing.","Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity":"From 2nd level, spending a Channel Divinity use lets you conjure a flawless illusion of yourself in an empty space you can see within 30 feet. It lasts up to a minute unless you lose concentration. Each turn, as a bonus action, you can slide the duplicate up to 30 feet while it stays within 120 feet of you. You can cast spells from the duplicate's position while still using your own senses, and you gain advantage on attacks against creatures within 5 feet of both you and the duplicate that can see it.","Channel Divinity: Cloak of Shadows":"At 6th level, you use Channel Divinity as an action to become invisible until the end of your next turn. Making an attack or casting a spell makes you visible again.","Divine Strike":"At 8th level, once per turn when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can add 1d8 poison damage to that hit. The extra damage rises to 2d8 at 14th level.","Improved Duplicity":"At 17th level, Invoke Duplicity creates up to four duplicates instead of one. As a bonus action on your turn, you can move any number of them up to 30 feet each, keeping every duplicate within 120 feet of you."},
"cleric:twilight":{"Bonus Proficiencies":"At 1st level, this subclass grants training with all martial weapons and heavy armor. It broadens the cleric's combat options without requiring any resource or activation.","Eyes of Night":"From 1st level, you have darkvision to 300 feet, and within that range dim light looks bright and darkness looks dim to you. As an action you can share this darkvision with willing creatures within 10 feet, up to your Wisdom modifier (minimum one), for 1 hour. You can share it again only after a long rest, unless you spend a spell slot of any level.","Vigilant Blessing":"At 1st level, you can use an action to touch a creature, including yourself, and give it advantage on its next initiative roll. The boost is lost once that roll is made, and using the feature again replaces any unused benefit.","Channel Divinity: Twilight Sanctuary":"At 2nd level, you spend a Channel Divinity use as an action to present your holy symbol and create a 30-foot-radius sphere of dim light centered on you that moves with you for up to 1 minute, ending early if you are incapacitated or die. Each creature, including you, that ends its turn inside gains either temporary hit points equal to 1d6 plus your cleric level or the removal of one charmed or frightened effect.","Steps of Night":"Starting at 6th level, while you stand in dim light or darkness, you can use a bonus action to gain a flying speed equal to your walking speed for 1 minute. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and all uses return when you finish a long rest.","Divine Strike":"At 8th level, once per turn when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can add 1d8 radiant damage to that attack. The extra damage grows to 2d8 at 14th level.","Twilight Shroud":"At 17th level, you and your allies gain half cover while inside the sphere created by Twilight Sanctuary. This gives a passive defensive bonus to everyone who stays within the sphere's area."},
"cleric:war":{"Bonus Proficiencies":"At level 1, you become trained with martial weapons and heavy armor, giving you access to sturdier gear than most clerics can use.","War Priest":"From level 1, your deity grants you bursts of inspiration in combat. When you take the Attack action, you can spend a bonus action to make one extra weapon attack. You can do this a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum once), and all uses return after a long rest.","Channel Divinity: Guided Strike":"Starting at level 2, you can spend a Channel Divinity use to sharpen your aim. After you roll an attack, you can add +10 to that roll, choosing after seeing the result but before the DM announces whether it hits. Channel Divinity uses are shared with your other cleric options and recharge on a rest.","Channel Divinity: War God's Blessing":"At level 6, you can use your reaction and a Channel Divinity use to boost an ally's attack. When a creature within 30 feet of you makes an attack roll, you add +10 to it, deciding after the roll but before the hit or miss is revealed. It uses the same shared Channel Divinity pool as your other options.","Divine Strike":"At level 8, once per turn when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can add 1d8 extra damage of the weapon's damage type. The bonus rises to 2d8 when you reach level 14. It is a passive feature with no rest-based limit beyond once per turn.","Avatar of Battle":"At level 17, you gain resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage from nonmagical sources."},
"cleric:ambition":{"Warding Flare":"Starting at 1st level, you can use your reaction when a creature you can see within 30 feet attacks you, forcing the attacker to make the roll at disadvantage as a burst of light dazzles them. Creatures that can't be blinded are unaffected. You can use this a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum once), and you regain all uses after a long rest.","Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity":"Beginning at 2nd level, you spend a Channel Divinity use to conjure a flawless illusory copy of yourself for up to 1 minute, ending early if your concentration breaks. As an action, it appears in an empty visible space within 30 feet, and on later turns you can slide it up to 30 feet as a bonus action, always keeping it within 120 feet of you. You cast spells from the copy's position while still using your own senses, and you gain advantage on attacks against a creature that can see the illusion when you and it are both within 5 feet of that creature.","Channel Divinity: Cloak of Shadows":"At 6th level, you can spend Channel Divinity as an action to become invisible until the end of your next turn. Making an attack or casting a spell causes you to become visible again.","Potent Spellcasting":"From 8th level onward, your Wisdom modifier is added to the damage of any cleric cantrip you cast.","Improved Duplicity":"At 17th level, Invoke Duplicity lets you create up to four illusory copies rather than one. As a bonus action on your turn, you can shift any number of these copies up to 30 feet each, though all of them must stay within 120 feet of you."},
"cleric:solidarity":{"Bonus Proficiency":"At 1st level, you become trained in heavy armor, letting you wear the sturdiest protection available to clerics.","Solidarity's Action":"From 1st level, when you use the Help action to boost an ally's attack, you can immediately make one weapon attack as a bonus action. You can do this a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier, with a minimum of once, and uses return after a long rest.","Channel Divinity: Preserve Life":"Starting at 2nd level, you can spend Channel Divinity as an action to heal wounded allies by displaying your holy symbol. The healing totals five times your cleric level and is split among creatures of your choice within 30 feet. No creature can be healed above half its maximum hit points, and undead and constructs are immune.","Channel Divinity: Oketra's Blessing":"At 6th level, when a creature within 30 feet makes an attack roll, you can use your reaction and Channel Divinity to add +10 to that roll. You decide after seeing the roll but before the outcome of hit or miss is announced.","Divine Strike":"At 8th level, once per turn when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can add extra radiant or other weapon-matching damage of 1d8 to that hit. The bonus die grows to 2d8 at 14th level. It has no limited uses per rest, only the once-per-turn limit.","Supreme Healing":"At 17th level, whenever a spell requires you to roll dice to restore hit points, you instead use the maximum value of each die. For example, a spell that would heal 2d6 instead restores 12 hit points."},
"cleric:strength":{"Bonus Proficiency":"At 1st level you become proficient with heavy armor, so you can wear the sturdiest armor class without penalty.","Acolyte of Strength":"At 1st level you learn one druid cantrip of your choice and gain proficiency in one skill from Animal Handling, Athletics, Nature, or Survival, which you select.","Channel Divinity: Feat of Strength":"Starting at 2nd level, you can spend a Channel Divinity use to add +10 to any Strength-based attack roll, ability check, or saving throw. You decide after seeing the d20 result but before the DM announces the outcome.","Channel Divinity: Rhonas' Blessing":"At 6th level, when a creature within 30 feet makes a Strength-based attack roll, ability check, or saving throw, you can use your reaction and a Channel Divinity use to give it +10 to that roll. Like Feat of Strength, you choose after seeing the roll but before the result is decided.","Divine Strike":"At 8th level, once on each of your turns when you hit with a weapon attack, you can add 1d8 extra damage of the weapon's damage type. The extra damage increases to 2d8 at 14th level.","Avatar of Battle":"At 17th level, you gain resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage from nonmagical attacks."},
"cleric:zeal":{"Priest of Zeal":"From 1st level, when you take the Attack action you can make one extra weapon attack as a bonus action. You can do this a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum once), and all uses return after a long rest.","Channel Divinity: Consuming Fervor":"Starting at 2nd level, you can spend Channel Divinity whenever you roll fire or thunder damage to deal the maximum possible damage instead of rolling. It trades a die roll for guaranteed peak output.","Resounding Strike":"At 6th level, when your attack deals thunder damage to a creature of Large size or smaller, you can shove that creature up to 10 feet directly away from you. This adds battlefield control to your thunder attacks.","Divine Strike":"At 8th level, once on each of your turns when a weapon attack hits a creature, you can add 1d8 extra damage of the weapon's damage type. The bonus grows to 2d8 at 14th level.","Blaze of Glory":"Starting at 17th level, if an attacker you can see reduces you to 0 hit points, you can use your reaction to move up to your speed to reach it and make a melee weapon attack with advantage. A hit deals an extra 5d10 fire damage plus 5d10 weapon-type damage, then you fall unconscious and start death saves, or die if the damage was lethal. You can use this once per long rest."},
"cleric:fate-ua":{"Omens and Portents":"At 1st level, you can cast Augury once per long rest without a spell slot, and it needs no components when cast this way. Until your next long rest, divination spells that can give a blank or random result, like Commune, have that chance cut by 25 percent.","Ties That Bind":"At 1st level, as an action, you magically link a strand of fate to a touched creature or object for 1 hour or until you reuse it. An unwilling creature can resist with a Wisdom save against your spell save DC. While the link holds and you share a plane, you can sense the bound target's direction, and its movement if it moves. Once per turn, a damaging or healing spell you cast on the target adds a d6 to that effect. You can use the action a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest.","Channel Divinity: Strands of Fate":"At 2nd level, as a bonus action, you can perceive fate's threads around others for up to 1 minute, ending early if your concentration breaks. During that time, when a visible creature makes an attack roll or ability check, you can spend your reaction to give that roll advantage or disadvantage.","Insightful Striking":"At 6th level, as a bonus action, you pick a visible creature within 30 feet and glimpse its defenses until the end of your next turn. You then choose either to add a d6 to your next attack roll against it, or to subtract a d6 from its next saving throw against one of your spells. You can use this bonus action a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all uses on a long rest.","Potent Spellcasting":"At 8th level, you add your Wisdom modifier to the damage dealt by any cleric cantrip you cast.","Visions of the Future":"At 17th level, you can cast Foresight once without expending a spell slot, and that casting lasts 1 minute instead of its normal duration. You regain this ability after a long rest."},
"druid:dreams":{"Balm of the Summer Court":"At 2nd level you gain a pool of fey energy made of d6s equal to your druid level. As a bonus action, you can spend up to half your druid level in dice on an ally within 120 feet, healing them for the total rolled plus 1 temporary hit point per die spent. The spent dice return after a long rest, and a higher druid level means a bigger pool and more dice per use.","Hearth of Moonlight and Shadow":"Starting at 6th level, during a short or long rest you touch a point to create an invisible sphere of magic with a 30-foot radius, which total cover blocks. You and your allies inside get a +5 bonus to Dexterity (Stealth) and Wisdom (Perception) checks, and light from flames inside is hidden from outside observers. The sphere lasts until the rest ends or you leave it.","Hidden Paths":"From 10th level, you can use fey pathways to teleport. As a bonus action, you can teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see, or with your action you can teleport a willing creature you touch up to 30 feet. You can use this a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum once), and all uses return when you finish a long rest.","Walker in Dreams":"At 14th level, after finishing a short rest you can cast Dream (with you as the messenger), Scrying, or Teleportation Circle without a spell slot or material components. The Teleportation Circle version opens a portal to where you last finished a long rest on your current plane, and if you have not rested there, the spell fails without being wasted. You can use this once, and you regain it when you finish a long rest."},
"druid:land":{"Bonus Cantrip":"Taking this circle at 2nd level grants one extra druid cantrip of your choice. That cantrip is free in the sense that it does not take up one of your normal cantrip slots.","Natural Recovery":"From 2nd level, you can reclaim some spent spell slots during a short rest by meditating. The combined level of the slots you recover can be no more than half your druid level, rounded up, and no slot can be 6th level or higher. For example, a 4th-level druid could recover either one 2nd-level slot or two 1st-level slots, and you can use this only once until you finish a long rest.","Circle Spells":"At 3rd, 5th, 7th, and 9th level, you gain access to a set of spells tied to a land you choose from arctic, coast, desert, forest, grassland, mountain, swamp, or Underdark, with two new spells unlocked at each of those levels. These spells are always prepared for you and do not count against your daily prepared spell total. Any of them that are not normally on the druid list still count as druid spells for you.","Land's Stride":"Starting at 6th level, you ignore the extra movement cost of nonmagical difficult terrain. You can also move through nonmagical plants with thorns or spines without being slowed or hurt by them. You further gain advantage on saving throws against magically created or shaped plants meant to restrain movement, such as those from Entangle.","Nature's Ward":"At 10th level, elementals and fey can no longer charm or frighten you. You also gain immunity to poison and disease.","Nature's Sanctuary":"At 14th level, beasts and plant creatures become reluctant to attack you. When one tries, it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your druid spell save DC or else pick a different target, or its attack misses automatically. A creature that passes the save is immune to this effect for 24 hours, and it knows about the effect before it attacks."},
"druid:moon":{"Combat Wild Shape":"Starting at 2nd level, you can use Wild Shape as a bonus action instead of an action, which speeds up combat. While transformed, you can spend a bonus action to burn a spell slot and heal 1d8 hit points for each level of that slot.","Circle Forms":"At 2nd level, your Wild Shape can take the form of a beast with a challenge rating up to 1, ignoring the Max. CR column of the Beast Shapes table while still following its other rules. At 6th level, the challenge rating cap rises to your druid level divided by 3, rounded down.","Primal Strike":"At 6th level, attacks you make in beast form are treated as magical. This lets them get past resistances and immunities that normally shrug off nonmagical physical damage.","Elemental Wild Shape":"At 10th level, you can spend two uses of Wild Shape at the same time to take on the form of an air, earth, fire, or water elemental. This lets you access elemental forms that a single use could not reach.","Thousand Forms":"By 14th level, you can cast Alter Self whenever you like, without spending a spell slot or a daily use. It lets you subtly reshape your body with magic rather than through animal forms."},
"druid:shepherd":{"Speech of the Woods":"Starting at 2nd level, you learn Sylvan and can converse with beasts, which understand your speech while you interpret their sounds and body language. Simple animals can't convey complex ideas, but a friendly one can describe what it saw or heard recently. Gifts can improve a beast's attitude toward you, much as they would with any non-player character.","Spirit Totem":"Starting at 2nd level, you can use a bonus action to conjure an incorporeal spirit at a point you can see within 60 feet, creating a 30-foot-radius aura that lasts 1 minute. A later bonus action can move it up to 60 feet to another visible point. You regain this ability after a short or long rest. Choose bear, hawk, or unicorn: bear grants temporary HP equal to 5 plus your druid level and advantage on Strength checks and saves, hawk lets you spend your reaction to give advantage on attacks against targets in the aura and grants advantage on Perception, and unicorn grants advantage on detecting creatures and lets healing spells you cast restore HP equal to your druid level to chosen allies in the aura.","Mighty Summoner":"At 6th level, beasts and fey you conjure or create with spells gain 2 extra hit points per Hit Die. Their natural weapon damage also counts as magical, so it can get past resistance and immunity to nonmagical attacks.","Guardian Spirit":"Starting at 10th level, when a beast or fey you summoned or created with a spell ends its turn inside your Spirit Totem's aura, that creature regains HP equal to half your druid level.","Faithful Summons":"At 14th level, if you drop to 0 hit points or are incapacitated against your will, you automatically gain the effect of Conjure Animals as if cast with a 9th-level slot, summoning four beasts of CR 2 or lower within 20 feet. They protect you and attack your foes if given no orders, and the effect lasts 1 hour without concentration until you dismiss it. You can use this once per long rest."},
"druid:spores":{"Halo of Spores":"From 2nd level, invisible necrotic spores surround you. When a creature you can see enters or starts its turn within 10 feet, you can use your reaction to deal necrotic damage to it unless it makes a Constitution save against your spell save DC. The damage die grows from d4 to d6 at 6th level, d8 at 10th, and d10 at 14th.","Symbiotic Entity":"At 2nd level, you can spend a Wild Shape use as an action to awaken your spores instead of taking a beast form, gaining temporary hit points equal to 4 times your druid level. For 10 minutes, or until those temporary hit points are gone or you use Wild Shape again, Halo of Spores damage gets an extra roll of its die, and your melee weapon attacks deal an extra 1d6 necrotic damage on hit.","Fungal Infestation":"At 6th level, when a Small or Medium beast or humanoid dies within 10 feet of you, you can use your reaction to reanimate it as a zombie that stands immediately with 1 hit point. It acts right after your turn, obeys your mental commands, can only make one melee attack, and lasts 1 hour before collapsing. You can use this a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum once), and regain all uses on a long rest.","Spreading Spores":"At 10th level, while Symbiotic Entity is active, you can use a bonus action to hurl spores up to 30 feet away, forming a 10-foot cube that lasts 1 minute. Creatures that enter the cube or start their turn there take Halo of Spores damage unless they succeed on a Constitution save against your DC, and a creature can be hit by this only once per turn. You can end the cube early with a bonus action or by creating a new one, but you can't use your Halo of Spores reaction while it persists.","Fungal Body":"At 14th level, the spores within you make you immune to being blinded, deafened, frightened, or poisoned. Critical hits against you count as normal hits instead, unless you are incapacitated."},
"druid:stars":{"Star Map":"At 2nd level you get a Tiny star chart that works as a spellcasting focus, with its form chosen or rolled on a d6 table. While you hold it you know Guidance and have Guiding Bolt prepared without it counting against your prepared spells, and you can cast Guiding Bolt free a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining those uses on a long rest. If lost, a 1-hour ceremony during a short or long rest creates a new map and destroys the old one.","Starry Form":"At 2nd level, spending one Wild Shape use as a bonus action turns you into a luminous starry form instead of a beast, keeping your own statistics. The form casts bright light in a 10-foot radius plus 10 feet of dim light, lasts 10 minutes, and ends early if you dismiss it, become incapacitated, die, or use it again. Each activation lets you pick Archer, which lets you fire a 60-foot radiant arrow for 1d8 plus Wisdom as a bonus action on later turns; Chalice, which lets you or a creature within 30 feet regain 1d8 plus Wisdom HP whenever you cast a healing spell using a slot; or Dragon, which lets you treat a d20 roll of 9 or lower as a 10 when maintaining concentration.","Cosmic Omen":"At 6th level, after each long rest you can consult your star map and roll a d6 to receive an omen that lasts until your next long rest. An even result grants Weal, letting you add a d6 to the roll of a visible creature within 30 feet making an attack, saving throw, or ability check, while an odd result grants Woe, letting you subtract that d6 instead. You can use this reaction a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all uses on a long rest.","Twinkling Constellations":"At 10th level the Archer and Chalice constellations increase their damage or healing die to 2d8, and while Dragon is active you gain a 20-foot flying speed with the ability to hover. You can also switch which constellation glows on your body at the start of each of your turns while in starry form.","Full of Stars":"At 14th level, your partially incorporeal body grants you resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage while you are in your starry form."},
"druid:wildfire":{"Summon Wildfire Spirit":"At 2nd level, you can spend one Wild Shape use as an action to call forth a wildfire spirit instead of taking beast form. Creatures within 10 feet of it (other than you) must pass a Dexterity save against your spell save DC or take 2d6 fire damage. The spirit has 5 + five times your druid level in hit points, uses your proficiency bonus, and acts right after you on initiative, dodging unless you spend a bonus action to direct it. It lasts up to 1 hour, until it drops to 0 hit points, until you summon it again, or until you die.","Enhanced Bond":"At 6th level, while your spirit is summoned, your fire-damage and healing spells gain a bonus. Each time you cast one, roll a d8 and add the result to one damage or healing roll from that spell. Spells with a range beyond self can also originate from either you or the spirit.","Cauterizing Flames":"At 10th level, when a Small or larger creature dies within 30 feet of you or your spirit, a spectral flame appears in its space for 1 minute. When a creature you can see enters that space, you can use your reaction to extinguish the flame and either heal that creature or deal fire damage equal to 2d10 plus your Wisdom modifier. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and uses return after a long rest.","Blazing Revival":"At 14th level, your spirit can save you from dropping. If you fall to 0 hit points while the spirit is within 120 feet, you can force it to drop to 0 hit points instead, letting you recover half your maximum hit points and stand up immediately. You can use this once, and you must finish a long rest before using it again."},
"druid:primeval-ua":{"Keeper of Old":"You become proficient in History. Whenever you make an Intelligence (History) check, you can roll a d4 and add the result to that check. This bonus is a simple add-on that works on any History check you make.","Primeval Companion":"You can spend one Wild Shape use as an action to summon a primeval creature within 30 feet instead of taking a beast form. The companion is friendly, follows your commands, and uses your proficiency bonus in its stats, with 13 + PB natural armor and 5 + 5 hit points per druid level. Its Strike deals 1d8 + PB damage, and its Intercept Attack reaction halves damage aimed at an adjacent ally. It acts right after you on your initiative, only Dodges unless you spend a bonus action to direct a different action, and vanishes at 0 hit points or when you die. Summoning a new one replaces the current one.","Prehistoric Conduit":"Spells you cast with a range other than self can start from your companion instead of you. When your companion must make a saving throw against one of your spells, it rolls with advantage. If a spell would normally halve its damage on a successful save, the companion takes no damage on a success and only half damage on a failure, without any extra effects.","Titanic Bond":"Your companion grows to Large size, and when you summon it you can give it a climbing or swimming speed equal to its walking speed. Once per turn, when you hit a creature with an attack or damage a creature you can see with a spell, you can force that creature to make a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the creature becomes frightened of you until the end of your next turn.","Scourge of the Ancients":"When you use your bonus action to command your companion, you can expend a spell slot of any level to empower it. The companion becomes Huge and gains temporary hit points equal to 10 times the slot's level, or grows to the largest size the space allows. Its Strike adds 1d8 plus the slot level in extra damage on a hit, and its walking speed increases by 5 times the slot level in feet. The boost lasts up to 1 hour, until the companion vanishes, or until you spend another spell slot on this feature."},
"fighter:arcane-archer":{"Arcane Archer Lore":"At 3rd level you gain proficiency in either Arcana or Nature and learn either Prestidigitation or Druidcraft as a cantrip. This gives you a touch of arcane or natural knowledge alongside your archery training.","Arcane Shot":"At 3rd level you know two Arcane Shot options and can add one to an arrow fired from a shortbow or longbow as part of the Attack action, once per turn, choosing when it hits. You have two uses that refresh on a short or long rest. You learn another option at 7th, 10th, 15th, and 18th level, and every option grows stronger at 18th level, with saving throw DCs equal to 8 plus your proficiency bonus plus your Intelligence modifier.","Magic Arrow":"From 7th level you can infuse a nonmagical arrow fired from a shortbow or longbow with magic, letting it overcome resistance and immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage. The enchantment lasts only until the arrow hits or misses its target.","Curving Shot":"At 7th level, if a magic arrow you fire misses, you can spend a bonus action to reroll that attack against a different target within 60 feet of the original target. This lets a wasted shot still find a new victim.","Ever-Ready Shot":"Starting at 15th level, when you roll initiative and have no Arcane Shot uses left, you regain one expended use. This gives you a ready magical arrow at the start of every battle."},
"fighter:banneret":{"Rallying Cry":"Whenever you use Second Wind, you can choose up to three allies within 60 feet. Each chosen ally regains hit points equal to your fighter level, but only if it can see or hear you. Its uses are tied to Second Wind's own once-per-short-rest limit.","Royal Envoy":"At 7th level you become proficient in Persuasion. If you already have that proficiency, you instead gain proficiency in one skill of your choice from Animal Handling, Insight, Intimidation, or Performance. Your proficiency bonus is doubled on any Persuasion check, whichever source gave you the proficiency.","Inspiring Surge":"Starting at 10th level, when you take an Action Surge, you can pick one ally within 60 feet that can see or hear you. That ally can then make one melee or ranged weapon attack using its reaction. At 18th level you can affect two allies instead of one.","Bulwark":"At 15th level, when you spend Indomitable to reroll a failed Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma saving throw while not incapacitated, you can also choose one ally within 60 feet that failed the same effect. If that ally can see or hear you, it rerolls its own save and must keep the new result."},
"fighter:battle-master":{"Combat Superiority":"At 3rd level you learn three maneuvers powered by superiority dice, and you can apply only one maneuver per attack. You gain two more at 7th, 10th, and 15th level, and each time you learn new ones you may swap one you already know. You start with four d8 superiority dice that are spent when used and refreshed on a short or long rest, with an extra die at 7th and 15th level. Some maneuvers force a saving throw with DC 8 + proficiency bonus + your Strength or Dexterity modifier.","Student of War":"At 3rd level you become proficient with one type of artisan's tools of your choice. This gives you a practical skill outside of combat rather than a combat resource.","Know Your Enemy":"Starting at 7th level, after spending at least 1 minute observing or interacting with a creature outside combat, you can learn how it compares to you. Choose two traits from Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, Armor Class, current hit points, total class levels, and fighter class levels, and the DM tells you whether the creature is your equal, superior, or inferior in each. It requires time spent studying the target rather than a limited number of uses.","Improved Combat Superiority":"At 10th level your superiority dice increase from d8s to d10s. At 18th level they improve again to d12s, making each maneuver's bonus damage or effect stronger.","Relentless":"Starting at 15th level, if you roll initiative and have no superiority dice left, you regain one superiority die. This helps you restart your maneuvers when you have run out at the start of a fight."},
"fighter:cavalier":{"Bonus Proficiency":"At 3rd level, you can become proficient in one skill from Animal Handling, History, Insight, Performance, or Persuasion, or instead learn a language of your choice.","Born to the Saddle":"From 3rd level, you have advantage on saves to avoid being thrown from your mount, and a fall of 10 feet or less lets you land on your feet unless incapacitated. Mounting or dismounting costs only 5 feet of movement instead of half your speed.","Unwavering Mark":"From 3rd level, when you hit a creature with a melee attack, you can mark it until the end of your next turn, ending early if you are incapacitated, die, or another creature marks it. A marked foe within 5 feet has disadvantage on attacks against anyone other than you, and if it harms someone besides you, you can make a special melee attack with advantage as a bonus action on your next turn, dealing extra damage equal to half your fighter level on a hit. You can use this special attack a number of times equal to your Strength modifier (minimum once) and regain all uses on a long rest.","Warding Maneuver":"At 7th level, when you or a creature you can see within 5 feet is hit by an attack, you can use a reaction while wielding a melee weapon or shield to roll 1d8 and add it to the attacker's AC against that attack. If the attack still hits, the target takes only resistance to its damage. You can use this a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum once) and regain all uses on a long rest.","Hold the Line":"At 10th level, creatures that move 5 feet or more while within your reach provoke opportunity attacks from you. Hitting a creature with an opportunity attack reduces its speed to 0 until the end of the current turn.","Ferocious Charger":"Starting at 15th level, if you move at least 10 feet in a straight line before hitting a creature with an attack, whether mounted or on foot, that target must succeed on a Strength save against DC 8 plus your proficiency bonus and Strength modifier or be knocked prone. You can use this only once on each of your turns.","Vigilant Defender":"Starting at 18th level, you gain a special reaction that you can use once on every creature's turn except your own. It can only be used to make an opportunity attack, and you cannot use it on the same turn you have used your normal reaction."},
"fighter:champion":{"Improved Critical":"Starting at 3rd level, your weapon attacks crit on a 19 or 20 instead of only a 20, making critical strikes noticeably more frequent. Superior Critical at 15th level expands this further.","Remarkable Athlete":"From 7th level, you add half your proficiency bonus, rounded up, to Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution checks that don't already include it. Your running long jump also covers extra distance equal to your Strength modifier in feet.","Additional Fighting Style":"At 10th level, you pick a second option from the Fighting Style class feature, letting you combine two styles for greater combat versatility.","Superior Critical":"Beginning at 15th level, your weapon attacks crit on any roll of 18, 19, or 20. It builds on Improved Critical and makes landing critical hits far more reliable.","Survivor":"At 18th level, you recover hit points at the start of each of your turns if you are at or below half your maximum. The recovery equals 5 plus your Constitution modifier, but it doesn't trigger while you're at 0 hit points."},
"fighter:echo-knight":{"Manifest Echo":"As a bonus action, you conjure a translucent gray copy of yourself within 15 feet that lasts until it is destroyed, dismissed, replaced, or you are incapacitated. The echo has AC 14 plus your proficiency bonus, 1 hit point, and immunity to all conditions, and you can move it up to 30 feet on your turn without spending an action, but it is destroyed if it ends your turn more than 30 feet away. You can also swap places with it for a bonus action at a cost of 15 feet of movement, attack from either its space or yours, and make opportunity attacks from its position.","Unleash Incarnation":"When you take the Attack action, you can make one extra melee attack from your echo's position. You can use this a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum once), and you regain all uses after a long rest.","Echo Avatar":"Starting at 7th level, you can use an action to perceive the world through your echo's senses, which leaves you blinded and deafened while active. You can keep this up for up to 10 minutes and end it at any moment without an action, and the echo can be as far as 1,000 feet away without being destroyed while you do so.","Shadow Martyr":"Starting at 10th level, when a creature you can see is about to be attacked, you can use your reaction before the attack roll to teleport your echo into an open space within 5 feet of that creature, redirecting the attack onto the echo. You can use this once, then must finish a short or long rest before using it again.","Reclaim Potential":"By 15th level, when damage destroys one of your echoes, you can gain temporary hit points equal to 2d6 plus your Constitution modifier, as long as you have no temporary hit points already. You can use this a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum once), regaining all uses after a long rest.","Legion of One":"At 18th level, you can use a bonus action to create a second echo with Manifest Echo, and both can exist at once. Creating a third echo destroys the first two, and anything you can do from one echo's space you can also do from the other's. Additionally, when you roll initiative with no uses of Unleash Incarnation remaining, you regain one use of it."},
"fighter:eldritch-knight":{"Spellcasting":"Starting at 3rd level, you cast wizard spells using Intelligence, with cantrips, known spells, and spell slots that grow as you level. You begin with two cantrips and three 1st-level spells, most drawn from abjuration or evocation, and gain a third cantrip at 10th level. Expended slots return after a long rest, and your spell save DC is 8 plus your proficiency bonus plus your Intelligence modifier.","Weapon Bond":"At 3rd level, you can spend an hour performing a ritual, which may fit into a short rest, to magically link yourself to a weapon within reach. Once bonded, that weapon can't be taken from you unless you're incapacitated, and as a bonus action you can summon it to your hand if it's on the same plane. You can keep two bonded weapons but summon only one per bonus action, and binding a third means severing one of the existing bonds.","War Magic":"From 7th level, whenever you use your action to cast a cantrip, you can immediately follow up with one weapon attack as a bonus action. This lets you combine a cantrip with a melee strike in the same turn. The trigger is limited to cantrips until Improved War Magic arrives.","Eldritch Strike":"At 10th level, landing a weapon hit on a creature makes it weaker against your magic for a short window. That creature has disadvantage on its next saving throw against one of your spells, provided the save occurs before the end of your following turn.","Arcane Charge":"At 15th level, when you use Action Surge, you can also teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. You may do this either before or after the extra action, giving you added mobility during your burst of activity.","Improved War Magic":"Starting at 18th level, whenever you use your action to cast any spell, not just a cantrip, you can make one weapon attack as a bonus action. This extends the War Magic combination to your full spell repertoire."},
"fighter:psi-warrior":{"Psionic Power":"Starting at 3rd level you gain a pool of d6 psionic dice, equal to twice your proficiency bonus, that fuel your other psionic powers. Spent dice return on a long rest, and as a bonus action you can recover one spent die, but only once per short or long rest. The die size grows to d8 at 5th level, d10 at 11th, and d12 at 17th.","Telekinetic Adept":"At 7th level you unlock two abilities. Psi-Powered Leap lets you grant yourself a flying speed of twice your walking speed as a bonus action, usable once per rest unless you spend a psionic die. Telekinetic Thrust lets a successful Psionic Strike force a Strength save, and on a failed save you can knock the target prone or push it up to 10 feet.","Guarded Mind":"Beginning at 10th level, your mind is hardened by psionic energy, giving you resistance to psychic damage. If you start your turn charmed or frightened, you can spend a psionic die to end every effect on yourself that causes those conditions.","Bulwark of Force":"At 15th level, as a bonus action, you wrap a number of visible creatures within 30 feet of you, up to your Intelligence modifier (minimum one, and you may include yourself), in telekinetic force that grants half cover for 1 minute or until you are incapacitated. You can use this once per long rest, or spend a psionic die to use it again sooner.","Telekinetic Master":"By 18th level you can cast Telekinesis without components, using Intelligence as your spellcasting ability. While concentrating on it, you can make one weapon attack as a bonus action on each of your turns. You can cast it with this feature once per long rest, or spend a psionic die to cast it again."},
"fighter:rune-knight":{"Bonus Proficiencies":"At 3rd level, you become proficient with smith's tools and gain the ability to speak, read, and write Giant. These come from the archetype itself, so you get them once when you pick Rune Knight.","Rune Carver":"Starting at 3rd level, you know two runes from a list of six and can swap one for another whenever you gain a fighter level. After each long rest, you inscribe a different rune on each of up to as many wearable or handheld objects as you have runes known, and each object can carry only one rune. Runes last until your next long rest, and their save DC is 8 + proficiency bonus + Constitution modifier. The number of runes you know rises to three at 7th level, four at 10th, and five at 15th. Cloud, Fire, Frost, and Stone runes are available from the start, while Hill and Storm runes need 7th level. Most runes give passive skill or resistance benefits and a once-per-rest activated effect, such as Fire's burning restraints or Stone's charm.","Giant's Might":"At 3rd level, you can use a bonus action to gain giant-like power for 1 minute. You become Large if you are smaller and have room, you gain advantage on Strength checks and Strength saves, and once per turn one weapon or unarmed hit deals an extra 1d6 damage. You can use this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all uses on a long rest. The bonus damage grows to 1d8 at 10th level and 1d10 at 18th level.","Runic Shield":"At 7th level, you can react when another creature you can see within 60 feet is hit by an attack roll, forcing the attacker to reroll the d20 and use the new result. You can use this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and all uses return when you finish a long rest.","Great Stature":"At 10th level, your runes permanently enlarge you. Roll 3d4 and increase your height by that many inches. This feature also raises the extra damage from Giant's Might to 1d8.","Master of Runes":"At 15th level, you can invoke each rune you know twice between rests instead of once. Expended uses return when you finish either a short or a long rest.","Runic Juggernaut":"At 18th level, the extra damage from Giant's Might rises to 1d10. When you activate that feature, you can grow to Huge size, and while Huge your reach increases by 5 feet."},
"fighter:samurai":{"Bonus Proficiency":"At 3rd level, this archetype lets you become proficient in one skill from History, Insight, Performance, or Persuasion of your choice. Instead, you can learn one language of your choice.","Fighting Spirit":"Starting at 3rd level, you can use a bonus action on your turn to gain advantage on all weapon attack rolls until the end of that turn, along with 5 temporary hit points. The temporary hit points rise to 10 at 10th level and 15 at 15th level. You can use this three times and regain all uses after a long rest.","Elegant Courtier":"Starting at 7th level, add your Wisdom modifier to your Charisma (Persuasion) checks. You also gain proficiency in Wisdom saving throws, or if you already have that, in Intelligence or Charisma saving throws of your choice.","Tireless Spirit":"Starting at 10th level, if you roll initiative and have no Fighting Spirit uses left, you regain one use. This restores a use each time you roll initiative in that situation.","Rapid Strike":"Starting at 15th level, when you take the Attack action and have advantage on an attack roll against a target, you can give up that advantage to make one additional weapon attack against that target as part of the same action. You can do this only once per turn.","Strength Before Death":"Starting at 18th level, if damage reduces you to 0 hit points, you can use your reaction to stay conscious and immediately take an extra turn. Damage during that turn still causes death saving throw failures, and if you are still at 0 hit points when it ends, you fall unconscious. You can use this once, then must finish a long rest before using it again."},
"monk:mercy":{"Implements of Mercy":"At 3rd level you gain proficiency in Insight, Medicine, and the herbalism kit, plus a mask that defines your monastic healer persona. You can design the mask yourself or roll a d6 on a table of options such as a raven, skull, or butterfly. You'll usually wear it when using this subclass's abilities.","Hand of Healing":"Starting at 3rd level, you can spend 1 ki point as an action to touch a creature and restore hit points equal to a Martial Arts die roll plus your Wisdom modifier. When you use Flurry of Blows, you can swap one unarmed strike for this healing without spending ki for it. The Martial Arts die grows with your monk level, which increases the healing you can deliver.","Hand of Harm":"Starting at 3rd level, you can spend 1 ki point when an unarmed strike hits to add necrotic damage equal to a Martial Arts die roll plus your Wisdom modifier. You can apply this only once per turn. The Martial Arts die scales as you advance in monk levels.","Physician's Touch":"Starting at 6th level, your Hands of Healing can also end one disease or one of the following conditions on the target: blinded, deafened, paralyzed, poisoned, or stunned. Your Hands of Harm can instead leave the target poisoned until the end of your next turn. These options add utility to both your healing and harming touches.","Flurry of Healing and Harm":"Starting at 11th level, each unarmed strike in your Flurry of Blows can be replaced with Hands of Healing without spending ki for the healing. You can also use Hands of Harm on a Flurry strike without paying its ki cost. You still can't apply Hands of Harm more than once per turn.","Hand of Ultimate Mercy":"At 17th level, as an action you can touch the corpse of a creature that died within the last 24 hours and spend 5 ki points to bring it back. The creature returns with hit points equal to 4d10 plus your Wisdom modifier, and it wakes free of any blinded, deafened, paralyzed, poisoned, or stunned conditions it had when it died. You can use this ability once, then must finish a long rest before using it again."},
"monk:ascendant-dragon":{"Draconic Disciple":"At 3rd level, you can use your reaction to reroll a failed Charisma (Intimidation) or Charisma (Persuasion) check, but once that reroll turns a failure into a success, you must finish a long rest before using it again. Your unarmed strikes can also deal acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison damage instead of their normal type. You additionally learn Draconic or one other language of your choice.","Breath of the Dragon":"Starting at 3rd level, when you take the Attack action, you can replace one of your attacks with a blast of elemental breath, either a 20-foot cone or a 5-foot-wide, 30-foot line, dealing acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison damage. Creatures in the area make a Dexterity save against your ki save DC, taking two Martial Arts dice of damage on a failure or half on a success. At 11th level the damage rises to three Martial Arts dice. You can use it a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all uses on a long rest, and you can spend 2 ki points to use it once more when you're out of uses.","Wings Unfurled":"At 6th level, when you use Step of the Wind, spectral draconic wings appear on your back and vanish at the end of your turn. While they last, your flying speed equals your walking speed. You can use this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all uses after a long rest.","Aspect of the Wyrm":"At 11th level, as a bonus action, you project a 10-foot draconic aura for 1 minute. You pick either Frightful Presence, which lets you target a creature with a Wisdom save against your ki save DC to frighten it, with you able to target again with a bonus action on later turns, or Resistance, which grants you and allies in the aura resistance to one chosen damage type. After using it, you must finish a long rest before using it again unless you spend 3 ki points to reactivate it.","Ascendant Aspect":"At 17th level, you gain three enhancements. Augment Breath lets you spend 1 ki point to enlarge your Breath of the Dragon to a 60-foot cone or 90-foot line, with four Martial Arts dice of damage. Blindsight extends out to 10 feet, letting you perceive hidden or invisible creatures within that range unless they're behind total cover. Explosive Fury makes creatures you choose in your aura, when you activate it, make a Dexterity save or take 3d10 damage of a type you select."},
"monk:astral-self":{"Arms of the Astral Self":"Spending 1 ki as a bonus action summons spectral arms that last 10 minutes, and each creature you can see within 10 feet must make a Dexterity save or take force damage equal to two Martial Arts dice. While the arms are out, you can use Wisdom for Strength checks and saves, and the arms make unarmed strikes with 5 extra feet of reach, using Wisdom for attack and damage rolls with force damage.","Visage of the Astral Self":"At 6th level, spending 1 ki as a bonus action (or alongside the Arms bonus action) summons a spectral mask for 10 minutes. While it lasts, you can see in magical and nonmagical darkness out to 120 feet, you have advantage on Wisdom (Insight) and Charisma (Intimidation) checks, and you can speak privately to one creature within 60 feet or project your voice to everyone within 600 feet.","Body of the Astral Self":"Starting at 11th level, once both your astral arms and visage are summoned, you can call up a spectral body over your form at no action cost. While it is present, you can use your reaction to reduce acid, cold, fire, force, lightning, or thunder damage by 1d10 plus your Wisdom modifier (never less than 1), and once per turn when your astral arms hit, you deal extra damage equal to your Martial Arts die.","Awakened Astral Self":"Starting at 17th level, spending 5 ki as a bonus action summons the arms, visage, and body together for 10 minutes. While awakened, you gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class, and when your Extra Attack lets you attack twice with your astral arms, you can attack three times instead."},
"monk:drunken-master":{"Bonus Proficiencies":"At 3rd level you become proficient in Performance if you lack it, and in brewer's supplies if you lack that too. These reflect a fighting style that mixes martial discipline with a dancer's precision and a jester's showmanship.","Drunken Technique":"Starting at 3rd level, each time you take the Flurry of Blows action you also get the Disengage action for free. Your walking speed also rises by 10 feet until the end of the turn, letting you slip away after striking.","Tipsy Sway":"Starting at 6th level you gain two swaying tricks. Leap to Your Feet lets you stand up from prone for only 5 feet of movement instead of half your speed. Redirect Attack lets you spend 1 ki point as a reaction when a melee attack misses you, forcing it to hit another creature you can see within 5 feet of you, other than the attacker.","Drunkard's Luck":"Starting at 11th level, when you make an ability check, attack roll, or saving throw with disadvantage, you can spend 2 ki points to cancel that disadvantage for the roll.","Intoxicated Frenzy":"At 17th level, when you take Flurry of Blows you can make up to three extra strikes with it, for a total of five Flurry of Blows attacks. Each of those attacks must target a different creature during the same turn."},
"monk:four-elements":{"Disciple of the Elements":"At 3rd level you learn ki-powered elemental disciplines, starting with Elemental Attunement plus one other discipline of your choice, and each use costs ki points. You gain another discipline at 6th, 11th, and 17th level, and whenever you gain one you can swap out a discipline you already know for a different one. From 5th level, you can spend extra ki to raise the level of a scalable elemental spell you cast, adding one spell level per extra point, with total ki per spell capped at 3 (5th-8th), 4 (9th-12th), 5 (13th-16th), or 6 (17th-20th)."},
"monk:kensei":{"Path of the Kensei":"At 3rd level you train intensely with weapons and gain the Kensei Weapons, Agile Parry, Kensei's Shot, and Way of the Brush benefits. Several of these only work with the kensei weapons you select. The tradition also includes brush training, so you can gain calligraphy or painting skills.","One with the Blade":"At 6th level your ki flows into your kensei weapons, giving you Magic Kensei Weapons and Deft Strike. Together these make your weapon strikes more effective against creatures that resist ordinary attacks and add extra damage when you spend ki.","Sharpen the Blade":"At 11th level, as a bonus action, you can spend up to 3 ki points to give a kensei weapon you touch a bonus to attack and damage rolls equal to the ki spent. The bonus lasts 1 minute or until you use this feature again, and it does nothing for a magic weapon that already has such a bonus.","Unerring Accuracy":"At 17th level, if you miss with an attack roll using a monk weapon on your turn, you can reroll it. You can use this once on each of your turns."},
"monk:long-death":{"Touch of Death":"Starting at 3rd level, whenever you knock a creature within 5 feet of you down to 0 hit points, you siphon life from it and gain temporary hit points. The amount equals your Wisdom modifier plus your monk level, with a minimum of 1. This feature has no listed later-level improvements.","Hour of Reaping":"Beginning at 6th level, you can use an action to project a deathly aura that unnerves nearby foes. Each creature within 30 feet that can see you must make a Wisdom saving throw, and those that fail become frightened of you until the end of your next turn.","Mastery of Death":"From 11th level onward, you can cheat death when you would fall to 0 hit points. Spending 1 ki point requires no action and lets you instead drop to 1 hit point.","Touch of the Long Death":"At 17th level, you can use an action to channel death energy through a touch on a creature within 5 feet. You spend between 1 and 10 ki points, and the target makes a Constitution saving throw. It takes 2d10 necrotic damage for each ki point spent on a failed save, or half that on a success."},
"monk:open-hand":{"Open Hand Technique":"Starting at 3rd level, each Flurry of Blows strike that hits lets you add one rider to the target. It can fall prone after a Dexterity save, get shoved up to 15 feet after failing a Strength save, or be unable to take reactions until the end of your next turn. You pick one rider per hit.","Wholeness of Body":"From 6th level, you can use an action to heal yourself for three times your monk level in hit points. After using it, you must finish a long rest before it works again, so it's a once-per-long-rest healing tool.","Tranquility":"From 11th level, when you finish a long rest, you gain a Sanctuary effect that lasts until your next long rest, though it can still end early as usual. Its save DC is 8 plus your Wisdom modifier plus your proficiency bonus. It refreshes automatically each time you complete a long rest.","Quivering Palm":"At 17th level, when an unarmed strike hits, you can spend 3 ki to plant vibrations in the target that last a number of days equal to your monk level. You can only have one creature affected at a time. Later, using your action while on the same plane forces a Constitution save: failure drops the target to 0 hit points, while success deals 10d10 necrotic damage. You can also end the vibrations harmlessly without using an action."},
"monk:shadow":{"Shadow Arts":"Starting at 3rd level, you can spend 2 ki points as an action to cast Darkness, Darkvision, Pass Without Trace, or Silence without material components. You also learn the Minor Illusion cantrip if you don't already have it. Ki is the resource that limits how often you can use these effects.","Shadow Step":"At 6th level, while you stand in dim light or darkness, you can use a bonus action to teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is also dim or dark. The first melee attack you make after arriving that turn is made with advantage.","Cloak of Shadows":"At 11th level, while you are in dim light or darkness, you can use your action to turn invisible. The invisibility lasts until you attack, cast a spell, or end up in bright light.","Opportunist":"At 17th level, when a creature within 5 feet of you is hit by an attack from someone other than you, you can use your reaction to make a melee attack against that creature. This lets you take advantage of openings created by others' strikes."},
"monk:sun-soul":{"Radiant Sun Bolt":"Starting at 3rd level, you gain a ranged spell attack with a 30-foot range that you can use as part of the Attack action. You add your Dexterity modifier to its attack and damage rolls, and it deals radiant damage using a die that grows with your monk level. Spending 1 ki point lets you fire it twice as a bonus action after taking the Attack action, and once you have Extra Attack, you can use it for any of those attacks.","Searing Arc Strike":"At 6th level, right after you take the Attack action, you can spend 2 ki points as a bonus action to cast Burning Hands. You can spend extra ki to cast it at a higher level, with each additional point raising the spell level by one. Your total ki spent on it cannot exceed half your monk level.","Searing Sunburst":"At 11th level, as an action, you hurl an orb up to 150 feet away that bursts into a 20-foot-radius sphere of radiant light. Each creature inside must make a Constitution saving throw or take 2d6 radiant damage, and creatures behind fully opaque total cover are spared. You can spend up to 3 ki points to add 2d6 damage for each point spent.","Sun Shield":"At 17th level, you are surrounded by a magical aura that sheds bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for another 30 feet. You can turn this light on or off as a bonus action. While it shines, if a creature hits you with a melee attack, you can use your reaction to deal radiant damage to it equal to 5 plus your Wisdom modifier."},
"paladin:ancients":{"Channel Divinity: Nature's Wrath":"At 3rd level you gain two options. Nature's Wrath, used as an action, summons spectral vines that can restrain a creature within 10 feet, and the target can choose Strength or Dexterity to resist; it retries the save at the end of each of its turns. Turn the Faithless, also an action while showing your holy symbol, forces each fey or fiend within 30 feet that can hear you to make a Wisdom save or be driven away for 1 minute or until it takes damage, leaving it unable to approach you, use reactions, or do more than Dash or flee. Illusions or disguises hiding a turned creature's true form are also stripped away.","Channel Divinity: Turn the Faithless":"At 3rd level you gain two options. Nature's Wrath, used as an action, summons spectral vines that can restrain a creature within 10 feet, and the target can choose Strength or Dexterity to resist; it retries the save at the end of each of its turns. Turn the Faithless, also an action while showing your holy symbol, forces each fey or fiend within 30 feet that can hear you to make a Wisdom save or be driven away for 1 minute or until it takes damage, leaving it unable to approach you, use reactions, or do more than Dash or flee. Illusions or disguises hiding a turned creature's true form are also stripped away.","Aura of Warding":"Starting at 7th level, you and friendly creatures within 10 feet of you gain resistance to damage from spells. At 18th level, the radius of this protective aura grows to 30 feet.","Undying Sentinel":"At 15th level, if you would be knocked to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can instead drop to 1 hit point. You must finish a long rest before using this again. You also stop suffering the physical penalties of aging and cannot be aged by magic.","Elder Champion":"At 20th level, you transform into an ancient nature force of your chosen appearance, such as green skin, bark, leafy hair, or antlers, using your action. For 1 minute you regain 10 hit points at the start of each of your turns, can cast any paladin spell with a 1-action casting time as a bonus action, and enemies within 10 feet have disadvantage on saves against your paladin spells and Channel Divinity. You can use this feature once, then must finish a long rest before using it again."},
"paladin:conquest":{"Channel Divinity: Conquering Presence":"Gained at 3rd level, this feature offers two options. Conquering Presence is an action that forces chosen creatures you can see within 30 feet to make a Wisdom save, frightening those who fail for 1 minute and letting them retry at the end of each of their turns. Guided Strike lets you spend Channel Divinity after seeing an attack roll, before the hit or miss is declared, to add +10 to that roll.","Channel Divinity: Guided Strike":"Gained at 3rd level, this feature offers two options. Conquering Presence is an action that forces chosen creatures you can see within 30 feet to make a Wisdom save, frightening those who fail for 1 minute and letting them retry at the end of each of their turns. Guided Strike lets you spend Channel Divinity after seeing an attack roll, before the hit or miss is declared, to add +10 to that roll.","Aura of Conquest":"Beginning at 7th level, you project a menacing 10-foot aura in every direction whenever you aren't incapacitated, which is blocked by total cover. Any creature frightened of you has its speed reduced to 0 while inside the aura and takes psychic damage equal to half your paladin level at the start of its turn there. At 18th level, the aura's radius expands to 30 feet.","Scornful Rebuke":"Starting at 15th level, anyone who strikes you with an attack suffers a psychic backlash. The attacker takes psychic damage equal to your Charisma modifier, with a minimum of 1, as long as you aren't incapacitated.","Invincible Conqueror":"At 20th level, you can use an action to transform into an avatar of conquest for 1 minute. While transformed, you gain resistance to all damage, can make an extra attack whenever you take the Attack action, and score critical hits on melee weapon attacks with a roll of 19 or 20. Once used, you must finish a long rest before using it again."},
"paladin:crown":{"Channel Divinity: Champion Challenge":"At 3rd level, this oath gives you two Channel Divinity options used as bonus actions. Champion Challenge forces creatures within 30 feet that fail a Wisdom save to stay within 30 feet of you, while Turn the Tide heals wounded allies who can hear you within 30 feet by 1d6 plus your Charisma modifier (minimum 1) if they are at half their hit points or less.","Channel Divinity: Turn the Tide":"At 3rd level, this oath gives you two Channel Divinity options used as bonus actions. Champion Challenge forces creatures within 30 feet that fail a Wisdom save to stay within 30 feet of you, while Turn the Tide heals wounded allies who can hear you within 30 feet by 1d6 plus your Charisma modifier (minimum 1) if they are at half their hit points or less.","Divine Allegiance":"Starting at 7th level, you can use your reaction when a creature within 5 feet of you takes damage to take that damage yourself, so the creature takes none. The damage you absorb can't be reduced or prevented in any way.","Unyielding Saint":"Starting at 15th level, you have advantage on saving throws made to avoid being paralyzed or stunned.","Exalted Champion":"At 20th level, you can use your action to enter a empowered state lasting 1 hour. During it, you resist bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage from nonmagical weapons, your allies within 30 feet have advantage on death saving throws, and you and those allies have advantage on Wisdom saving throws. The effect ends early if you are incapacitated or die, and you must finish a long rest before using it again."},
"paladin:devotion":{"Channel Divinity: Sacred Weapon":"At 3rd level you gain two options that use your Channel Divinity. Sacred Weapon, as an action, charges a held weapon with radiant energy, adding your Charisma modifier (minimum +1) to its attack rolls for a minute and making it shed bright light in a 20-foot radius plus 20 feet of dim light. Turn the Unholy, as an action with your holy symbol, forces fiends and undead within 30 feet that can see or hear you to make a Wisdom save, and those who fail flee from you, lose their reactions, and can only Dash or escape for a minute or until they take damage.","Channel Divinity: Turn the Unholy":"At 3rd level you gain two options that use your Channel Divinity. Sacred Weapon, as an action, charges a held weapon with radiant energy, adding your Charisma modifier (minimum +1) to its attack rolls for a minute and making it shed bright light in a 20-foot radius plus 20 feet of dim light. Turn the Unholy, as an action with your holy symbol, forces fiends and undead within 30 feet that can see or hear you to make a Wisdom save, and those who fail flee from you, lose their reactions, and can only Dash or escape for a minute or until they take damage.","Aura of Devotion":"From 7th level, you and friendly creatures within 10 feet of you cannot be charmed while you remain conscious. At 18th level, the protected radius expands to 30 feet.","Purity of Spirit":"Starting at 15th level, you always have Protection from Evil and Good active on yourself. You never need to cast it or spend a spell slot to keep that safeguard running.","Holy Nimbus":"At 20th level, as an action, you radiate sunlight for 1 minute, with bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light extending 30 feet beyond. Each enemy that begins its turn in the bright light takes 10 radiant damage, and you gain advantage on saves against spells cast by fiends or undead while it lasts. Once used, it returns only after you complete a long rest."},
"paladin:glory":{"Channel Divinity: Peerless Athlete":"As a bonus action, spend a Channel Divinity use to sharpen your physique for 10 minutes. You gain advantage on Strength (Athletics) and Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks, double your carrying, pushing, dragging, and lifting capacity, and add 10 feet to your long and high jumps, which still costs normal movement.","Channel Divinity: Inspiring Smite":"Right after you deal damage with Divine Smite, you can spend a Channel Divinity use as a bonus action to hand out temporary hit points to creatures within 30 feet, including yourself. The pool equals 2d8 plus your paladin level, and you choose how to split it among them.","Aura of Alacrity":"Starting at 7th level, your walking speed increases by 10 feet, and each ally that begins its turn within 5 feet of you gets the same 10-foot boost until that turn ends, as long as you aren't incapacitated. At 18th level, the aura's range grows to 10 feet.","Glorious Defense":"At 15th level, when you or a visible creature within 10 feet is hit by an attack roll, you can use your reaction to add a bonus to that target's AC equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum +1), which may turn the hit into a miss. If the attack misses and the attacker is within your weapon's range, you can make one weapon attack against it as part of the same reaction. You can use this a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum once), and all uses return after a long rest.","Living Legend":"At 20th level, as a bonus action, you gain 1 minute of heroic presence: advantage on all Charisma checks, the ability once per turn to turn a missed weapon attack into a hit, and a reaction to reroll a failed saving throw, which you must then use. You can use this once per long rest, or spend a 5th-level spell slot to use it again."},
"paladin:redemption":{"Channel Divinity: Emissary of Peace":"Gained at 3rd level, this lets you choose one of two options. Emissary of Peace is a bonus action that gives you +5 to Charisma (Persuasion) checks for 10 minutes. Rebuke the Violent is a reaction you use after an attacker within 30 feet damages a creature other than you, forcing a Wisdom save where failure means radiant damage equal to what it just dealt, and success halves that.","Channel Divinity: Rebuke the Violent":"Gained at 3rd level, this lets you choose one of two options. Emissary of Peace is a bonus action that gives you +5 to Charisma (Persuasion) checks for 10 minutes. Rebuke the Violent is a reaction you use after an attacker within 30 feet damages a creature other than you, forcing a Wisdom save where failure means radiant damage equal to what it just dealt, and success halves that.","Aura of the Guardian":"Starting at 7th level, you can use your reaction to take on damage that would hit a creature within 10 feet of you, so you suffer it instead. Other effects that come with the damage don't pass to you, and you can't reduce that damage in any way. At 18th level, the aura's range grows to 30 feet.","Protective Spirit":"Beginning at 15th level, you recover hit points during combat if you end your turn conscious and with less than half your hit points left. The healing equals 1d6 plus half your paladin level.","Emissary of Redemption":"At 20th level, you become resistant to all damage from other creatures, and any creature that hits you with an attack takes radiant damage equal to half the damage you took from it. If you attack, damage, or cast a spell on a creature, these benefits stop applying against that creature until you finish a long rest."},
"paladin:vengeance":{"Channel Divinity: Abjure Enemy":"At 3rd level, this oath grants two Channel Divinity options. Abjure Enemy takes an action and targets a visible creature within 60 feet, which makes a Wisdom save (fiends and undead roll at disadvantage): on a failure it is frightened and its speed drops to 0 for a minute or until it takes damage, while on a success its speed is only halved. Vow of Enmity is a bonus action aimed at a visible creature within 10 feet, giving you advantage on attacks against it for a minute or until it drops to 0 hit points or falls unconscious.","Channel Divinity: Vow of Enmity":"At 3rd level, this oath grants two Channel Divinity options. Abjure Enemy takes an action and targets a visible creature within 60 feet, which makes a Wisdom save (fiends and undead roll at disadvantage): on a failure it is frightened and its speed drops to 0 for a minute or until it takes damage, while on a success its speed is only halved. Vow of Enmity is a bonus action aimed at a visible creature within 10 feet, giving you advantage on attacks against it for a minute or until it drops to 0 hit points or falls unconscious.","Relentless Avenger":"Starting at 7th level, when an opportunity attack hits a creature, you can immediately move up to half your speed as part of that same reaction. That movement does not provoke opportunity attacks, so you can keep a fleeing foe from escaping.","Soul of Vengeance":"At 15th level, your Vow of Enmity grows more dangerous. Whenever a creature under its effect attacks, you can use your reaction to make a melee weapon attack against that creature, as long as it is within your weapon's reach.","Avenging Angel":"At 20th level, you can use your action to transform for one hour. Wings grow from your back, giving you a 60-foot flying speed, and you project a 30-foot aura of menace. Enemies that enter the aura or start their turn in it must succeed on a Wisdom save or be frightened for a minute, and attacks against frightened creatures have advantage. You can use this transformation once, and you regain that use after a long rest."},
"paladin:watchers":{"Channel Divinity: Watcher's Will":"Spending one Channel Divinity use as an action lets you bolster up to your Charisma modifier (minimum one) visible creatures within 30 feet, plus yourself. For 1 minute, you and those chosen allies have advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws. The effect's targets and duration don't scale with level.","Channel Divinity: Abjure the Extraplanar":"As an action, you display your holy symbol to force each aberration, celestial, elemental, fey, or fiend within 30 feet that can hear you to make a Wisdom save. A failed save leaves the creature turned for 1 minute or until it takes damage, and it must flee to get 30+ feet from you. A turned creature can only Dash or try to escape restraints, and if it can't move, it Dodges instead. This costs one Channel Divinity use.","Aura of the Sentinel":"While you're not incapacitated, you radiate alertness that helps you and chosen creatures within 10 feet when initiative is rolled, granting each a bonus equal to your proficiency bonus. At 18th level, the aura's radius expands to 30 feet. The bonus grows automatically with your proficiency bonus as you level.","Vigilant Rebuke":"Starting at 15th level, when you or a creature you can see within 30 feet succeeds on an Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma saving throw, you can use your reaction to strike back at the creature that caused the save. That creature takes 2d8 plus your Charisma modifier in force damage. It's usable whenever the triggering save succeeds, with no stated per-rest limit.","Mortal Bulwark":"At 20th level, a bonus action grants you divine power for 1 minute: truesight out to 120 feet, advantage on attacks against aberrations, celestials, elementals, fey, and fiends, and a banishment effect on your hits. When you damage a creature with an attack, it must make a Charisma save against your spell save DC or be sent back to its native plane if it's elsewhere. Creatures that succeed are immune to this for 24 hours. You regain the use on a long rest, or by expending a 5th-level spell slot."},
"paladin:oathbreaker":{"Channel Divinity: Control Undead":"At 3rd level you choose from two Channel Divinity options: Control Undead, which can force one nearby undead to obey you for 24 hours on a failed Wisdom save, and Dreadful Aspect, which frightens nearby foes who can see you for 1 minute. Undead with a challenge rating at or above your paladin level resist Control Undead entirely. Each use spends your Channel Divinity, which normally recharges on a rest.","Channel Divinity: Dreadful Aspect":"At 3rd level you choose from two Channel Divinity options: Control Undead, which can force one nearby undead to obey you for 24 hours on a failed Wisdom save, and Dreadful Aspect, which frightens nearby foes who can see you for 1 minute. Undead with a challenge rating at or above your paladin level resist Control Undead entirely. Each use spends your Channel Divinity, which normally recharges on a rest.","Aura of Hate":"From 7th level, you and fiends or undead within 10 feet add your Charisma modifier (minimum +1) to melee weapon damage rolls. The aura's radius grows to 30 feet at 18th level. A creature can only benefit from one paladin's aura at a time.","Supernatural Resistance":"At 15th level, you resist bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage from nonmagical weapons. This makes ordinary blades and blunt weapons far less effective against you.","Dread Lord":"At 20th level, you can spend an action to create a 30-foot gloom aura lasting 1 minute that dims bright light to dim light. Enemies frightened of you take 4d10 psychic damage at the start of their turn inside it, and you and chosen allies gain shadow cover that gives sight-reliant attackers disadvantage against you. While the aura lasts, a bonus action lets you make a melee spell attack to lash shadows at a target for 3d10 plus your Charisma modifier necrotic damage on a hit. You can activate the aura once per long rest."},
"ranger:beast-master":{"Ranger's Companion":"At 3rd level you bond with a beast of Medium size or smaller with a challenge rating of 1/4 or lower, and your proficiency bonus raises its AC, attacks, damage, and proficient saves and skills. Its hit point maximum is the higher of its normal value or four times your ranger level. It acts on your initiative, follows your verbal movement and Attack, Dash, Disengage, or Help commands, and takes Dodge if you give no order. At 5th level, when you command it to Attack, you can also make one weapon attack yourself, and if you die or are absent it acts independently, protecting you and itself. If it dies, an 8-hour magical bonding ritual with a willing beast gets you a new one.","Exceptional Training":"Starting at 7th level, on any turn your beast doesn't attack, you can spend a bonus action to order it to Dash, Disengage, or Help. Its attacks also count as magical, so they get past resistance and immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage. This makes your companion effective against creatures that shrug off ordinary weapons.","Bestial Fury":"Beginning at 11th level, when you order your beast to take the Attack action, it can make two attacks in that action. If the beast already has the Multiattack action, it can use that instead. This sharply increases its damage output in the fights where you commit it to attacking.","Share Spells":"At 15th level, when you cast a spell that targets only you, you can also apply its effect to your beast if the beast is within 30 feet of you. This lets your companion benefit from your buffs and healing without using additional spell slots."},
"ranger:drakewarden":{"Draconic Gift":"At 3rd level, your bond with your drake grants you a ranger-usable Thaumaturgy cantrip and the ability to speak, read, and write Draconic or one language of your choice. These benefits expand your magical utility and linguistic reach from the moment you gain the feature.","Drake Companion":"Starting at 3rd level, you can use an action to summon your drake into an open space within 30 feet, and it stays until it drops to 0 hit points, you summon it again, or you die. You can summon it once per long rest, or spend a 1st-level or higher spell slot to summon it again sooner. Its hit points scale as 5 plus five times your ranger level, its Bite uses your proficiency bonus, and it acts right after your turn, taking only the Dodge action unless you spend a bonus action to direct it. Its Infused Strikes reaction adds an extra 1d6 of its chosen damage type when a creature it can see within 30 feet lands a weapon attack.","Bond of Fang and Scale":"At 7th level, your summoned drake gains wings and a flying speed equal to its walking speed, and it grows to Medium size so you can ride it if you are Medium or smaller. While it is summoned, its Bite deals an extra 1d6 of its essence damage type, and you gain resistance to that same damage type. The flying speed does not function while you are riding it.","Drake's Breath":"At 11th level, you can use an action to unleash a 30-foot cone of acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison breath, or have your drake exhale it. Creatures in the cone make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 8d6 damage on a failed save or half on a success, rising to 10d6 at 15th level. You can use it once per long rest, or spend a 3rd-level or higher spell slot to use it again.","Perfected Bond":"At 15th level, your summoned drake's Bite deals an additional 1d6 of its essence damage, for 2d6 extra in total, and the drake grows to Large size. You can now ride it while it uses its flying speed. You can also use your reaction to grant yourself or the drake resistance to a single instance of damage while you are within 30 feet of each other, a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest."},
"ranger:fey-wanderer":{"Dreadful Strikes":"Starting at 3rd level, when you hit with a weapon you can add 1d4 psychic damage to the target, but only once per turn. The damage die grows to 1d6 at 11th level in this class.","Otherworldly Glamour":"Starting at 3rd level, every Charisma check you make gains a bonus equal to your Wisdom modifier, with a minimum bonus of +1. You also become proficient in one skill of your choice from Deception, Performance, or Persuasion.","Beguiling Twist":"From 7th level, you have advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened. When you or a visible creature within 120 feet succeeds on such a save, you can use your reaction to force another visible creature within 120 feet to make a Wisdom save against your spell save DC. On a failure, that creature is charmed or frightened by you for 1 minute, and it can end the effect with a successful save at the end of each of its turns.","Fey Reinforcements":"At 11th level you know Summon Fey, which doesn't count against your known ranger spells, and you can cast it without a material component. You can also cast it once per long rest without a spell slot. When you cast it, you may choose to remove the concentration requirement, which changes its duration to 1 minute for that casting.","Misty Wanderer":"At 15th level you can cast Misty Step without expending a spell slot, a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum once) per long rest. Whenever you cast Misty Step, you can also bring one willing creature you can see within 5 feet of you, which then appears within 5 feet of your destination."},
"ranger:gloom-stalker":{"Dread Ambusher":"At 3rd level you add your Wisdom modifier to your initiative rolls. At the start of your first turn in each combat, your walking speed rises by 10 feet until that turn ends. If you take the Attack action that turn, you can make one extra weapon attack, and a hit deals an additional 1d8 damage of the weapon's type.","Umbral Sight":"At 3rd level you gain darkvision out to 60 feet, or if you already have racial darkvision, its range grows by 30 feet. While you stand in darkness, creatures that rely on darkvision to see you there cannot perceive you, so you are effectively invisible to them.","Iron Mind":"At 7th level you gain proficiency in Wisdom saving throws. If you already have that proficiency, you choose to gain proficiency in either Intelligence or Charisma saving throws instead.","Stalker's Flurry":"At 11th level, once on each of your turns, if a weapon attack misses, you can immediately make another weapon attack as part of the same Attack action. This lets a miss turn into a second strike.","Shadowy Dodge":"Starting at 15th level, you can use your reaction to surround yourself with shadowy wisps when a creature attacks you without advantage, forcing that attacker to roll with disadvantage. You must choose to use this before you learn whether the attack roll hits or misses."},
"ranger:horizon-walker":{"Detect Portal":"At 3rd level, as an action, you sense the direction and distance to the closest planar portal within 1 mile. You can use it once, then must finish a short or long rest before using it again.","Planar Warrior":"At 3rd level, as a bonus action, you mark a creature you can see within 30 feet. Your next weapon hit on that creature this turn converts all its damage to force and adds 1d8 extra force damage, which grows to 2d8 at 11th ranger level.","Ethereal Step":"At 7th level, as a bonus action on your turn, you cast Etherealness without spending a spell slot, but it lasts only until the end of that turn. You can use it once, then must finish a short or long rest to use it again.","Distant Strike":"At 11th level, when you take the Attack action, you can teleport up to 10 feet before each attack to an unoccupied space you can see. If you attack at least two different creatures with that action, you can make one additional attack against a third creature.","Spectral Defense":"At 15th level, when you take damage from an attack, you can use your reaction to gain resistance to all of that attack's damage for the rest of the turn, letting you slip partly out of the planes to blunt the blow."},
"ranger:hunter":{"Multiattack":"After a creature hits you, you gain a +4 bonus to AC against that same creature's later attacks for the rest of the current turn. It shields you from a single heavy hitter that keeps swinging at you."},
"ranger:monster-slayer":{"Hunter's Sense":"As an action, you can study a creature you see within 60 feet to instantly learn its damage immunities, resistances, and vulnerabilities. Creatures shielded from divination appear to have none. You can use this a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum one), and you regain all uses after a long rest.","Slayer's Prey":"As a bonus action, you mark a visible creature within 60 feet, and the first time each turn you hit it with a weapon attack, that attack deals an extra 1d6 damage. The mark lasts until you finish a short or long rest, and marking a different creature ends it early.","Supernatural Defense":"At 7th level, you become tougher against your marked prey. You add 1d6 to saving throws it forces you to make and to ability checks you make to escape its grapple.","Magic-User's Nemesis":"At 11th level, when a creature within 60 feet casts a spell or teleports, you can use your reaction to disrupt it. The creature must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC, or its spell or teleport fails and is wasted. You can use this once, then must finish a short or long rest before using it again.","Slayer's Counter":"At 15th level, when your prey forces you to make a saving throw, you can use your reaction to make one weapon attack against it right before the save. If that attack hits, the save succeeds automatically, and the attack's normal effects still apply."},
"ranger:swarmkeeper":{"Gathered Swarm":"Starting at 3rd level, a swarm of nature spirits stays with you while you live and can join your attacks. Once per turn, right after you hit with an attack, you can have the swarm deal 1d6 piercing damage to the target, or force a target that fails a Strength save against your spell save DC to be pushed up to 15 feet, or push yourself 5 feet. At 11th level the damage increases to 1d8 and the swarm can knock pushed targets prone.","Writhing Tide":"Beginning at 7th level, you can gather part of your swarm beneath you as a bonus action to gain a 10-foot flying speed and the ability to hover for up to 1 minute, or until you are incapacitated. You can use this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all expended uses after a long rest.","Mighty Swarm":"At 11th level, your Gathered Swarm grows stronger in several ways. Its damage increases to 1d8, a failed push can also knock the target prone, and when the swarm moves you, you gain half cover until the start of your next turn.","Swarming Dispersal":"At 15th level, when you take damage you can use your reaction to gain resistance to that damage and dissolve into your swarm, then reappear in an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet. You can use this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all expended uses after a long rest."},
"rogue:arcane-trickster":{"Spellcasting":"Starting at 3rd level, you can cast wizard spells using Intelligence, beginning with three cantrips including Mage Hand. Your spell slots and known spells grow with level, and you regain all expended slots after a long rest. You gain another wizard cantrip at 10th level, and your spell save DC and attack bonus scale with your proficiency bonus and Intelligence modifier.","Mage Hand Legerdemain":"From 3rd level, your Mage Hand can turn invisible and take on extra jobs, such as slipping an item into or pulling one out of another creature's gear and picking locks or disarming traps from a distance with thieves' tools. Doing a covert task requires a Sleight of Hand check contested by the target's Perception. You can also use your Cunning Action bonus action to move the hand.","Magical Ambush":"Beginning at 9th level, if a creature can't see you when you cast a spell at it, that creature makes its saving throw against the spell with disadvantage for the rest of that turn. This works as a stealth-based boost for your offensive spells.","Versatile Trickster":"At 13th level, you can use a bonus action on your turn to mark a creature within 5 feet of your spectral hand. Until the end of that turn, you have advantage on attack rolls against the marked creature. This can be used once per turn, as long as your Mage Hand is still active nearby.","Spell Thief":"At 17th level, you can use your reaction right after a creature casts a spell targeting you or including you in its area, forcing that caster to make a saving throw against your spell save DC. If it fails, the spell is negated against you and you learn it for 8 hours, able to cast it with your own slots, while the caster cannot. You can use this once until you finish a long rest."},
"rogue:assassin":{"Bonus Proficiencies":"Taking this path at 3rd level trains you in the disguise kit and the poisoner's kit, so you can craft convincing disguises and prepare toxins for your work.","Assassinate":"Starting at 3rd level, you gain an edge against foes who have not yet acted in a fight, with advantage on attacks against them. Any hit you land on a surprised creature also counts as a critical hit.","Infiltration Expertise":"From 9th level, you can build a fabricated identity covering a false history, profession, and contacts by spending seven days and 25 gp, but you cannot impersonate a real person. Once established, you can adopt that identity as a disguise, and observers accept it as genuine until they get an obvious reason to doubt you.","Impostor":"At 13th level, after studying a person's speech, handwriting, and mannerisms for at least three hours, you can imitate them with near-perfect accuracy. If a wary creature becomes suspicious, you gain advantage on Charisma (Deception) checks to keep your ruse from being discovered.","Death Strike":"At 17th level, hitting a surprised creature forces it to make a Constitution saving throw against DC 8 plus your Dexterity modifier plus your proficiency bonus. If it fails, your attack deals double damage."},
"rogue:inquisitive":{"Ear for Deceit":"Starting at 3rd level, your ear for lies makes Wisdom (Insight) checks to catch deception more reliable. Any d20 roll of 7 or lower on those checks counts as an 8 instead. This raises the floor on your lie-detection rolls without changing the high end.","Eye for Detail":"From 3rd level, you can spend a bonus action to make a Wisdom (Perception) check to spot something hidden, or an Intelligence (Investigation) check to uncover or decode clues. This lets you search and analyze quickly alongside your other actions in a turn.","Insightful Fighting":"At 3rd level, as a bonus action, you make a Wisdom (Insight) check against a visible, non-incapacitated creature, opposed by its Charisma (Deception) check. On a success, you can use Sneak Attack on that target even without advantage on the attack, though disadvantage still blocks it. The effect lasts 1 minute or until you use it successfully on a different target.","Steady Eye":"At 9th level, you gain advantage on Wisdom (Perception) and Intelligence (Investigation) checks if you move no more than half your speed during that turn. Staying mostly still lets you study your surroundings with sharper focus.","Unerring Eye":"At 13th level, as an action, you sense illusions, shapechangers in disguise, and other deceptive magic within 30 feet, as long as you are not blinded or deafened. You learn that something is trying to fool you, but not what is hidden or its true form. You can use this a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum once), regaining all uses after a long rest.","Eye for Weakness":"At 17th level, while Insightful Fighting applies to a creature, your Sneak Attack damage against that creature increases by 3d6. This makes your studied targets far more vulnerable to your strikes."},
"rogue:mastermind":{"Master of Intrigue":"At 3rd level you gain proficiency with a disguise kit, a forgery kit, and one gaming set of your choice, plus two languages. After hearing a creature speak for at least 1 minute, you can copy its accent and speech patterns flawlessly, letting you pass as a native of a region whose language you know.","Master of Tactics":"Starting at 3rd level, you can take the Help action as a bonus action. When you use Help to aid an ally's attack, the target can be up to 30 feet away from you instead of 5, as long as it can see or hear you.","Insightful Manipulator":"At 9th level, spending at least 1 minute watching or talking with a creature outside combat reveals how it compares to you. Choose two of its Intelligence, Wisdom, Charisma, or class levels, and the DM tells you whether it is your equal, superior, or inferior in each. The DM may also let you learn a piece of its history or one of its personality traits.","Misdirection":"Beginning at 13th level, you can make an attack aimed at you strike a nearby ally instead. When an attacker targets you and a creature within 5 feet provides you cover from that attack, you can use your reaction to redirect the attack onto that creature.","Soul of Deceit":"At 17th level, telepathy and similar mind-reading effects cannot read your thoughts unless you permit it, and you can plant false thoughts by making a Charisma (Deception) check opposed by the reader's Wisdom (Insight) check. Magic that detects lies will show you as truthful whenever you choose, and magic cannot force you to tell the truth."},
"rogue:phantom":{"Whispers of the Dead":"Starting at 3rd level, you can gain one skill or tool proficiency of your choice each time you finish a short or long rest, drawn from spectral knowledge. Choosing a new proficiency you lack causes you to lose the previous one. This lets your set of proficiencies shift over time as you rest.","Wails from the Grave":"At 3rd level, immediately after you deal Sneak Attack damage to a creature on your turn, you can strike a second creature you can see within 30 feet of the first with necrotic damage. The damage equals a roll of half your Sneak Attack dice for your level, rounded up. You can use this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all uses on a long rest. At 17th level, the necrotic damage applies to both the first and second creatures.","Tokens of the Departed":"At 9th level, as a reaction when a creature you can see dies within 30 feet of you, a Tiny soul trinket appears in your free hand. You can hold up to a number of trinkets equal to your proficiency bonus, and you can't create one while at that maximum. While carrying one, you have advantage on death saves and Constitution saves; destroying one on your person when you deal Sneak Attack damage triggers Wails from the Grave without using a charge; and as an action you can destroy one anywhere to ask its spirit a single question.","Ghost Walk":"At 13th level, as a bonus action, you take a spectral form for up to 10 minutes or until you end it with another bonus action. In this form you gain a 10-foot flying speed, can hover, and attackers have disadvantage against you. You can pass through creatures and objects as difficult terrain, but take 1d10 force damage if you end your turn inside one, and you regain use after a long rest or by destroying a soul trinket as part of activating it.","Death's Friend":"At 17th level, your bond with death deepens in two ways. Your Wails from the Grave now deals its necrotic damage to both the first and second creature. Additionally, at the end of each long rest, a soul trinket appears in your hand if you currently have none."},
"rogue:scout":{"Skirmisher":"Starting at 3rd level, you can respond when an enemy ends its turn within 5 feet of you by moving up to half your speed. That repositioning does not provoke opportunity attacks, so you can slip out of melee reach without taking a hit.","Survivalist":"At 3rd level you become proficient in Nature and Survival if you aren't already. For any check using either skill, your proficiency bonus is doubled, which makes tracking, foraging, and wilderness lore especially reliable.","Superior Mobility":"At 9th level, your walking speed rises by 10 feet. If you also have a climbing or swimming speed, that speed gets the same 10-foot boost, making overland travel and water or cliff crossings faster.","Ambush Master":"From 13th level, you roll initiative with advantage, so you usually act first. During the opening round, the first creature you hit becomes easier for everyone to strike, since attacks against it have advantage until the start of your next turn.","Sudden Strike":"At 17th level, when you take the Attack action on your turn, you can make one extra attack as a bonus action. That bonus attack can use your Sneak Attack even if you already used it this turn, but you still cannot apply Sneak Attack to the same target more than once per turn."},
"rogue:soulknife":{"Psionic Power":"Starting at 3rd level, you gain a pool of Psionic Energy dice, each a d6, equal to twice your proficiency bonus, which fuel your other psionic powers. Spent dice return on a long rest, and once per short or long rest, a bonus action restores one spent die. The die size grows to d8 at 5th level, d10 at 11th, and d12 at 17th.","Psychic Blades":"When you take the Attack action, you can conjure a simple, finesse, thrown psychic blade in your free hand with a 60-foot normal range. A hit deals 1d6 psychic damage plus the ability modifier used for the attack, and the blade vanishes after attacking. With a bonus action, if your other hand is free, you can conjure and throw a second blade that deals 1d4 damage.","Soul Blades":"Starting at 9th level, your Psychic Blades gain two psionic powers that draw on your dice: Homing Strikes, which can rescue a missed blade attack, and Psychic Teleportation, which lets you jump to a spot where you throw a blade.","Psychic Veil":"At 13th level, you can make yourself and your belongings invisible as an action for up to one hour, and you can end this at will. The effect breaks early if you deal damage to a creature or force a creature to make a saving throw. You can use it once per long rest, or spend a Psionic Energy die to use it again.","Rend Mind":"At 17th level, when your Psychic Blades deal Sneak Attack damage, you can force the target to make a Wisdom saving throw against 8 plus your proficiency bonus plus your Dexterity modifier. On a failure, the target is stunned for a minute and can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns to end it. You can use this once per long rest, or spend three Psionic Energy dice to use it again."},
"rogue:swashbuckler":{"Fancy Footwork":"Starting at 3rd level, when you make a melee attack on your turn, the target loses its ability to make opportunity attacks against you for the rest of that turn. You can use this on every turn you attack in melee, so it works as a repeatable hit-and-retreat tool.","Rakish Audacity":"At 3rd level, you add your Charisma modifier to your initiative rolls. You also gain a second route to Sneak Attack: you can use it without advantage on the attack roll if you are within 5 feet of the target, no other enemy is within 5 feet of you, and you don't have disadvantage on that attack. All other Sneak Attack rules still apply.","Panache":"At 9th level, you can take an action to make a Charisma (Persuasion) check against a creature's Wisdom (Insight) check, provided it can hear you and you share a language. Against a hostile creature, a win makes it have disadvantage on attacks against anyone but you and stops it from making opportunity attacks against others for 1 minute, ending early if an ally attacks or spells it or if you get more than 60 feet apart. Against a non-hostile creature, a win charms it for 1 minute so it sees you as a friendly acquaintance, ending if you or your allies harm it.","Elegant Maneuver":"Starting at 13th level, you can use a bonus action on your turn to gain advantage on the next Dexterity (Acrobatics) or Strength (Athletics) check you make that same turn. This makes it easy to ensure key athletic or agility checks succeed when you need them.","Master Duelist":"Beginning at 17th level, when you miss with an attack roll, you can roll it again with advantage, turning a miss into a likely hit. You can use this once, then it stays unavailable until you finish a short or long rest."},
"rogue:thief":{"Fast Hands":"Beginning at 3rd level, you can spend the bonus action from Cunning Action on a Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check, on using thieves' tools to disarm a trap or pick a lock, or on the Use an Object action. This lets one bonus action cover several tricky tasks.","Second-Story Work":"At 3rd level, climbing no longer eats into your movement, so you climb at your normal speed. Your running long jumps also reach farther, adding feet equal to your Dexterity modifier to the distance covered.","Supreme Sneak":"Starting at 9th level, you gain advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks on any turn where you move no more than half your speed. Slow, deliberate movement becomes your best way to stay hidden.","Use Magic Device":"At 13th level, your grasp of how magic works lets you improvise with items that aren't meant for you. You ignore class, race, and level requirements for using magic items.","Thief's Reflexes":"At 17th level, you can take two turns in the first round of any combat: one at your normal initiative and another at initiative minus 10. This doesn't function if you're surprised. It makes ambushes and quick escapes far more dangerous."},
"sorcerer:aberrant-mind":{"Telepathic Speech":"As a bonus action, you can open a mental link with one creature you can see within 30 feet, and you can converse through it as long as you're within a number of miles equal to your Charisma modifier (at least 1). Both of you must share a language to understand each other. The link lasts a number of minutes equal to your sorcerer level and ends early if you're incapacitated, die, or create a link with someone else.","Psionic Sorcery":"Starting at 6th level, you can cast your psionic spells of 1st level or higher by spending sorcery points equal to the spell's level instead of using a spell slot. Spells cast this way need no verbal or somatic components, and no material components unless the spell consumes them.","Psychic Defenses":"At 6th level, you resist psychic damage and make saving throws against being charmed or frightened with advantage.","Revelation in Flesh":"Starting at 14th level, you can use a bonus action to spend sorcery points and transform your body for 10 minutes, with each point spent unlocking one option: seeing invisible creatures within 60 feet that aren't behind total cover, gaining a hovering flying speed equal to your walking speed, gaining a swimming speed of twice your walking speed with the ability to breathe water, or becoming slimy and pliable enough to slip through 1-inch gaps and escape restraints or grapples by spending 5 feet of movement.","Warping Implosion":"At 18th level, you can use an action to teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 120 feet. Creatures within 30 feet of where you vanished must make a Strength save against your spell save DC, taking 3d10 force damage and being pulled toward your old space on a failure, or half damage with no pull on a success. You can use this once per long rest, or spend 5 sorcery points to use it again."},
"sorcerer:clockwork-soul":{"Restore Balance":"Starting at 1st level, you can use your reaction to stop a creature you can see within 60 feet from rolling a d20 with advantage or disadvantage. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and those uses return after a long rest.","Bastion of Law":"At 6th level, you can spend 1 to 5 sorcery points as an action to surround yourself or a visible ally within 30 feet with a protective ward. The ward is made of d8s equal to the points you spent, and the warded creature can spend those dice to reduce incoming damage by the total rolled. The ward lasts until you finish a long rest or create a new one.","Trance of Order":"Starting at 14th level, you can use a bonus action to enter a focused state for 1 minute. While it lasts, attacks against you can't gain advantage, and you can treat any d20 roll of 9 or lower as a 10 on attack rolls, ability checks, and saving throws. You can use the bonus action once per long rest, or spend 5 sorcery points to use it again.","Clockwork Cavalcade":"At 18th level, you can use an action to summon intangible, invulnerable spirits shaped like modrons or constructs into a 30-foot cube originating from you. The spirits restore up to 100 hit points divided among creatures in the cube, instantly repair damaged objects there, and end every spell of 6th level or lower on creatures and objects you choose. You can use this once per long rest, or spend 7 sorcery points to use it again."},
"sorcerer:draconic-bloodline":{"Dragon Ancestor":"At 1st level you pick a dragon type whose damage type (such as fire, cold, or acid) powers your later features. You also learn Draconic, and when a Charisma check involves dragons, your proficiency bonus counts twice.","Draconic Resilience":"Your hit point maximum rises by 1 at 1st level and by 1 more each time you gain a sorcerer level. While you wear no armor, your AC becomes 13 plus your Dexterity modifier, reflecting scales that grow across your skin.","Elemental Affinity":"Starting at 6th level, when a spell you cast deals damage of your ancestor's type, you add your Charisma modifier to one of its damage rolls. You can also spend 1 sorcery point to gain resistance to that damage type for 1 hour.","Dragon Wings":"At 14th level you can sprout draconic wings as a bonus action, gaining a flying speed equal to your walking speed. You dismiss them with another bonus action, and they remain until you do. Armor not built to fit wings blocks manifesting them, and ordinary clothing may tear when they appear.","Draconic Presence":"Starting at 18th level, you can spend 5 sorcery points as an action to project an aura of awe or fear in a 60-foot radius, lasting up to 1 minute while you maintain concentration. Hostile creatures that begin their turn within the aura must make a Wisdom saving throw or become charmed or frightened, depending on your choice. A creature that resists is immune to this aura for 24 hours."},
"sorcerer:divine-soul":{"Divine Magic":"Whenever you gain a new sorcerer spell, you may pick it from the cleric list as well as the sorcerer list, and it becomes a sorcerer spell for you. You also choose a divine affinity (good, evil, law, chaos, or neutrality) that grants one bonus sorcerer spell tied to it, which doesn't count against your spells known. If you later swap that bonus spell, the replacement must come from the cleric list.","Favored by the Gods":"When you fail a saving throw or miss with an attack, you can add 2d4 to the total, which may turn the outcome around. You can do this once, and then you must finish a short or long rest before you can use it again.","Empowered Healing":"Starting at 6th level, when you or an ally within 5 feet rolls dice to restore hit points with a spell, you can spend 1 sorcery point to reroll any number of those dice once, as long as you aren't incapacitated. You can use this only once per turn.","Otherworldly Wings":"Starting at 14th level, a bonus action conjures spectral wings that grant a 30-foot flying speed. The wings stay until you are incapacitated, die, or dismiss them with a bonus action, and their look depends on your divine affinity: eagle wings for good or law, bat wings for evil or chaos, and dragonfly wings for neutrality.","Unearthly Recovery":"At 18th level, when you have fewer than half your hit points, you can use a bonus action to regain hit points equal to half your maximum. You can use this once, then you must finish a long rest to use it again."},
"sorcerer:lunar-sorcery":{"Lunar Embodiment":"After each long rest, you choose a lunar phase (Full Moon, New Moon, or Crescent Moon). While in that phase, you can cast one 1st-level spell from that phase's list without a spell slot, once until your next long rest. You also learn extra lunar spells at sorcerer levels 1, 3, 5, 7, and 9, and these don't count against your sorcerer spells known.","Moon Fire":"Starting at 1st level, you learn the Sacred Flame cantrip, which doesn't count against your cantrips known. When you cast it, you can target one creature normally or hit two creatures within range that are within 5 feet of each other.","Lunar Boons":"Starting at 6th level, when you use Metamagic on a spell from a school tied to your current lunar phase, you can reduce that Metamagic's sorcery point cost by 1, to a minimum of 0. You can use this reduction a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and those uses return when you finish a long rest. Full Moon covers Abjuration and Divination, New Moon covers Enchantment and Necromancy, and Crescent Moon covers Illusion and Transmutation.","Waxing and Waning":"Starting at 6th level, you can spend 1 sorcery point as a bonus action to shift from your current lunar phase to another. You can also cast one 1st-level spell from each lunar phase's list without a spell slot, but only while your current phase matches that spell's phase, and each one returns after a long rest.","Lunar Empowerment":"Starting at 14th level, you gain a benefit tied to whichever phase you are in. In Full Moon, you can use a bonus action to make bright light in a 10-foot radius with 10 more feet of dim light, or extinguish it, and you and chosen creatures gain advantage on Investigation and Perception checks within that bright light. In New Moon, you have advantage on Stealth checks, and attacks against you have disadvantage while you are completely in darkness. In Crescent Moon, you resist necrotic and radiant damage.","Lunar Phenomenon":"At 18th level, you can use a bonus action to tap your current phase's power, or use the bonus action for changing phases to immediately activate the power of the phase you are entering. Full Moon blinds creatures of your choice within 30 feet unless they pass a Constitution save against your spell save DC, and heals one creature in that area for 3d8 hit points. New Moon forces Dexterity saves within 30 feet, dealing 3d10 necrotic damage and reducing speed to 0 on a failure, and makes you invisible until the end of your next turn or until you attack or cast a spell. Crescent Moon teleports you up to 60 feet to a visible unoccupied space, optionally carrying one willing creature within 5 feet, and you both gain resistance to all damage until the start of your next turn. Once used, each power recharges on a long rest, or you can spend 5 sorcery points to use it again."},
"sorcerer:shadow-magic":{"Eyes of the Dark":"You have darkvision out to 120 feet starting at 1st level. At 3rd level you learn the darkness spell for free, without it counting against your known sorcerer spells. You can cast it by spending 2 sorcery points or a spell slot, and if you pay with sorcery points you can still see through the darkness it creates.","Strength of the Grave":"Starting at 1st level, when damage would reduce you to 0 hit points, you can make a Charisma saving throw with a DC of 5 plus the damage taken. A success leaves you at 1 hit point instead of falling unconscious. Radiant damage and critical hits bypass this feature, and after a success you must finish a long rest before using it again.","Hound of Ill Omen":"At 6th level, as a bonus action, you can spend 3 sorcery points to summon a shadowy hound that uses dire wolf statistics but is Medium and a monstrosity. It appears within 30 feet of a creature you can see within 120 feet, gains temporary hit points equal to half your sorcerer level, and can move through creatures and objects as difficult terrain. While it is within 5 feet of its target, that target has disadvantage on saves against your spells, and the hound vanishes when it drops to 0 hit points, its target drops to 0, or 5 minutes pass.","Shadow Walk":"At 14th level, while you stand in dim light or darkness, you can use a bonus action to teleport up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is also dim or dark. This lets you move quickly and unpredictably through areas of shadow.","Umbral Form":"Starting at 18th level, you can spend 6 sorcery points as a bonus action to become a shadowy form for 1 minute. In this form you resist all damage except force and radiant, and you can pass through creatures and objects as difficult terrain, taking 5 force damage if you end your turn inside an object. The form ends early if you are incapacitated, if you die, or if you dismiss it with a bonus action."},
"sorcerer:storm-sorcery":{"Wind Speaker":"Your spellcasting is tied to air magic, which grants you Primordial, the language of elementals, so you can read, write, and speak it. Because of that tongue, you can also communicate with Aquan, Auran, Ignan, and Terran speakers.","Tempestuous Magic":"As a bonus action, just before or after casting a spell of 1st level or higher, you summon swirling air around yourself. This lets you fly up to 10 feet without triggering opportunity attacks.","Heart of the Storm":"Starting at 6th level, you resist lightning and thunder damage. When you begin casting a 1st-level or higher spell that deals lightning or thunder damage, a burst of storm energy strikes creatures you choose within 10 feet, dealing lightning or thunder damage equal to half your sorcerer level to each one.","Storm Guide":"At 6th level, you can subtly manipulate nearby weather. As an action, you can stop rain from falling in a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on you, and you can end that effect as a bonus action.","Storm's Fury":"Starting at 14th level, when a melee attack hits you, you can use your reaction to unleash lightning on the attacker for damage equal to your sorcerer level. The attacker must also succeed on a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC or be pushed in a straight line up to 20 feet away from you.","Wind Soul":"At 18th level, you become immune to lightning and thunder damage and gain a magical flying speed of 60 feet. As an action, you can lower your flying speed to 30 feet for 1 hour and grant that same 30-foot flying speed for 1 hour to a number of creatures within 30 feet equal to 3 plus your Charisma modifier. Once used, you must finish a short or long rest before doing so again."},
"sorcerer:wild-magic":{"Wild Magic Surge":"After casting a sorcerer spell of 1st level or higher, the DM may ask you to roll a d20 once per turn. A natural 1 triggers a random chaotic effect from a surge table. Surge spells ignore Metamagic and skip concentration, so they last their full duration.","Tides of Chaos":"You can grant yourself advantage on one attack roll, ability check, or saving throw, and you need a long rest before using it again. The DM can also force a surge roll after you cast a 1st-level or higher sorcerer spell, which restores this feature immediately.","Bend Luck":"At 6th level, when a creature you can see makes an attack roll, ability check, or saving throw, you can spend your reaction and 2 sorcery points to roll 1d4. You then add or subtract that number from the creature's roll, choosing which, before the outcome takes effect.","Controlled Chaos":"At 14th level, whenever you roll on the Wild Magic Surge table, you roll twice and choose whichever result you prefer.","Spell Bombardment":"At 18th level, when a damage die from your spell comes up at its maximum value, you can reroll one of those maximum dice and add the new result to the damage. You can use this once per turn."},
"sorcerer:pyromancy":{"Heart of Fire":"When you start casting a spell of 1st level or higher that deals fire damage, a burst of flame erupts from you. Creatures you can see within 10 feet that you choose take fire damage equal to half your sorcerer level, with a minimum of 1. The damage grows as your sorcerer level rises.","Fire in the Veins":"At 6th level, you become resistant to fire damage. Your spells also bypass fire resistance in their targets, so resistant foes take full fire damage from them.","Pyromancer's Fury":"Starting at 14th level, when a melee attack hits you, you can spend your reaction to strike back with fire at the attacker. The fire deals damage equal to your sorcerer level and ignores fire resistance.","Fiery Soul":"At 18th level, you become immune to fire damage. Your spells and other effects ignore fire resistance, and they treat fire immunity as if it were only fire resistance."},
"warlock:archfey":{"Fey Presence":"As an action, you radiate a fearsome, beguiling aura over a 10-foot cube from you, forcing each creature inside to make a Wisdom save against your warlock spell save DC. Creatures that fail become charmed or frightened by you (your choice) until the end of your next turn. You can use it once, then must finish a short or long rest to regain it, and its save DC scales with your proficiency bonus as you level.","Misty Escape":"Starting at 6th level, when you take damage you can use your reaction to dissolve into mist, becoming invisible and teleporting up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. The invisibility lasts until the start of your next turn or until you attack or cast a spell. You can use it once per short or long rest.","Beguiling Defenses":"Starting at 10th level, you become immune to being charmed. If another creature tries to charm you, you can use your reaction to turn that charm back on it, forcing a Wisdom save against your spell save DC. On a failure, the creature is charmed by you for 1 minute, or until it takes damage.","Dark Delirium":"Starting at 14th level, as an action you choose a creature you can see within 60 feet and force it to make a Wisdom save against your spell save DC. On a failure, it is charmed or frightened by you (your choice) for 1 minute or until your concentration ends, and it becomes trapped in an illusory misty realm you design, where it can perceive only itself, you, and the illusion. The effect ends early if the creature takes damage, and you must finish a short or long rest before using it again."},
"warlock:celestial":{"Bonus Cantrips":"At 1st level you learn Light and Sacred Flame as extra warlock cantrips. They don't count against your cantrips known, so they add to your options without costing a slot in that total.","Healing Light":"You get a pool of d6s equal to 1 plus your warlock level. As a bonus action, you can spend dice from the pool to heal one visible creature within 60 feet, rolling the spent dice and restoring that total in hit points, up to your Charisma modifier in dice per use (minimum one). The pool refills fully on a long rest, and it grows as your warlock level rises.","Radiant Soul":"Starting at 6th level, you resist radiant damage. Whenever you cast a spell that deals radiant or fire damage, you add your Charisma modifier to one of that spell's radiant or fire damage rolls against a single target. This scales with your Charisma score rather than your level.","Celestial Resilience":"Starting at 10th level, finishing a short or long rest grants you temporary hit points equal to your warlock level plus your Charisma modifier. You can also choose up to five visible creatures at the end of the rest, and each gains temporary hit points equal to half your warlock level plus your Charisma modifier.","Searing Vengeance":"Starting at 14th level, when you would make a death saving throw at the start of your turn, you can instead burst back up with radiant energy, regaining half your maximum hit points and optionally standing. Chosen creatures within 30 feet take 2d8 plus your Charisma modifier in radiant damage and are blinded until the end of the current turn. You can use this once per long rest."},
"warlock:fathomless":{"Tentacle of the Deep":"As a bonus action, you conjure a 10-foot spectral tentacle within 60 feet that lasts up to a minute, and when created it can make a melee spell attack against a creature within 10 feet. A hit deals cold damage (1d8, rising to 2d8 at 10th level) and slows the target by 10 feet until your next turn. Using another bonus action lets you slide it up to 30 feet and attack again. You can summon it a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, with all uses returning after a long rest.","Gift of the Sea":"At 1st level you gain a 40-foot swimming speed and the ability to breathe underwater, letting you operate freely in aquatic environments.","Oceanic Soul":"At 6th level you become resistant to cold damage. While fully submerged, you can understand and be understood by any other fully submerged creature.","Guardian Coil":"Starting at 6th level, your tentacle can shield nearby creatures. When you or a visible creature within 10 feet of the tentacle takes damage, you can use your reaction to reduce that damage by 1d8, increasing to 2d8 at 10th level.","Grasping Tentacles":"At 10th level you learn Evard's Black Tentacles as a warlock spell that doesn't count against your known spells. You can cast it once for free each long rest, and casting it grants temporary hit points equal to your warlock level. While concentrating on it, taking damage cannot end your concentration.","Fathomless Plunge":"At 14th level, as an action, you and up to five willing creatures you can see within 30 feet teleport up to a mile away into a body of water you've seen (pond-sized or larger) or within 30 feet of one. You all reappear in open spaces near each other. You can use this once per short or long rest."},
"warlock:fiend":{"Dark One's Blessing":"Beginning at 1st level, whenever you bring a hostile creature down to 0 hit points, you receive a burst of temporary hit points. The amount equals your Charisma modifier plus your warlock level, with a floor of 1. It triggers on every qualifying kill and does not consume a use.","Dark One's Own Luck":"Starting at 6th level, you can ask your patron to tilt fate, adding a d10 to an ability check or saving throw you make. You decide after seeing the original roll but before its effects resolve. You can use it once, then must finish a short or long rest before using it again.","Fiendish Resilience":"At 10th level, each time you finish a short or long rest, you pick one damage type to resist until your next rest or until you pick a different type. Nonmagical, non-silver weapon damage of that type is reduced, while magical and silver weapon damage gets past this resistance.","Hurl Through Hell":"From 14th level, when a hit lands on a creature, you can banish it into a nightmarish lower plane instead of dealing its normal effect alone. It returns at the end of your next turn to its former space or the closest open one. If it is not a fiend, it suffers 10d10 psychic damage on return. You can use this once, then must complete a long rest to use it again."},
"warlock:the-genie":{"Genie's Vessel":"At 1st level you gain a Tiny magical object that works as your spellcasting focus, either one you pick or one rolled on a d6 table of lamps, urns, bottles, and similar items. Bottled Respite lets you use an action to step inside an extradimensional retreat for up to twice your proficiency bonus in hours, and you can't re-enter until a long rest. Genie's Wrath adds extra damage equal to your proficiency bonus, once per turn on a hit, with a type set by your patron; the vessel's AC equals your spell save DC, its HP equals warlock level plus proficiency bonus, and you can rebuild it through a 1-hour ceremony during a rest.","Elemental Gift":"At 6th level you gain resistance to the damage type tied to your patron's kind. As a bonus action you can grant yourself a 30-foot flying speed lasting 10 minutes, including hovering, and you can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all uses on a long rest.","Sanctuary Vessel":"At 10th level, when you enter your vessel through Bottled Respite, you can pull up to five willing creatures within 30 feet inside with you. You can eject any of them as a bonus action, and anyone who remains inside for 10 minutes gains the benefits of a short rest, with Hit Dice healing boosted by your proficiency bonus.","Limited Wish":"At 14th level, as an action you can speak a request to your vessel to cast a spell of 6th level or lower with a 1-action casting time from any class's list, ignoring its requirements and costly components. Once used, it stays unavailable until you finish 1d4 long rests."},
"warlock:great-old-one":{"Awakened Mind":"From 1st level, you can send thoughts directly into the minds of visible creatures within 30 feet, bypassing spoken language. The target only needs to understand at least one language to receive your message, so a shared tongue isn't necessary.","Entropic Ward":"Starting at 6th level, you can spend your reaction when a creature attacks you to force that attack roll to be made at disadvantage. If the attack misses, your next strike against that creature gains advantage when made before the end of your following turn. You can use this once, then must finish a short or long rest before using it again.","Thought Shield":"Beginning at 10th level, you become effectively unreadable to telepathy and similar mental probing unless you choose to let someone in. You gain resistance to psychic damage, and any creature that harms you with psychic damage suffers an equal amount of psychic damage in return.","Create Thrall":"At 14th level, you can use your action to touch an incapacitated humanoid and bind its mind to your patron's alien influence, leaving it charmed by you. The charm lasts until a Remove Curse spell is cast on the creature, the charmed condition is otherwise removed, or you invoke this feature again. While the thrall shares your plane of existence, you can communicate with it telepathically."},
"warlock:hexblade":{"Hexblade's Curse":"As a bonus action, you mark a creature you can see within 30 feet for 1 minute. While it is marked, your hits deal extra damage equal to your proficiency bonus, and your attacks against it score critical hits on a 19 or 20. If the marked creature dies, you regain hit points equal to your warlock level plus your Charisma modifier (at least 1), and you can use this once per short or long rest. Master of Hexes later lets the mark jump to a new target.","Hex Warrior":"You gain proficiency with medium armor, shields, and martial weapons. After each long rest, you can bond with one weapon you know how to use that lacks the two-handed property, and until your next long rest you use your Charisma modifier instead of Strength or Dexterity for its attack and damage rolls. If you later gain Pact of the Blade, this Charisma-based bonus applies to every pact weapon you summon, regardless of weapon type.","Accursed Specter":"Starting at 6th level, when you slay a humanoid, you can bind its spirit to you as a specter that uses the Monster Manual statistics. The specter appears with temporary hit points equal to half your warlock level, gets its own initiative, and follows your spoken commands. It adds your Charisma modifier (minimum +0) to its attack rolls, and it serves you until the end of your next long rest, which you can use once per long rest.","Armor of Hexes":"At 10th level, when the creature under your Hexblade's Curse attacks you, you can use your reaction to roll a d6. On a roll of 4 or higher, that attack misses you no matter what the attack roll was. This makes the curse a real defensive tool against its target.","Master of Hexes":"Starting at 14th level, when a creature under your Hexblade's Curse dies, you can transfer the curse to another creature you can see within 30 feet, as long as you are not incapacitated. Moving the curse this way means you do not gain the hit point healing that normally comes from the earlier target's death."},
"warlock:undead":{"Form of Dread":"As a bonus action, you take on a dreadful aspect for 1 minute, gaining temporary hit points equal to 1d10 plus your warlock level. Once per turn, a hit can force the target to pass a Wisdom save or be frightened of you until the end of your next turn, and you are immune to being frightened yourself. You can use it a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and uses return on a long rest.","Grave Touched":"At 6th level, your patron's power sustains you, so you no longer need food, drink, or air. Once per turn, when you hit with an attack and roll damage, you can change that damage to necrotic. While transformed with Form of Dread, you roll one extra damage die for that necrotic damage.","Necrotic Husk":"At 10th level, you gain resistance to necrotic damage, which becomes full immunity while you are transformed with Form of Dread. When you would drop to 0 hit points, you can instead use your reaction to fall to 1 hit point and release a burst of death energy. Creatures you choose within 30 feet take 2d10 plus your warlock level in necrotic damage, and you gain one level of exhaustion; this reaction returns after 1d4 long rests.","Spirit Projection":"At 14th level, as an action, you can send your spirit out of your body for up to 1 hour, ending early if your concentration breaks, while your unconscious body stays in suspended animation. While projecting, your spirit and body both resist bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage, and your conjuration or necromancy spells drop verbal, somatic, and non-gold material components. Your spirit flies at your walking speed and can pass through creatures and objects, but takes 1d10 force damage if it ends a turn inside one, and while transformed with Form of Dread, dealing necrotic damage restores hit points equal to half that amount once per turn. You can use this projection once per long rest."},
"warlock:undying":{"Among the Dead":"Starting at 1st level, you learn the Spare the Dying cantrip as a warlock cantrip and gain advantage on saves against disease. Undead find it hard to hurt you: when one targets you directly with an attack or harmful spell, it must pass a Wisdom save against your spell save DC or switch to another target. Passing the save makes it immune to this for 24 hours, and so does you targeting it with an attack or harmful spell. Area effects that include you still catch you.","Defy Death":"Beginning at 6th level, you draw vitality from cheating death, whether for yourself or someone you help. When you succeed on a death saving throw or stabilize a creature with Spare the Dying, you regain 1d8 plus your Constitution modifier in hit points, with a minimum of 1. You can use this once, and you recover the ability after finishing a long rest.","Undying Nature":"At 10th level, you can hold your breath indefinitely and no longer need food, water, or sleep, though you still need rest to lower exhaustion and to gain the benefits of short and long rests. You also age far more slowly, with only 1 year passing on your body for every 10 real years. You are immune to magical aging.","Indestructible Life":"At 14th level, you tap into the deepest secrets of the Undying. As a bonus action on your turn, you regain hit points equal to 1d8 plus your warlock level. When you use this, you can also reattach a severed body part of yours to its place. You can use this once, and you regain the use after a short or long rest."},
"wizard:abjuration":{"Abjuration Savant":"Choosing this school at 2nd level halves the gold and time needed to copy abjuration spells into your spellbook. It makes building an abjuration collection cheaper and quicker, with no effect on other schools.","Arcane Ward":"Starting at 2nd level, casting an abjuration spell of 1st level or higher also conjures a protective ward on you with hit points equal to twice your wizard level plus your Intelligence modifier. The ward absorbs damage aimed at you, and any excess passes through to you once it's depleted. Each abjuration spell you cast restores twice that spell's level in ward hit points, and you can create a new ward only after a long rest.","Projected Ward":"At 6th level, you can use your reaction to have your Arcane Ward absorb damage dealt to a creature you can see within 30 feet. If that damage empties the ward, the protected creature takes whatever damage is left over. This extends your protection to allies, though it's limited by your reaction each round.","Improved Abjuration":"At 10th level, you add your proficiency bonus to ability checks you make while casting abjuration spells, such as Counterspell and Dispel Magic. This makes dispelling and countering magic far more reliable.","Spell Resistance":"Starting at 14th level, you gain advantage on saving throws against spells and resistance to spell damage. Together these make you very hard to overcome with magical effects, serving as a strong defensive capstone."},
"wizard:bladesinging":{"Training in War and Song":"At 2nd level you become trained with light armor and with one one-handed melee weapon of your choice, and you also gain Performance proficiency if you lack it. These proficiencies broaden your combat options and your artistic skills at the same time.","Bladesong":"Starting at 2nd level, while you wear no medium or heavy armor and carry no shield, you can use a bonus action to invoke a one-minute elven enchantment that boosts your speed, agility, and focus. It ends early if you are incapacitated, equip medium or heavy armor or a shield, or attack with a two-handed weapon, and you can dismiss it freely at any time. While active, your AC rises by your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1), your walking speed gains 10 feet, you have advantage on Acrobatics checks, and your concentration saves get a bonus equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1). You can use it a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and all uses return after a long rest.","Extra Attack":"Beginning at 6th level, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn, you can make two attacks instead of one. You may also replace one of those attacks with the casting of a cantrip.","Song of Defense":"Starting at 10th level, while your Bladesong is active, you can turn incoming harm into magical absorption. When you take damage, you can use your reaction to expend a spell slot and reduce that damage by five times the slot's level.","Song of Victory":"At 14th level, while your Bladesong is active, you add your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1) to the damage of your melee weapon attacks. This makes your blade a far more punishing force in sustained combat."},
"wizard:chronurgy":{"Chronal Shift":"At 2nd level, you can use a reaction after you or a creature within 30 feet makes an attack roll, ability check, or saving throw to force a reroll, deciding only after seeing the outcome. The target must keep the new result. You can do this twice, and both uses return after a long rest.","Temporal Awareness":"Starting at 2nd level, you add your Intelligence modifier to your initiative rolls. This gives you a steady boost to acting early in combat and works every time you roll initiative.","Momentary Stasis":"At 6th level, you can use an action to target a Large or smaller creature you can see within 60 feet, forcing a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the creature is encased in magical energy, becoming incapacitated with a speed of 0 until the end of your next turn or until it takes damage. You can use this a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum once), and all uses return after a long rest.","Arcane Abeyance":"At 10th level, when you cast a spell using a slot of 4th level or lower, you can instead lock the spell into a Tiny gray bead that lasts 1 hour, with AC 15, 1 hit point, and immunity to poison and psychic damage. A creature holding the bead can use its action to release the stored spell, which then uses your spell attack bonus and save DC, and the releaser counts as the caster. You can create one bead per short or long rest.","Convergent Future":"Starting at 14th level, when you or a creature you can see within 60 feet makes an attack roll, ability check, or saving throw, you can use your reaction to bypass the roll and set the result to the minimum needed to succeed or one less, your choice. Using this gives you one level of exhaustion, which only a long rest can remove."},
"wizard:conjuration":{"Conjuration Savant":"Starting at 2nd level, you spend only half the gold and time normally required to copy a Conjuration spell into your spellbook. This makes learning new conjuration magic considerably cheaper and faster.","Minor Conjuration":"Starting at 2nd level, you can use your action to create a small, nonmagical-looking inanimate object you have seen before, either in your hand or in an unoccupied space you can see within 10 feet. The object can be up to 3 feet on a side and 10 pounds, and it sheds dim light in a 5-foot radius. It vanishes after 1 hour, when you use this feature again, or once it takes or deals any damage.","Benign Transposition":"Starting at 6th level, you can use your action to teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see, or swap places with a willing Small or Medium creature within that range. You can use this once, then must finish a long rest or cast a conjuration spell of 1st level or higher to use it again.","Focused Conjuration":"Starting at 10th level, taking damage will not break your concentration on a conjuration spell. This keeps your summons, fog clouds, and similar effects active during combat.","Durable Summons":"Starting at 14th level, any creature you summon or create with a conjuration spell gains 30 temporary hit points. This gives your conjured allies a sturdy buffer that helps them survive longer in battle."},
"wizard:divination":{"Divination Savant":"Starting at 2nd level, you pay only half the usual gold and time to copy a Divination spell into your spellbook. This makes growing a divination library cheaper and faster throughout your career. It is a constant benefit rather than something you spend on a rest.","Portent":"Starting at 2nd level, after each long rest you roll two d20s and record the results. Once per turn, before the roll, you can swap an attack roll, saving throw, or ability check made by you or a creature you can see for one of those stored numbers. Each stored roll works only once, and any unused rolls disappear when you next finish a long rest. At 14th level you gain a third roll.","Expert Divination":"Starting at 6th level, when you cast a divination spell of 2nd level or higher using a spell slot, you regain one expended slot. The recovered slot must be lower than the spell's level and no higher than 5th level. This effectively makes your divination casting far less costly over the course of a day.","The Third Eye":"Starting at 10th level, you can use your action to enhance your perception with one of four options: darkvision out to 60 feet, seeing into the Ethereal Plane within 60 feet, reading any language, or seeing invisible creatures and objects within 10 feet in line of sight. The chosen benefit lasts until you are incapacitated or finish a short or long rest. You can use this feature again only after a short or long rest.","Greater Portent":"Starting at 14th level, your dreams paint a sharper picture of what is coming, so you roll three d20s for Portent after each long rest instead of two. This gives you more foretelling rolls to swap in during your adventures."},
"wizard:enchantment":{"Enchantment Savant":"Starting at 2nd level, you pay only half the gold and half the time when copying an enchantment spell into your spellbook. This makes building a collection of charm and compulsion magic much cheaper and quicker for you.","Hypnotic Gaze":"Starting at 2nd level, use your action to target a creature within 5 feet that can see or hear you. It must make a Wisdom save against your wizard spell save DC or become charmed until the end of your next turn, with its speed dropped to 0 and it left incapacitated and dazed. You can spend your action on later turns to extend the charm to the end of your next turn, but it breaks if you move more than 5 feet away, the target can no longer perceive you, or the target takes damage. Once the effect ends or the target resists it, you can't target that creature with this again until you finish a long rest.","Instinctive Charm":"Starting at 6th level, when a creature you can see within 30 feet makes an attack roll against you and another creature is within that attack's range, you can use your reaction to redirect the attack. The attacker makes a Wisdom save against your spell save DC, and on a failure it must target the creature nearest to it other than you or itself, with the attacker choosing if several are tied. If the attacker succeeds, you can't use this on it again until a long rest, and you must decide before knowing whether the attack hits. Creatures immune to being charmed are unaffected.","Split Enchantment":"Starting at 10th level, when you cast an enchantment spell of 1st level or higher that normally affects only one creature, you can choose a second creature to be affected by it as well. This lets you double the reach of your single-target charms and compulsions without spending extra resources.","Alter Memories":"At 14th level, when you cast an enchantment spell to charm one or more creatures, you can keep one of them from realizing it was charmed. Once before that spell ends, you can use your action to force a creature to make an Intelligence save against your spell save DC, and on a failure it loses 1 + your Charisma modifier in hours of memory (minimum 1). You may choose to erase less time, but never more than the spell's duration."},
"wizard:evocation":{"Evocation Savant":"Starting at 2nd level, you pay only half the gold and time normally needed to copy an evocation spell into your spellbook. This discount applies every time you add one of these spells to your book.","Sculpt Spells":"From 2nd level, when your evocation spell forces visible creatures to make saves, you can shield up to 1 plus the spell's level of them. Those chosen creatures succeed automatically and take no damage from half-damage saves, which makes the number of protected allies grow with the spell's level.","Potent Cantrip":"Beginning at 6th level, creatures that resist your damaging cantrip with a successful save still take half its damage. They avoid only the cantrip's additional effects.","Empowered Evocation":"At 10th level, you add your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1) to one damage roll of any wizard evocation spell you cast. This adds a reliable damage boost to your evocation spells.","Overchannel":"Starting at 14th level, a damaging wizard spell of 1st through 5th level can deal maximum damage instead of rolled damage. Your first use carries no penalty, but each further use before a long rest deals necrotic damage to you equal to 2d12 per spell level, and that cost rises by 1d12 per spell level with each extra use. This necrotic damage ignores resistance and immunity."},
"wizard:graviturgy":{"Adjust Density":"As an action at 2nd level, you change the weight of an object or creature you can see within 30 feet, provided it is Large or smaller. Halving it grants speed and jump bonuses but imposes disadvantage on Strength rolls, while doubling it slows the target but grants advantage on Strength rolls, lasting up to 1 minute or until your concentration ends. At 10th level, the maximum size rises to Huge or smaller.","Gravity Well":"Starting at 6th level, whenever you cast a spell on a creature that is willing, is hit by the spell's attack, or fails its saving throw, you can push that creature 5 feet into an unoccupied space you choose. This lets you reposition foes or allies as part of your spellcasting.","Violent Attraction":"At 10th level, you can use your reaction when a creature you can see within 60 feet lands a weapon attack, adding 1d10 extra damage of the weapon's type to the target. Alternatively, you can use the same reaction to add 2d10 damage when a creature within 60 feet takes falling damage. You can use this a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum once), and you regain all uses after a long rest.","Event Horizon":"At 14th level, you can take an action to project a 30-foot field of gravity for up to 1 minute or until your concentration ends. Each hostile creature that starts its turn in the field must make a Strength save against your spell save DC, taking 2d10 force damage and having its speed reduced to 0 until the start of its next turn on a failure. A success halves the damage and makes each foot of movement cost 2 extra feet that turn. You can use it once per long rest, or again by expending a spell slot of 3rd level or higher."},
"wizard:illusion":{"Illusion Savant":"Starting at 2nd level, copying an Illusion spell into your spellbook costs half the gold and half the time it normally would. This makes building an illusion-focused spellbook noticeably cheaper and faster.","Improved Minor Illusion":"At 2nd level you learn Minor Illusion, or another wizard cantrip if you already know it, and this cantrip doesn't count against your cantrips known. When you cast Minor Illusion, you can produce a sound and an image together in a single casting.","Malleable Illusions":"From 6th level, when you cast an illusion spell lasting at least 1 minute, you can spend your action to reshape that illusion using the spell's normal rules, as long as you can see it. This lets you adapt an ongoing illusion to changing situations.","Illusory Self":"Beginning at 10th level, you can use your reaction when a creature attacks you to slip in an illusory double, causing that attack to automatically miss, after which the duplicate vanishes. You can use this once, and then you must finish a short or long rest before using it again.","Illusory Reality":"At 14th level, when you cast an illusion spell of 1st level or higher, you can make one nonmagical, inanimate object within the illusion physically real. You do this as a bonus action while the spell lasts, and the object stays real for 1 minute, such as a bridge that allies can cross. The object cannot deal damage or directly harm anyone."},
"wizard:necromancy":{"Necromancy Savant":"Starting at 2nd level, copying a Necromancy spell into your spellbook costs only half the gold and half the time it normally would require.","Grim Harvest":"From 2nd level, when a spell of 1st level or higher kills at least one creature, you regain hit points once per turn. The amount is twice the spell's level, or three times that for Necromancy spells, and constructs and undead don't trigger it.","Undead Thralls":"At 6th level you learn Animate Dead if you don't already know it, and each casting can animate one extra corpse or pile of bones. Undead you create with necromancy spells gain maximum hit points equal to your wizard level and add your proficiency bonus to their weapon damage.","Inured to Undeath":"At 10th level you gain resistance to necrotic damage, and effects can't lower your maximum hit points. This reflects your long experience with undead and the draining forces they wield.","Command Undead":"From 14th level, as an action you can attempt to seize control of one undead you can see within 60 feet, forcing a Charisma save against your spell save DC. On a success, you can't try this on that creature again, but on a failure it becomes friendly and obeys you until you use this feature again. Intelligent undead with Intelligence 8 or higher roll with advantage, and those with Intelligence 12 or higher can retry the save every hour after failing until they break free."},
"wizard:order-of-scribes":{"Wizardly Quill":"At 2nd level, you can conjure a Tiny magic quill as a bonus action that writes in any ink color you pick, needing no ink. Copying a spell with it takes just 2 minutes per spell level, and a bonus-action wave erases its writing within 5 feet. Creating a new quill or dying makes the current one vanish.","Awakened Spellbook":"At 2nd level, while holding your spellbook, you can use it as a spellcasting focus for wizard spells. You can also swap a spell's damage type for one found in another spell of the same level as the slot used, for that casting only, and cast a ritual using its normal casting time once per long rest. During a short rest, you can transfer the book's mind and spells into a new book by inscribing sigils with your quill.","Manifest Mind":"At 6th level, you can use a bonus action to make your spellbook's mind appear as a Tiny intangible spectral form within 60 feet, which sheds dim light and has 60-foot darkvision. You can cast wizard spells from its position, using its senses, a number of times per day equal to your proficiency bonus, and you can move it 30 feet as a bonus action. It regains uses on a long rest and can be recalled again by spending any spell slot.","Master Scrivener":"At 10th level, after each long rest, you can copy a 1st or 2nd-level spell with a 1-action casting time from your spellbook onto a scroll using your quill, and the spell is treated as one level higher. You read the scroll to cast the spell as an action, and it disappears once cast or after your next long rest. Crafting ordinary spell scrolls also costs half the gold and time when you use the quill.","One with the Word":"At 14th level, you gain advantage on Intelligence (Arcana) checks while carrying your spellbook. Once per long rest, when you take damage while the mind is manifested, you can use your reaction to dismiss it and negate that damage, then roll 3d6 and lose spells from the book totaling at least that spell level. Those spells can't be cast for 1d6 long rests, and if the book lacks enough spells, you fall to 0 hit points."},
"wizard:transmutation":{"Transmutation Savant":"Starting at 2nd level, copying a Transmutation spell into your spellbook costs only half the usual gold and time. This makes expanding your transmutation library far cheaper and quicker. It works passively, so it never costs a use or a spell slot.","Minor Alchemy":"From 2nd level, you can temporarily turn one nonmagical object made of wood, stone (not gemstone), iron, copper, or silver into another of those materials. Each 10 minutes of work converts up to 1 cubic foot, and the change lasts 1 hour or until you lose concentration, then reverts. It's useful for quick field fixes or cheap shortcuts in crafting.","Transmuter's Stone":"At 6th level, spending 8 hours crafting a stone stores transmutation magic that grants a benefit to whoever carries it, which can be you or another creature. You pick the benefit at creation from darkvision out to 60 feet, a 10-foot speed boost while unencumbered, Constitution saving throw proficiency, or resistance to acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage. While you carry the stone, casting a transmutation spell of 1st level or higher lets you adjust its effect, and making a new stone disables the old one.","Shapechanger":"At 10th level, Polymorph joins your spellbook if it isn't there already. You can cast it on yourself without a spell slot, turning into a beast with a challenge rating of 1 or lower, and this free use recharges after a short or long rest. You can still cast it normally using a spell slot whenever you have one available.","Master Transmuter":"At 14th level, you can use your action to unleash the stored magic of your transmuter's stone, choosing one burst effect, which destroys the stone until you finish a long rest. Major Transformation converts a nonmagical object up to a 5-foot cube into another of similar size and mass, with equal or lesser value, after 10 minutes of handling. Panacea removes curses, diseases, and poisons from a touched creature and restores all its hit points, while Restore Life casts Raise Dead on a touched creature without a spell slot, and Restore Youth takes 3d10 years off a willing creature's apparent age, to a minimum of 13."},
"wizard:war-magic":{"Arcane Deflection":"Starting at 2nd level, you can spend your reaction when an attack hits you or you fail a saving throw to boost your defense: +2 AC against that attack or +4 to that save. Using it prevents you from casting leveled spells until the end of your next turn, though cantrips remain available. At 14th level, Deflecting Shroud adds a damaging effect to this feature.","Tactical Wit":"At 2nd level, you can add your Intelligence modifier to your initiative rolls, helping you act early in combat. The bonus scales with your Intelligence score, so investing in that ability boosts it.","Power Surge":"At 6th level, you can store magical energy in yourself as power surges, up to your Intelligence modifier (minimum one). You regain one surge when you finish a long rest, and gain one when you end a spell with Dispel Magic or Counterspell or end a short rest with none stored. Once per turn, when a wizard spell damages a creature or object, you can spend a surge to add force damage equal to half your wizard level.","Durable Magic":"Beginning at 10th level, you gain a +2 bonus to AC and to all saving throws while you maintain concentration on a spell. This makes concentration-based spells much safer to sustain in combat.","Deflecting Shroud":"At 14th level, your Arcane Deflection becomes infused with deadly magic. Whenever you use that feature, magical energy arcs out to up to three creatures of your choice within 60 feet, each taking force damage equal to half your wizard level."},
"blood-hunter:ghostslayer":{"Rite of the Dawn":"At 3rd level, your Crimson Rite gains this rite, and its extra damage becomes radiant. While it is active, your weapon glows with light in a 20-foot radius, you resist necrotic damage, and hits against undead roll an extra hemocraft die for the rite's extra damage.","Curse Specialist":"Starting at 3rd level, you gain one additional use of Blood Maledict. Your blood curses can also affect creatures that have no blood, such as constructs and undead.","Ethereal Step":"At 7th level, you can start your turn by stepping into the Ethereal Plane if you are not incapacitated. You can pass through creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain and can see and affect things on the Ethereal Plane, lasting a number of rounds equal to your Hemocraft modifier (minimum 1). Ending your turn inside an object deals 1d10 force damage, and if you are still inside when the effect ends, you are pushed to the nearest open space and take force damage equal to twice the distance you moved; you can use it once per rest, or twice per rest from 15th level.","Brand of Sundering":"At 11th level, creatures branded by your Brand of Castigation become more exposed to your Crimson Rite, so hits with an active rite roll an additional hemocraft die for its extra damage. A branded creature with Incorporeal Movement or a similar trait also cannot move through other creatures or objects while branded.","Blood Curse of the Exorcist":"At 15th level, you gain this blood curse as an option for your Blood Maledict, and it does not count against the number of curses you know. It is designed to purge corruption from your allies while punishing whoever caused it.","Rite Revival":"At 18th level, if you have one or more crimson rites active and are reduced to 0 hit points without dying outright, you can end all of those rites to drop to 1 hit point instead."},
"blood-hunter:lycan":{"Heightened Senses":"At 3rd level, your hearing and sense of smell sharpen to a predator's level, giving you advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that depend on those senses.","Hybrid Transformation":"Starting at 3rd level, a bonus action shifts you into a hybrid beast form that lasts up to an hour, and you can still talk, use gear, and wear armor. You can end it as a bonus action, and falling unconscious or dying also ends it. After each use you must take a short or long rest before using it again. While transformed, your Strength checks and saves gain advantage, your melee damage rises by +1 (+2 at 11th, +3 at 18th), and nonmagical physical damage not from silvered weapons is resisted. You also gain +1 AC without heavy armor, and your unarmed strikes use Dexterity for 1d6 damage (1d8 at 11th) with an extra unarmed strike as a bonus action after Attack. Finally, dropping below half HP can force a frenzied bloodlust attack that requires a DC 8 Wisdom save at the start of your turn.","Stalker's Prowess":"At 7th level, your speed increases by 10 feet, your long jump gains 10 feet, and your high jump gains 3 feet. In hybrid form, your unarmed strikes gain a +1 attack bonus that grows to +2 at 11th and +3 at 18th. If a crimson rite is active on your unarmed strikes in that form, they count as magical for overcoming resistance and immunity to nonmagical attacks.","Advanced Transformation":"At 11th level, you can use Hybrid Transformation twice before needing to rest, and a short or long rest restores both uses. Your hybrid form also gains Lycan Regeneration, which heals you at the start of your turn when you are above 0 but below half your maximum HP, for 1 plus your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). In hybrid form, this healing happens before your bloodlust saving throw.","Brand of the Voracious":"Starting at 15th level, you have advantage on bloodlust saving throws while in hybrid form. Your Brand of Castigation can also bind a foe to your hunter's ferocity, and in hybrid form you have advantage on attack rolls against a branded creature.","Hybrid Transformation Mastery":"At 18th level, you can activate Hybrid Transformation as many times as you choose, without waiting for a rest between uses. Your hybrid form now lasts until you revert on your own, fall unconscious, or die, instead of ending after an hour. You also gain the Blood Curse of the Howl for your Blood Maledict feature, which does not count against the number of blood curses you know."},
"blood-hunter:mutant":{"Mutagencraft":"Taken at 3rd level, this lets you brew volatile alchemical mutagens that briefly boost your mind or body. Drinking one is a bonus action, and its effects last until a short or long rest ends, though an action can purge all active mutagens early. You brew 1 mutagen per rest at 3rd level, rising to 2 at 7th, 2 at 11th, and 3 at 15th and 18th, and your known formulas grow from 4 to 8. Unused mutagens go inert when your next rest ends.","Strange Metabolism":"At 7th level, your body resists toxins, so you become immune to poison damage and the poisoned condition. You can also spend a bonus action to suppress the drawback of one active mutagen for 1 minute. Once you use that burst, you must finish a long rest before doing it again.","Brand of Axiom":"At 11th level, your Brand of Castigation exposes a branded foe's disguises, so any illusion or invisibility on it ends and it cannot gain those benefits while branded. A branded creature in an alternate form must succeed on a Wisdom save or revert to its true form and be stunned until the end of your next turn. The same save, with the same stun, is needed to stop it from changing shape.","Blood Curse of Corrosion":"Starting at 15th level, your Blood Maledict can use a toxic curse that poisons a creature's body. This curse is added to your options without counting against the number of blood curses you know.","Exalted Mutation":"At 18th level, you can use a bonus action to end the effects of one active mutagen and immediately start a different mutagen you know in its place. You can do this a number of times equal to your Hemocraft modifier, with a minimum of one, and all uses return when you finish a long rest."},
"blood-hunter:profane-soul":{"Otherworldly Patron":"At 3rd level you choose a patron from several options, and that choice shapes several of your subclass features later on. The patron acts as a thematic bargain that determines which specific bonuses you gain from Rite Focus and Revealed Arcana.","Pact Magic":"At 3rd level you learn two warlock cantrips, gaining a third at 10th level. Your spell slots are all the same level, rise in level as you advance, and refresh on a short or long rest, and you use your Hemocraft ability for spellcasting, with a save DC of 8 + proficiency bonus + Hemocraft modifier. You also know a set number of 1st-level-or-higher warlock spells that grows with your level, and you can swap one known spell whenever you gain a level.","Rite Focus":"Starting at 3rd level, while you have an active crimson rite, your weapon serves as a spellcasting focus and grants a benefit tied to your patron. Examples include forcing a struck creature to shed cover or invisibility, healing an ally by spending a Blood Maledict use, gaining a temporary flying speed, or frightening nearby foes after a critical hit. Several benefits scale with your Hemocraft die or modifier.","Mystic Frenzy":"Beginning at 7th level, casting a cantrip with your action lets you immediately make one weapon attack as a bonus action. This lets you pair spellcasting with melee strikes in the same turn.","Revealed Arcana":"At 7th level your patron grants one signature spell, which you can cast using any pact magic slot. Once you cast it, you cannot cast it again until you finish a long rest, and the specific spell depends on your patron.","Brand of the Sapping Scar":"At 11th level, creatures branded by your Brand of Castigation become marked by dark arcane scars. Those branded creatures make their saving throws against your warlock spells at disadvantage.","Unsealed Arcana":"At 15th level your patron grants a second signature spell that you can cast without spending a spell slot. Like your earlier patron spell, you regain the ability to cast it after completing a long rest, and the spell offered depends on your patron.","Blood Curse of the Souleater":"Starting at 18th level, you gain the Soul Eater blood curse as an option for your Blood Maledict feature, which lets you siphon life energy from fallen foes. This curse does not count against the number of blood curses you know."}};
